insert into public.academy_trades (slug, name, family, icon, intro, seo_title, seo_description, sales_challenge, sort_order) values
  ('roofing', 'Roofing', 'Exterior', 'House', 'Running a roofing business means pricing tear-off, underlayment, flashing, and ventilation by the square while keeping crews, dumpsters, and weather windows on track. This classroom covers the estimating, sales, and safety habits that turn roofing bids into well-run, profitable jobs.', 'Roofing Business Courses for Contractors', 'Roofing business courses on estimating squares, homeowner questions, weather scheduling, job costing and fall safety for small roofers.', 'Homeowners ask whether insurance will cover the work, what their deductible is, and whether the roof really needs replacing when it looks fine from the street. Bring photos and a written condition summary so you can answer those questions with facts.', 0),
  ('siding', 'Siding', 'Exterior', 'PanelsTopLeft', 'Siding businesses estimate removal, house wrap, panels, trim, and accessories in the units suppliers use, then turn them into a package the homeowner can compare. This classroom covers the field and office habits that keep siding bids accurate and jobs weathertight.', 'Siding Contractor Business Courses', 'Courses for siding contractors on estimating squares and trim, sequencing crews around weather, selling package prices and handling storm-repair work.', 'Homeowners compare siding bids by price per square and often cannot see why trim, wrap, and disposal cost what they do. Show the full package with clear line items so the comparison is between equal scopes.', 10),
  ('decks', 'Decks & Porches', 'Structures', 'Fence', 'Decks and porches break into footings, framing, decking, stairs, and railings, and each one has its own materials, inspections, and hardware. This classroom covers running a structure business that keeps permits and connectors accounted for while the homeowner sees clear package prices.', 'Deck and Porch Business Courses for Contractors', 'Deck and porch courses on footing layout, framing, decking choices, railings, permits, job costing and repeat maintenance work for small contractors.', 'Homeowners often compare pressure-treated and composite decks on sticker price alone, and some want a number before the design is settled. Walk them through maintenance, lifespan, and railing choices in writing so the decision rests on the same facts.', 20),
  ('concrete', 'Concrete', 'Sitework', 'Layers', 'Concrete work runs on excavation, base material, forms, reinforcement, and finishing, all measured in cubic yards and square feet with weather and cure time shaping every day. This classroom covers the bidding, crew, and cash habits that keep flatwork and structural pours profitable.', 'Concrete Contractor Business Courses', 'Concrete courses on yardage estimating, form and finish labor, pour-day scheduling, job costing and jobsite safety for small flatwork crews.', 'Customers often ask for a lower bid from a competitor who is cutting base depth, reinforcement, or finish quality without saying so. Compare scopes line by line and explain what a lower number leaves out.', 30),
  ('kitchens', 'Kitchens', 'Interior', 'CookingPot', 'Kitchen projects combine cabinetry, countertops, plumbing, electrical, flooring, and finishes, and each scope has its own trade and inspection timing. This classroom covers organizing a kitchen job into clear sections so the homeowner sees one confident number and understands what it includes.', 'Kitchen Remodeling Business Courses', 'Kitchen remodeling courses on layout planning, cabinet and counter scope, trade coordination, pricing, job costing and crew training.', 'Homeowners often fall in love with a design and then react to the total, asking what can be cut or why plumbing and electrical add so much. Present the design in phases with scope sections so the homeowner can decide what to change.', 40),
  ('bathrooms', 'Bathrooms', 'Interior', 'Bath', 'Bathroom remodels bring demolition, waterproofing, tile, fixtures, vanities, and finish work into a small space with tight sequencing and many inspections. This classroom covers running that work in clear sections so the homeowner knows exactly what is included and what it costs.', 'Bathroom Remodeling Business Courses', 'Bath remodeling courses on waterproofing, tub-to-shower conversions, tile and fixture scope, pricing, trade sequencing and repeat work.', 'Homeowners often expect a tub-to-shower conversion or full bath to cost what a big-box kit suggests, and they do not see the waterproofing, plumbing moves, or blocking behind the finished wall. Show what sits behind the tile so the price matches the work.', 50),
  ('interior-remodeling', 'Interior Remodeling', 'Interior', 'Sofa', 'Interior remodels combine framing changes, drywall, trim, flooring, and paint in one job, often across several rooms or floors. This classroom covers organizing those phases into an estimate the homeowner can follow, whether it is grouped by phase or by room.', 'Interior Remodeling Business Courses', 'Interior remodeling courses on phased estimates, wall opening scope, trade sequencing, change orders, job costing and crew training.', 'Homeowners often want a whole-floor refresh for a number they picked out of the air, and they resist change orders when a wall turns out to hide wiring or ductwork. Set the scope and allowances in writing before the first wall comes down.', 60),
  ('exterior-remodeling', 'Exterior Remodeling', 'Exterior', 'Trees', 'Exterior remodels often bundle siding, trim, windows, doors, gutters, and paint into one property-wide job that touches several trades. This classroom covers organizing that work into one estimate with clear sections, so the homeowner sees how each piece affects the look and the price.', 'Exterior Remodeling Business Courses', 'Exterior remodeling courses for contractors on combined estimates, curb-appeal packages, rot repair, trade coordination, pricing and repeat exterior work.', 'Homeowners often want the whole front elevation updated but fund it one piece at a time, and they ask which item to do first. Lay out the exterior in phases with the reasons for each order so the choice is informed.', 70),
  ('drywall', 'Drywall', 'Interior', 'Square', 'Drywall work tracks sheets, joint compound, tape, corner bead, and labor by square foot, with finish levels that the homeowner needs to understand. This classroom covers running a drywall business from hanging and taping through finishing, with estimates and crew habits that hold up on every job.', 'Drywall Contractor Business Courses', 'Drywall contractor courses on sheet and finish-level estimating, crew sequencing, fire-rated assemblies, job costing, repair work and jobsite safety.', 'Homeowners often do not know what a Level 5 finish is, and they expect a smooth wall at a Level 2 price. Show finish levels with photos and write them into the proposal so there is no surprise at the final walk.', 80),
  ('painting', 'Painting', 'Interior', 'Paintbrush', 'Painting businesses organize prep, masking, primer, paint, and labor so customers can see what a professional finish requires. This classroom covers building a painting business around prep quality, color selection, and the scheduling that keeps rooms and exteriors moving.', 'Painting Contractor Business Courses', 'Painting contractor courses on prep-based estimates, interior and exterior bids, cabinet painting, crew scheduling and job costing.', 'Customers often compare a painter''s bid to a neighbor''s quote for the same rooms and assume the lower price includes the same prep. Explain what the prep, primer, and number of coats add, so the difference is visible.', 90),
  ('electrical', 'Electrical', 'Systems', 'Zap', 'Electrical businesses track wire, devices, fixtures, panel work, labor, permits, and testing, and much of that work sits behind walls where mistakes are expensive. This classroom covers the licensing, estimating, and jobsite habits that keep electrical proposals clear and jobs safe to energize.', 'Electrical Contractor Business Courses', 'Electrical contractor courses on licensing, panel and EV charger estimating, permits and inspections, job costing, crew training and electrical safety.', 'Homeowners often ask why a panel upgrade costs so much, or whether they can skip the permit and handle a circuit themselves. Explain what the upgrade includes and what inspections protect the homeowner from later.', 100),
  ('plumbing', 'Plumbing', 'Systems', 'Droplets', 'Plumbing businesses organize supply, drain, fixtures, water heaters, labor, and permits into proposals that homeowners and builders can read. This classroom covers the licensing, pricing, and scheduling habits that keep plumbing jobs on time and inspection-ready.', 'Plumbing Contractor Business Courses', 'Plumbing courses on licensing, water heater and repipe estimating, rough-in sequencing, permits, job costing, crew training and safety.', 'Homeowners facing a sudden leak or a failing water heater often want the cheapest repair today, while the real fix is a larger job. Explain the options with photos and clear scope so the choice is made with the facts in front of them.', 110),
  ('hvac', 'HVAC', 'Systems', 'Fan', 'HVAC businesses handle equipment, line sets, ductwork, controls, labor, and startup, and the customer needs to understand the system they are buying. This classroom covers licensing, load calculations, equipment proposals, and service habits that keep installs and maintenance profitable.', 'HVAC Contractor Business Courses', 'HVAC courses on licensing, load-based equipment proposals, ductwork and mini-split estimating, job costing and maintenance agreements.', 'Customers often ask for the cheapest furnace and AC pair without knowing their home''s load, and they compare equipment by price alone. Explain sizing, efficiency, and ductwork in plain terms so the proposal reflects the system they will live with.', 120),
  ('flooring', 'Flooring', 'Interior', 'Grid2x2', 'Flooring businesses handle removal, subfloor prep, underlayment, flooring, transitions, and trim, with waste and moisture shaping every quantity. This classroom covers estimating, sequencing, and customer communication for floor installs and refinishing across homes and light commercial spaces.', 'Flooring Contractor Business Courses', 'Flooring courses on square-foot takeoffs with waste, subfloor prep, LVP and hardwood scope, trade sequencing, job costing and crew training.', 'Homeowners compare flooring quotes by per-square-foot material price and do not see subfloor repair, moisture testing, or transitions until the install starts. Show the prep and materials as their own lines so the comparison is between complete scopes.', 130),
  ('tile', 'Tile', 'Interior', 'LayoutGrid', 'Tile businesses price backer board, waterproofing, setting materials, tile, trim pieces, and labor the way tile setters actually work, from layout to grout. This classroom covers the estimating, sequencing, and quality habits that keep tile jobs accurate and profitable.', 'Tile Contractor Business Courses', 'Tile courses on waterproofing, backer board and setting-material estimates, large-format layout, sequencing, job costing and crew training.', 'Homeowners often want large-format porcelain at a tile price that ignores the flatter substrate, the extra labor, and the waterproofing it needs. Show what a large tile requires in prep and layout so the price matches the work.', 140),
  ('framing', 'Framing', 'Structures', 'Frame', 'Framing businesses quote lumber, sheathing, hardware, and labor by system, from walls and floors to roof framing and openings. This classroom covers the layout, estimating, and crew habits that keep framing packages quick to quote and accurate on site.', 'Framing Contractor Business Courses', 'Framing courses on system-based lumber takeoffs, engineered-lumber coordination, crew sequencing, job costing, hardware tracking and fall safety.', 'Builders and homeowners often ask for a framing number before plans are final, and they compare quotes that include different lumber grades and hardware. State the plan set and lumber assumptions in the quote so the price stays tied to the drawings.', 150),
  ('finish-carpentry', 'Finish Carpentry', 'Interior', 'Hammer', 'Finish carpenters handle baseboard, casing, crown, doors, built-ins, and hardware, where the quality of the cut and the fit is what the homeowner sees first. This classroom covers quoting finish packages, measuring for trim and millwork, and running a small shop and crew profitably.', 'Finish Carpentry Business Courses', 'Finish carpentry courses on trim and millwork estimating, door and built-in scope, proposal design, job costing, crew training and shop safety.', 'Homeowners often expect whole-house trim and built-ins for the price of paint, and they do not see the cutting, scribing, and fitting behind a clean casing line. Show the profile, material, and labor for each room so the proposal reads as craft.', 160),
  ('cabinets-countertops', 'Cabinets & Countertops', 'Interior', 'Archive', 'Cabinet and countertop businesses handle boxes, fillers, hardware, countertops, cutouts, and installation, where the selections drive most of the price. This classroom covers proposals that make selections obvious, measuring and templating accurately, and running install crews that protect finished surfaces.', 'Cabinet and Countertop Business Courses', 'Cabinet and countertop courses on measuring and templating, estimates, selection tracking, install sequencing, job costing and crew safety.', 'Customers often choose a countertop or cabinet line based on a showroom sample and are surprised by the cost of cutouts, edge profiles, or backsplash work. Confirm each selection in writing with its cutouts and edge profile before fabrication starts.', 170),
  ('windows-doors', 'Windows & Doors', 'Exterior', 'DoorOpen', 'Window and door businesses price each unit, its installation, trim, flashing, and disposal, and decide whether customers see per-unit pricing or a single package. This classroom covers measuring, ordering, and installing units so openings stay weathertight and the lead times match the schedule.', 'Window and Door Installer Business Courses', 'Window and door installer courses on measuring openings, per-unit versus package pricing, flashing, job costing and install safety.', 'Homeowners often compare window quotes unit by unit and wonder why one bid includes flashing, trim, and disposal while another does not. Decide how you price the job and explain the choice so the comparison is between equal scopes.', 180),
  ('insulation', 'Insulation', 'Interior', 'Thermometer', 'Insulation businesses install attic, wall, and crawlspace insulation with air sealing and baffles, usually priced by square foot and by material depth. This classroom covers measuring, estimating, and installing insulation in ways that hold up to inspection and keep crews and occupants safe.', 'Insulation Contractor Business Courses', 'Insulation courses on square-foot estimating, air sealing and baffles, blown-in and spray foam work, job costing and respiratory safety.', 'Homeowners often ask why insulation is priced by the square foot and whether the job can skip the air sealing and baffles. Explain how air sealing and ventilation work together so the bid includes the steps that make the insulation perform.', 190),
  ('gutters', 'Gutters', 'Exterior', 'Waves', 'Gutter businesses install seamless gutters, downspouts, guards, and removal, priced in the units installers use, usually linear feet and downspout count. This classroom covers measuring runs, sequencing installs with roofing and siding, and building a service and guard business that keeps customers returning.', 'Gutter Installer Business Courses', 'Gutter installer courses on linear-foot estimating, seamless gutter and guard installs, roofing coordination, job costing, crew training and ladder safety.', 'Customers often compare gutter quotes by price per foot and assume guards, downspout extensions, and removal are included when they are not. Show each line item so the bid is clear about what the homeowner receives.', 200),
  ('fencing', 'Fencing', 'Sitework', 'Fence', 'Fence businesses price posts, panels or pickets, gates, concrete, and labor, and customers need to see what makes up the price. This classroom covers measuring property lines, estimating by linear foot and gate, and running install crews that handle utilities, layout, and the homeowner''s expectations.', 'Fence Contractor Business Courses', 'Fence courses on linear-foot estimating, post and gate pricing, utility locates, pool fence requirements, job costing and crew safety.', 'Homeowners often compare fence quotes by linear foot and ask why one bid is higher when the style and height look the same. Show post spacing, concrete, gates, and removal as separate lines so the difference is visible.', 210),
  ('landscaping', 'Landscaping', 'Sitework', 'Sprout', 'Landscaping businesses combine plants, soil, mulch, edging, sod, and labor, and the work changes with each season and each lawn or bed. This classroom covers estimating installs, scheduling crews around planting windows, and building recurring maintenance so the business earns steadily across the year.', 'Landscaping Business Courses for Contractors', 'Landscaping courses on install estimates, planting and sod scheduling, recurring maintenance pricing, job costing and equipment safety.', 'Homeowners often compare a landscape install to a garden center''s plant list and do not see soil prep, grading, irrigation, or the labor of planting. Show the soil, grading, and planting steps as sections of the proposal so the price reflects the whole job.', 220),
  ('pressure-washing', 'Pressure Washing', 'Exterior', 'SprayCan', 'Pressure washing businesses measure driveways, walkways, patios, decks, and fences, note the surface and its condition, and price each job by area, flat rate, or custom line items. This classroom covers measuring, pricing, and scheduling exterior cleaning so each job is quoted clearly and finished safely.', 'Pressure Washing Business Courses', 'Pressure washing courses on surface measurement, square-foot and flat-rate pricing, minimum charges, routing, job costing and crew safety.', 'Customers often ask for a flat price on a whole house before anyone has measured the surfaces or checked the staining and wood condition. Measure, note the surface, and then quote as a flat rate or by area with the conditions listed.', 230),
  ('soft-washing', 'Soft Washing', 'Exterior', 'ShowerHead', 'Soft washing businesses measure building walls and roofs plane by plane, then price the job by area with the cleaning method and chemical choices kept separate from the estimate. This classroom covers measuring exteriors, pricing clearly, and making safe, documented decisions about method, chemicals, and runoff.', 'Soft Washing Business Courses', 'Soft washing courses on wall and roof area measurement, pricing by area, chemical and runoff rules, scheduling, job costing and safety.', 'Customers often ask for a whole-house price from the curb and do not understand why roof and wall areas need measuring. Explain the measurement and what the price covers, and note any areas that need a separate quote.', 240),
  ('cleaning', 'Cleaning', 'General', 'BrushCleaning', 'Cleaning companies win and keep work by quoting clearly, staffing reliably and turning one-time cleans into recurring service. This classroom covers pricing by area, room or hour, post-construction phases, crew scheduling, chemical safety and building a recurring customer base.', 'Cleaning Business Courses', 'Cleaning business courses on pricing by square foot, room or hour, post-construction cleaning, crew scheduling, chemical safety and recurring revenue.', 'Customers compare cleaning quotes on price alone and rarely see what is included. Explain the scope room by room, list add-ons separately, and show how a first deep clean differs from recurring visits.', 250),
  ('excavation', 'Excavation', 'Sitework', 'Shovel', 'Excavation businesses price equipment time, hauling, fill, grading, and mobilization, and the trucking is often where margins are lost. This classroom covers estimating dig and grade work by volume and hours, managing trucks and crews on tight sites, and keeping utility and safety responsibilities clear.', 'Excavation Contractor Business Courses', 'Excavation courses on equipment-hour and hauling estimates, grading and fill volumes, mobilization pricing, locates, job costing and trench safety.', 'Customers often compare excavation bids by equipment hourly rate and do not see the hauling, fill, and mobilization costs behind the number. Show the trucks, loads, and fill as separate lines so the price covers the trucking.', 260),
  ('foundations', 'Foundations', 'Structures', 'Building', 'Foundation businesses organize footings, walls, reinforcement, waterproofing, and drainage by phase, with inspections and cure time shaping the schedule. This classroom covers estimating and sequencing foundation work, managing concrete and rebar suppliers, and handling repair and waterproofing jobs in existing homes.', 'Foundation Contractor Business Courses', 'Foundation courses on footing and wall estimating, rebar and concrete coordination, waterproofing, repair scope, inspection sequencing and safety.', 'Homeowners with foundation cracks or water in the basement often want the cheapest patch, and they are surprised when the engineer or inspector calls for a larger fix. Explain the cause, the options, and the inspection steps so the homeowner chooses with the full picture.', 270),
  ('masonry', 'Masonry', 'Structures', 'BrickWall', 'Masonry businesses price brick, block, stone, mortar, reinforcement, and scaffolding for new veneer, retaining walls, and repair work, and weather governs much of the calendar. This classroom covers estimating units and mortar, scheduling around temperature, and running a crew that builds to specification.', 'Masonry Contractor Business Courses', 'Masonry courses on brick, block and stone estimating, mortar and reinforcement, cold-weather scheduling, tuckpointing, job costing and safety.', 'Homeowners often compare brick veneer or tuckpointing bids and expect the cheapest mortar and a fast timeline. Explain the mortar type, joint work, and cold-weather limits so the scope and schedule are realistic.', 280),
  ('asphalt-paving', 'Asphalt & Paving', 'Sitework', 'Route', 'Asphalt and paving businesses price base preparation, asphalt tonnage, sealcoating, and striping, and the work depends on temperature, moisture, and a schedule that fits the property. This classroom covers estimating paving by tons and area, scheduling around weather and traffic, and running crews and equipment safely on active sites.', 'Asphalt and Paving Business Courses', 'Asphalt and paving courses on base prep, tonnage estimating, sealcoat and striping scope, weather and traffic scheduling, job costing and jobsite safety.', 'Property owners often compare paving bids by price per square foot and do not see that base repair, not the surface, drives the life of the pavement. Show the base prep and thickness as lines so the lower bid can be judged against the same scope.', 290),
  ('demolition', 'Demolition', 'General', 'Hammer', 'Demolition businesses price labor, equipment, dumpsters, haul-off, and protection for interior and exterior tear-outs, and disposal costs can change the job after it starts. This classroom covers estimating by area and debris, planning sequences that protect adjacent spaces, and running crews safely around hazards that old buildings hide.', 'Demolition Contractor Business Courses', 'Demolition courses on debris and haul-off estimating, dumpster pricing, utility disconnects, hazardous material checks, job costing and safety.', 'Homeowners often ask for a demolition price before anyone knows what is inside the walls, and they resist disposal and dump-fee add-ons. Explain the testing, disconnects, and disposal costs in writing so the price is clear before the first wall comes down.', 300),
  ('basements', 'Basements', 'Interior', 'ArrowDownToLine', 'Basement projects move through framing, insulation, electrical, drywall, flooring, and finishes, and moisture and egress decisions shape nearly every phase. This classroom covers organizing a basement estimate by phase, managing moisture and code-related choices, and keeping the owner informed as hidden conditions surface.', 'Basement Finishing Business Courses', 'Basement finishing courses on phased estimates, moisture and waterproofing checks, egress and permit basics, trade sequencing and job costing.', 'Homeowners often want a finished basement at a price based on the open floor area, and they do not expect the waterproofing, egress, or electrical work that the code requires. Walk the space with them and list those items before the number goes out.', 310),
  ('additions', 'Additions', 'Structures', 'BoxSelect', 'Home additions bring foundations, framing, roofing, windows, mechanical work, and finishes into one project, organized as phases with a clear total. This classroom covers estimating each phase, sequencing a project that stays under permit, and managing a household that keeps living in the house during construction.', 'Home Addition Business Courses for Contractors', 'Home addition courses on phased estimates, foundation and roof tie-ins, permits, sequencing, job costing, crew training and site safety.', 'Homeowners often think of an addition as a room and are surprised by the foundation, roof tie-in, and mechanical upgrades it requires. Lay out each phase and the reason it is needed before the design is finalized.', 320),
  ('garages', 'Garages', 'Structures', 'Warehouse', 'Garage projects cover slabs, framing, roofing, siding, doors, and electrical for detached and attached structures, each with its own permits and inspections. This classroom covers estimating garages as systems, sequencing trades around the slab and roof, and building repeat work from garage doors and conversions.', 'Garage Construction Business Courses', 'Garage construction courses on detached and attached estimating, slab and framing sequence, door and electrical scope, job costing and safety.', 'Homeowners often want a two-car garage at the price of a shed, and they do not expect the footings, slab thickness, and electrical service that the design needs. Lay out the slab, framing, and electrical in the proposal so the scope and price match.', 330),
  ('pole-barns', 'Pole Barns & Metal Buildings', 'Structures', 'Tractor', 'Pole barn and metal building businesses organize posts, trusses, purlins, metal panels, trim, doors, and labor for post-frame and steel structures, with the footing layout setting everything that follows. This classroom covers quoting kits and site-built packages, sequencing erection around weather, and managing agricultural and shop customers.', 'Pole Barn and Metal Building Business Courses', 'Pole barn and metal building courses on post-frame estimating, kit versus installed pricing, erection sequencing, job costing and lift safety.', 'Customers comparing a kit price from a supplier against an installed bid often miss the footings, concrete, insulation, and erection labor that the kit does not include. Show the kit and the installed scope as separate columns so the comparison is fair.', 340),
  ('commercial-remodeling', 'Commercial Remodeling', 'General', 'Building2', 'Commercial remodeling businesses organize tenant improvements by division or area, with general conditions, subcontractors, and fees in one professional proposal. This classroom covers bidding and managing commercial interior and exterior work, working within owner and tenant schedules, and keeping the documentation that commercial clients expect.', 'Commercial Remodeling Business Courses', 'Commercial remodeling courses on tenant improvement estimating, general conditions, sub bids, schedules, job costing and documentation.', 'Commercial owners and property managers often compare bids on a single line total and ask why general conditions and fees are separate. Show the scope by division, with general conditions and fees explained, so the total can be checked line by line.', 350),
  ('general-contracting', 'General Contracting', 'General', 'HardHat', 'General contracting businesses combine their own labor with subcontractor quotes, allowances, and fees, and the owner''s trust depends on how clearly the proposal shows each piece. This classroom covers building proposals that show as much detail as the client wants, managing subs and schedules, and running the business side of a general contractor.', 'General Contractor Business Courses', 'General contractor courses on sub bid leveling, allowances and fees, proposal detail, schedule management, job costing and site safety.', 'Owners often compare a general contractor''s total with a single trade bid and ask why the number includes fees and allowances. Explain the fee, the allowances, and what each sub quote covers so the total is traceable.', 360),
  ('handyman', 'Handyman Services', 'General', 'Wrench', 'Handyman businesses price work by the hour or by the task, with materials and trip charges added, and a list of small jobs can fill a week fast. This classroom covers quick, clear pricing, scheduling many small calls efficiently, and building a steady base of repeat homeowner and property manager work.', 'Handyman Business Courses for Contractors', 'Handyman business courses on hourly and per-task pricing, materials and trip charges, route scheduling, job costing, quality repairs and ladder safety.', 'Homeowners often ask for a quick price over the phone for a list of small repairs and expect a single low number. Quote by task with a minimum or trip charge, and say what needs an on-site look before a firm price.', 370)
insert into public.academy_resources (id, kind, title, creator_name, creator_url, community_name, platform, source_url, embed_id, embed_allowed, thumbnail_url, summary, why_it_matters, takeaways, trades, skill, access_note, permission_status, views_at_verification, verified_at, verification_note, status) values
  (md5('academy:resource:hormozi-leads')::uuid, 'youtube', 'Watch This To Generate 1000s of Leads (In Any Niche)', 'Alex Hormozi', 'https://www.youtube.com/@AlexHormozi', null, 'YouTube', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Mst4hreQYl0', 'Mst4hreQYl0', false, null, 'A long-form talk from Alex Hormozi on lead generation for any kind of business: the main ways to get attention and turn it into enquiries.', 'Most contractors rely on one lead source. A clear map of the options helps you add a second and third channel before the first one dries up.', array['List every way a homeowner could hear about you, then pick one new channel to test.', 'Track where each lead came from so you know which channel actually pays.']::text[], '{}'::text[], 'sales', null, 'link_only', 927966, '2026-11-18'::date, 'Title, channel, views and embed setting read from the public YouTube page; summary written from the title and creator''s description. The creator has disabled embedding, so Built2Bid links to the original video instead of playing it here.', 'verified'),
  (md5('academy:resource:hormozi-free-customers')::uuid, 'youtube', '7 Ways To Get Customers for Free', 'Alex Hormozi', 'https://www.youtube.com/@AlexHormozi', null, 'YouTube', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=qpQvdBFW_yI', 'qpQvdBFW_yI', false, null, 'Alex Hormozi covers low-cost ways to win customers without paid advertising.', 'Referrals, reviews and past customers are the cheapest leads a contractor will ever get. This is a useful prompt to work them on purpose.', array['Ask every happy customer for a referral at the moment they''re happiest, not months later.', 'Your past-customer list is a lead source. Stay in touch.']::text[], '{}'::text[], 'sales', null, 'link_only', 232287, '2026-11-18'::date, 'Title, channel, views and embed setting read from the public YouTube page; summary written from the title and creator''s description. The creator has disabled embedding, so Built2Bid links to the original video instead of playing it here.', 'verified'),
  (md5('academy:resource:hunsaker-gbp')::uuid, 'youtube', 'How to Optimize Your Google Business Profile to Outrank 99% of Local Businesses on Google', 'Steve Hunsaker | Home Service Accelerator', 'https://www.youtube.com/@SteveHunsaker', null, 'YouTube', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=PlZ43ZKMk34', 'PlZ43ZKMk34', true, 'https://i.ytimg.com/vi/PlZ43ZKMk34/hqdefault.jpg', 'A walkthrough of setting up and improving a Google Business Profile for a home-service company, aimed at showing up in local map results.', 'For most local contractors the Google Business Profile is the front door: reviews, photos and service areas are what homeowners see first.', array['Fill in every field: services, service area, hours and real job photos.', 'Ask for reviews consistently and reply to every one.']::text[], '{}'::text[], 'marketing', null, 'link_only', 24346, '2026-11-18'::date, 'Title, channel, views and embed setting read from the public YouTube page; summary written from the title and creator''s description.', 'verified'),
  (md5('academy:resource:roofing-insights-7-steps')::uuid, 'youtube', 'My 7 Steps Sales Process as a Contractor', 'Roofing Insights', 'https://www.youtube.com/@RoofingInsights3.0', null, 'YouTube', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=azbZRnBRrIQ', 'azbZRnBRrIQ', true, 'https://i.ytimg.com/vi/azbZRnBRrIQ/hqdefault.jpg', 'A contractor''s step-by-step sales process, from first contact to signed job, presented by the Roofing Insights channel.', 'Writing your process down as steps is what lets you repeat it, train someone else on it, and see where deals stall.', array['Name each step of your sales process and what has to happen before moving on.', 'Compare it with your own: which step do you usually skip?']::text[], array['roofing']::text[], 'sales', null, 'link_only', 10149, '2026-11-18'::date, 'Title, channel, views and embed setting read from the public YouTube page; summary written from the title and creator''s description.', 'verified'),
  (md5('academy:resource:miner-discovery')::uuid, 'youtube', 'What Questions To Ask Prospects During The Sales Discovery Process', 'Jeremy Miner', 'https://www.youtube.com/@JeremyMiner', null, 'YouTube', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=dDGX95UkV10', 'dDGX95UkV10', true, 'https://i.ytimg.com/vi/dDGX95UkV10/hqdefault.jpg', 'Jeremy Miner on asking questions that get a prospect to describe their real problem, instead of jumping straight to a pitch.', 'On a walk-through, the contractor who understands why the customer called (not just what they want built) writes the proposal that fits.', array['Ask what prompted the call now, and what happens if nothing changes.', 'Listen for the problem behind the project, then repeat it back.']::text[], '{}'::text[], 'sales', null, 'link_only', 73289, '2026-11-18'::date, 'Title, channel, views and embed setting read from the public YouTube page; summary written from the title and creator''s description.', 'verified'),
  (md5('academy:resource:miner-better-questions')::uuid, 'youtube', 'How to Ask BETTER Sales Questions', 'Jeremy Miner', 'https://www.youtube.com/@JeremyMiner', null, 'YouTube', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=bz505UfWme0', 'bz505UfWme0', true, 'https://i.ytimg.com/vi/bz505UfWme0/hqdefault.jpg', 'A longer session from Jeremy Miner on wording sales questions so they open up a conversation rather than feel like an interrogation.', 'Homeowners have usually met several contractors. Better questions are one of the few ways to stand out before you''ve quoted anything.', array['Prefer open questions (how, what, why) over yes/no questions early on.', 'Follow up on answers instead of moving to the next item on your list.']::text[], '{}'::text[], 'sales', null, 'link_only', 160861, '2026-11-18'::date, 'Title, channel, views and embed setting read from the public YouTube page; summary written from the title and creator''s description.', 'verified'),
  (md5('academy:resource:builder-funnel-remodel-sales')::uuid, 'youtube', 'Remodeling Sales Training: Complete Process Breakdown', 'Builder Funnel', 'https://www.youtube.com/@BuilderFunnel', null, 'YouTube', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=YaWfoYjxKy8', 'YaWfoYjxKy8', true, 'https://i.ytimg.com/vi/YaWfoYjxKy8/hqdefault.jpg', 'Builder Funnel breaks down a remodeling sales process, starting with a short phone pre-qualification on location, budget and project type.', 'Remodelers lose whole days to appointments that were never a fit. A short qualifying call protects your calendar.', array['Confirm service area, budget range and project type before booking a site visit.', 'It''s fine to refer out work you don''t do.']::text[], array['kitchens', 'bathrooms', 'interior-remodeling', 'basements', 'additions']::text[], 'sales', null, 'link_only', 6020, '2026-11-18'::date, 'Title, channel, views and embed setting read from the public YouTube page; summary written from the title and creator''s description.', 'verified'),
  (md5('academy:resource:barstow-painting-sales')::uuid, 'youtube', 'Sales Basics Painting Contractors Miss', 'Eric Barstow', 'https://www.youtube.com/@EricBarstowCo', null, 'YouTube', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=DzGZOrfIM48', 'DzGZOrfIM48', true, 'https://i.ytimg.com/vi/DzGZOrfIM48/hqdefault.jpg', 'Eric Barstow covers sales fundamentals that painting contractors often overlook when meeting homeowners and quoting jobs.', 'Painting is easy for customers to compare on price alone. The basics of a good sales visit are how a painter avoids becoming the cheapest bid.', array['Treat the estimate visit as a sales appointment, not just a measurement.', 'Explain your prep process; it''s what the customer can''t see in a price.']::text[], array['painting']::text[], 'sales', null, 'link_only', 9979, '2026-11-18'::date, 'Title, channel, views and embed setting read from the public YouTube page; summary written from the title and creator''s description.', 'verified'),
  (md5('academy:resource:contractor-cuts-present')::uuid, 'youtube', 'How to Present an Estimate So Clients Say Yes', 'Contractor Cuts', 'https://www.youtube.com/@contractorcuts', null, 'YouTube', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=PQjZIWADgJg', 'PQjZIWADgJg', true, 'https://i.ytimg.com/vi/PQjZIWADgJg/hqdefault.jpg', 'A Contractor Cuts podcast episode on presenting an estimate as part of a relationship with the client, rather than just sending a number.', 'The same price lands very differently when the customer trusts you. How you present matters as much as what you charge.', array['Walk the customer through the proposal instead of only emailing it.', 'Build trust before price: process, communication and how you handle problems.']::text[], '{}'::text[], 'sales', null, 'link_only', 571, '2026-11-18'::date, 'Title, channel, views and embed setting read from the public YouTube page; summary written from the title and creator''s description.', 'verified'),
  (md5('academy:resource:wallin-break-down-bid')::uuid, 'youtube', 'NEVER Break Down A Bid For A Customer - Here''s Why', 'Successful Contractor', 'https://www.youtube.com/@SuccessfulContractor', null, 'YouTube', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Vr5G1wBaBMg', 'Vr5G1wBaBMg', true, 'https://i.ytimg.com/vi/Vr5G1wBaBMg/hqdefault.jpg', 'The Successful Contractor channel explains the difference between a bid and an estimate, and why he doesn''t itemize prices when customers ask.', 'Itemized pricing invites line-by-line shopping. Deciding your policy before the customer asks keeps the conversation on scope and value.', array['Decide in advance what level of detail your proposals show.', 'Show the scope in detail even if you don''t show every unit price.']::text[], '{}'::text[], 'sales', null, 'link_only', 592570, '2026-11-18'::date, 'Title, channel, views and embed setting read from the public YouTube page; summary written from the title and creator''s description.', 'verified'),
  (md5('academy:resource:hormozi-never-lower-prices')::uuid, 'youtube', 'NEVER lower your prices...', 'Alex Hormozi', 'https://www.youtube.com/@AlexHormozi', null, 'YouTube', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=BZQtuK-ucDM', 'BZQtuK-ucDM', false, null, 'Alex Hormozi argues against discounting as a way to win sales.', 'A discount comes straight out of profit. Contractors who change scope or terms instead of price protect their margin.', array['If the budget is tight, reduce scope or offer options instead of cutting the price.', 'Know your margin floor before the appointment.']::text[], '{}'::text[], 'sales', null, 'link_only', 127859, '2026-11-18'::date, 'Title, channel, views and embed setting read from the public YouTube page; summary written from the title and creator''s description. The creator has disabled embedding, so Built2Bid links to the original video instead of playing it here.', 'verified'),
  (md5('academy:resource:reber-too-expensive')::uuid, 'youtube', 'Exactly What to Say When They Say "You''re Too Expensive"', 'Contractor Fight TV', 'https://www.youtube.com/@contractorfighttv', null, 'YouTube', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=xsv_C5uHrXU', 'xsv_C5uHrXU', true, 'https://i.ytimg.com/vi/xsv_C5uHrXU/hqdefault.jpg', 'Contractor sales training on why customers say a price is too high, how to find the real objection, and how to respond without discounting.', '"Too expensive" is rarely the full story. Finding out what the customer is comparing you to is the first step to answering it.', array['Ask what they''re comparing your price to before you respond.', 'Answer the real concern (trust, timing, scope) instead of the price alone.']::text[], '{}'::text[], 'sales', null, 'link_only', 187469, '2026-11-18'::date, 'Title, channel, views and embed setting read from the public YouTube page; summary written from the title and creator''s description.', 'verified'),
  (md5('academy:resource:miner-too-expensive')::uuid, 'youtube', 'How To Handle "This Is Too Expensive" Objection', 'Jeremy Miner', 'https://www.youtube.com/@JeremyMiner', null, 'YouTube', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=amdE9PVSyZI', 'amdE9PVSyZI', true, 'https://i.ytimg.com/vi/amdE9PVSyZI/hqdefault.jpg', 'A short Jeremy Miner clip on responding to the price objection with questions rather than defending the number.', 'A calm question keeps the conversation going. Arguing for your price usually ends it.', array['Respond to a price objection with a question, not a justification.', 'Stay curious: "compared to what?" is a fair question.']::text[], '{}'::text[], 'sales', null, 'link_only', 76282, '2026-11-18'::date, 'Title, channel, views and embed setting read from the public YouTube page; summary written from the title and creator''s description.', 'verified'),
  (md5('academy:resource:bensman-roofing-objections')::uuid, 'youtube', 'Every Roofing Sales Objection & How to Overcome It', 'The STRONG Roofer™ w/ Adam Bensman', 'https://www.youtube.com/@TheSTRONGRoofer', null, 'YouTube', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=5LnEZQG_BpA', '5LnEZQG_BpA', true, 'https://i.ytimg.com/vi/5LnEZQG_BpA/hqdefault.jpg', 'A compilation of the channel''s roofing objection-handling videos in one session.', 'Roofing homeowners raise the same handful of objections. Having practised answers keeps you calm and honest at the kitchen table.', array['Write down the five objections you hear most and your honest answer to each.', 'Practise them out loud before appointments.']::text[], array['roofing', 'gutters', 'siding']::text[], 'sales', null, 'link_only', 50638, '2026-11-18'::date, 'Title, channel, views and embed setting read from the public YouTube page; summary written from the title and creator''s description.', 'verified'),
  (md5('academy:resource:bensman-roofing-price')::uuid, 'youtube', 'Roofing Sales Objections: "It Costs Too Much" or "You''re Too Expensive" - How to Overcome & Close!', 'The STRONG Roofer™ w/ Adam Bensman', 'https://www.youtube.com/@TheSTRONGRoofer', null, 'YouTube', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=8zGslRlZ6Rs', '8zGslRlZ6Rs', true, 'https://i.ytimg.com/vi/8zGslRlZ6Rs/hqdefault.jpg', 'Focused on financial objections in roofing sales: educating the homeowner and handling cost concerns.', 'A roof is a large, unplanned purchase for most homeowners. Helping them understand the investment is part of the job.', array['Explain what''s included and why, especially items the homeowner can''t see.', 'Be ready to talk through payment timing honestly.']::text[], array['roofing']::text[], 'sales', null, 'link_only', 9500, '2026-11-18'::date, 'Title, channel, views and embed setting read from the public YouTube page; summary written from the title and creator''s description.', 'verified'),
  (md5('academy:resource:profitdig-bidding')::uuid, 'youtube', 'Construction Bidding Tips That Actually Win Jobs (and Protect Your Profit)', 'ProfitDig | Contractor Business Strategies, Advice', 'https://www.youtube.com/@profitdig', null, 'YouTube', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Mah03fCqN1w', 'Mah03fCqN1w', true, 'https://i.ytimg.com/vi/Mah03fCqN1w/hqdefault.jpg', 'A ProfitDig Live panel on building bids strategically rather than just competitively: what to include, what to exclude, and handling unknowns such as rock in excavation.', 'When you''re up against a lower number, a clear scope with written exclusions is often what protects both the job and your margin.', array['Write exclusions and allowances for the unknowns you can''t price.', 'Compete on clarity and risk, not only on the bottom line.']::text[], array['concrete', 'excavation', 'foundations', 'asphalt-paving', 'general-contracting']::text[], 'estimating', null, 'link_only', 3368, '2026-11-18'::date, 'Title, channel, views and embed setting read from the public YouTube page; summary written from the title and creator''s description.', 'verified'),
  (md5('academy:resource:reber-follow-up')::uuid, 'youtube', 'When Should You Follow Up on Estimates? (without Sounding Desperate)', 'Contractor Fight TV', 'https://www.youtube.com/@contractorfighttv', null, 'YouTube', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=dY7KLX2sOvg', 'dY7KLX2sOvg', true, 'https://i.ytimg.com/vi/dY7KLX2sOvg/hqdefault.jpg', 'Tom Reber''s take on how long to wait before following up on a quote, and how to follow up without sounding desperate.', 'Many estimates are lost to silence rather than to a competitor. A planned follow-up is one of the cheapest wins in contracting.', array['Agree on the next step and date before you leave the appointment.', 'Follow up with something useful, not just "checking in".']::text[], '{}'::text[], 'sales', null, 'link_only', 15688, '2026-11-18'::date, 'Title, channel, views and embed setting read from the public YouTube page; summary written from the title and creator''s description.', 'verified'),
  (md5('academy:resource:hormozi-3-steps-close')::uuid, 'youtube', '3 Simple Steps To Close Any Sale', 'Alex Hormozi', 'https://www.youtube.com/@AlexHormozi', null, 'YouTube', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=CojS0DwflXc', 'CojS0DwflXc', false, null, 'Alex Hormozi outlines a simple three-step structure for closing a sale.', 'Many contractors present well and then never actually ask for the job. A simple structure makes asking feel natural.', array['End every presentation with a clear question about next steps.', 'Then stop talking and let the customer answer.']::text[], '{}'::text[], 'sales', null, 'link_only', 459854, '2026-11-18'::date, 'Title, channel, views and embed setting read from the public YouTube page; summary written from the title and creator''s description. The creator has disabled embedding, so Built2Bid links to the original video instead of playing it here.', 'verified'),
  (md5('academy:resource:jobnimbus-communication')::uuid, 'youtube', 'The Best Way Contractors Communicate With Customers | Building Business', 'JobNimbus', 'https://www.youtube.com/@JobNimbusCRM', null, 'YouTube', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=3EvXT0NI49o', '3EvXT0NI49o', true, 'https://i.ytimg.com/vi/3EvXT0NI49o/hqdefault.jpg', 'An episode of JobNimbus''s Building Business series on how contractors communicate with customers.', 'Customers judge a contractor by how informed they feel. Regular, predictable updates prevent most complaints.', array['Set expectations for how and when you''ll update the customer.', 'Bad news travels better early.']::text[], '{}'::text[], 'project_management', null, 'link_only', 1091, '2026-11-18'::date, 'Title, channel, views and embed setting read from the public YouTube page; summary written from the title and creator''s description.', 'verified'),
  (md5('academy:resource:schroeder-communication')::uuid, 'youtube', 'Communication: The Secret Weapon In Construction Management', 'Jason Schroeder', 'https://www.youtube.com/@jasonwilliamschroeder', null, 'YouTube', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=y2lHilKysZY', 'y2lHilKysZY', true, 'https://i.ytimg.com/vi/y2lHilKysZY/hqdefault.jpg', 'Jason Schroeder on why communication is a core construction-management skill for everyone on a team, with advice on improving your communication systems.', 'Crews, subs and customers all run on the same information. A simple system beats heroic phone calls.', array['Decide which updates go to whom, and how often.', 'Write it down: a short written update avoids "I thought you said".']::text[], '{}'::text[], 'project_management', null, 'link_only', 3935, '2026-11-18'::date, 'Title, channel, views and embed setting read from the public YouTube page; summary written from the title and creator''s description.', 'verified'),
  (md5('academy:resource:schroeder-manage-project')::uuid, 'youtube', 'How To Manage A Construction Project Step By Step', 'Jason Schroeder', 'https://www.youtube.com/@jasonwilliamschroeder', null, 'YouTube', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=PDAmTebSIv8', 'PDAmTebSIv8', true, 'https://i.ytimg.com/vi/PDAmTebSIv8/hqdefault.jpg', 'A step-by-step approach to managing a construction project from Jason Schroeder.', 'Small contractors often manage projects from memory. A repeatable sequence is how you take on more work without dropping balls.', array['Use the same project start-up checklist on every job.', 'Plan the work before the crew shows up.']::text[], '{}'::text[], 'project_management', null, 'link_only', 275143, '2026-11-18'::date, 'Title, channel, views and embed setting read from the public YouTube page; summary written from the title and creator''s description.', 'verified'),
  (md5('academy:resource:schroeder-scheduling-101')::uuid, 'youtube', 'Construction Scheduling 101', 'Jason Schroeder', 'https://www.youtube.com/@jasonwilliamschroeder', null, 'YouTube', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=0ppqmwX-4jg', '0ppqmwX-4jg', true, 'https://i.ytimg.com/vi/0ppqmwX-4jg/hqdefault.jpg', 'An introduction to construction scheduling methods and techniques, with the pros and cons of each.', 'A realistic schedule is a sales tool too: customers buy from the contractor who can tell them when the job will happen.', array['Pick one scheduling method and use it consistently.', 'Share start dates and milestones with customers in writing.']::text[], '{}'::text[], 'project_management', null, 'link_only', 22079, '2026-11-18'::date, 'Title, channel, views and embed setting read from the public YouTube page; summary written from the title and creator''s description.', 'verified'),
  (md5('academy:resource:claudio-metrics')::uuid, 'youtube', 'Contractor Business Tips - Metrics You Need To Be Tracking', 'Construction Business Expert', 'https://www.youtube.com/@themikeclaudio', null, 'YouTube', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=vS5tNMnU-d0', 'vS5tNMnU-d0', true, 'https://i.ytimg.com/vi/vS5tNMnU-d0/hqdefault.jpg', 'Mike Claudio on the business metrics contractors should track.', 'You can''t improve a close rate you don''t measure. A few numbers reviewed weekly beat a big report nobody reads.', array['Track leads, appointments, proposals sent and jobs won every week.', 'Look at trends over months, not single weeks.']::text[], '{}'::text[], 'sales', null, 'link_only', 745, '2026-11-18'::date, 'Title, channel, views and embed setting read from the public YouTube page; summary written from the title and creator''s description.', 'verified'),
  (md5('academy:resource:link-estimate-5-steps')::uuid, 'youtube', 'How to Estimate Projects: 5 Simple Steps to Profitable Pricing', 'Tyler Link', 'https://www.youtube.com/@Tyler-link', null, 'YouTube', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=7UkZreTuH1Q', '7UkZreTuH1Q', true, 'https://i.ytimg.com/vi/7UkZreTuH1Q/hqdefault.jpg', 'Tyler Link explains an estimating system that accounts for overhead and direct costs before setting a price.', 'Pricing that forgets overhead feels competitive and quietly loses money. Knowing your real costs is what makes a price defensible.', array['Separate direct job costs from overhead.', 'Know the minimum you need on every job before you bid.']::text[], array['concrete']::text[], 'estimating', null, 'link_only', 65502, '2026-11-18'::date, 'Title, channel, views and embed setting read from the public YouTube page; summary written from the title and creator''s description.', 'verified'),
  (md5('academy:resource:bta-job-costing')::uuid, 'youtube', 'STOP Losing Money on Jobs (Job Costing 101)', 'Breakthrough Academy', 'https://www.youtube.com/@BreakthroughAcademy', null, 'YouTube', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=nCzP0B2u4BM', 'nCzP0B2u4BM', true, 'https://i.ytimg.com/vi/nCzP0B2u4BM/hqdefault.jpg', 'Breakthrough Academy explains what job costing is, why it matters for profitability, and how to start doing it.', 'Job costing closes the loop between what you estimated and what the job really cost, which makes your next estimate better.', array['Compare estimated versus actual labor and materials on every job.', 'Use the gaps to adjust your pricing.']::text[], '{}'::text[], 'accounting', null, 'link_only', 6288, '2026-11-18'::date, 'Title, channel, views and embed setting read from the public YouTube page; summary written from the title and creator''s description.', 'verified'),
  (md5('academy:resource:construction-cpa-job-costing')::uuid, 'youtube', 'Construction Job Costing Basics | Labor, Materials & Overhead', 'The Construction CPA', 'https://www.youtube.com/@theconstructioncpa', null, 'YouTube', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=cWLoT8PKvp4', 'cWLoT8PKvp4', true, 'https://i.ytimg.com/vi/cWLoT8PKvp4/hqdefault.jpg', 'A CPA''s introduction to construction job costing across labor, materials and overhead.', 'Getting the categories right is what makes job-cost reports useful. Talk to your own accountant about how to apply it.', array['Track labor, materials and overhead separately.', 'Ask your accountant how they want job costs coded.']::text[], '{}'::text[], 'accounting', null, 'link_only', 969, '2026-11-18'::date, 'Title, channel, views and embed setting read from the public YouTube page; summary written from the title and creator''s description.', 'verified'),
  (md5('academy:resource:reber-find-employees')::uuid, 'youtube', '6 Little-Known Ways to Find Employees for Your Construction Business', 'Contractor Fight TV', 'https://www.youtube.com/@contractorfighttv', null, 'YouTube', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=C5G2CjheghE', 'C5G2CjheghE', true, 'https://i.ytimg.com/vi/C5G2CjheghE/hqdefault.jpg', 'Ideas for marketing your company to potential employees, treating hiring like a marketing problem.', 'Production capacity limits sales. Recruiting continuously, not only when you''re desperate, is how contractors grow.', array['Recruit all year, not only when someone quits.', 'Tell candidates why your company is a good place to work.']::text[], '{}'::text[], 'hr', null, 'link_only', 13419, '2026-11-18'::date, 'Title, channel, views and embed setting read from the public YouTube page; summary written from the title and creator''s description.', 'verified'),
  (md5('academy:resource:andes-recurring-lawn')::uuid, 'youtube', 'How to Charge Customers for Lawn Care: Recurring vs Non-Recurring', 'Mike Andes Highlights', 'https://www.youtube.com/@mikeandeshighlights', null, 'YouTube', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=9LorPIGYu8s', '9LorPIGYu8s', true, 'https://i.ytimg.com/vi/9LorPIGYu8s/hqdefault.jpg', 'A short clip on structuring lawn-care pricing as recurring versus one-time work.', 'Recurring maintenance smooths out cash flow between installation jobs and keeps you in front of the customer for the next project.', array['Offer every install customer a maintenance option.', 'Recurring billing should be simple for the customer to understand.']::text[], array['landscaping', 'pressure-washing', 'soft-washing']::text[], 'growth', null, 'link_only', 1526, '2026-11-18'::date, 'Title, channel, views and embed setting read from the public YouTube page; summary written from the title and creator''s description.', 'verified'),
  (md5('academy:resource:histurf-agreements')::uuid, 'youtube', 'What are lawn care maintenance agreements and should you have them? Lawn Care Tips and Tricks', 'it''s HIS turf', 'https://www.youtube.com/@itshisturf23', null, 'YouTube', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=vOz2sR9emnQ', 'vOz2sR9emnQ', true, 'https://i.ytimg.com/vi/vOz2sR9emnQ/hqdefault.jpg', 'A lawn-care operator discusses service agreements and why to offer them.', 'A written agreement sets expectations for frequency, price and cancellation, which protects both sides of a recurring service.', array['Put frequency, price changes and cancellation terms in writing.', 'Have your agreement reviewed for your state.']::text[], array['landscaping']::text[], 'growth', null, 'link_only', 5029, '2026-11-18'::date, 'Title, channel, views and embed setting read from the public YouTube page; summary written from the title and creator''s description.', 'verified'),
  (md5('academy:resource:dol-falls')::uuid, 'official', 'Falls in Construction/Leading Edge Work', 'U.S. Department of Labor', 'https://www.youtube.com/@USDepartmentofLabor', null, 'YouTube', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=kRUywsBpWY8', 'kRUywsBpWY8', true, 'https://i.ytimg.com/vi/kRUywsBpWY8/hqdefault.jpg', 'A short U.S. Department of Labor video on fall hazards during leading-edge construction work.', 'Falls are a well-known cause of serious construction injuries. Federal OSHA rules apply nationally, and some states run their own plans with additional requirements.', array['Plan fall protection before work at height starts.', 'Check whether your state runs its own OSHA-approved plan.']::text[], array['roofing', 'framing', 'siding', 'gutters', 'general-contracting', 'additions', 'pole-barns']::text[], 'safety', null, 'link_only', 179708, '2026-11-18'::date, 'Title, channel, views and embed setting read from the public YouTube page; summary written from the title and creator''s description.', 'verified'),
  (md5('academy:resource:skool-construction-contractors-hub')::uuid, 'skool_community', 'Construction Contractors Hub', 'Tim Fairley', null, 'Construction Contractors Hub', 'Skool', 'https://www.skool.com/construction-contractors/about', null, false, null, 'A Skool community offering free construction project-management lessons for contractors and people building their skills.', 'A good free place to go deeper on project management after the Academy''s introduction.', array['Pair it with the Project Management courses in your trade classroom.']::text[], '{}'::text[], 'project_management', 'Public community on Skool. No membership price was shown on its listing when checked.', 'link_only', null, '2026-11-18'::date, 'Name, owner and description read from the community''s public Skool About page. Not signed in; no member content accessed.', 'verified'),
  (md5('academy:resource:skool-cch-pm-course')::uuid, 'skool_course', '10+ Hour Construction Mgt Course', 'Tim Fairley', null, 'Construction Contractors Hub', 'Skool', 'https://www.skool.com/construction-contractors/classroom/6e2a1d8d?md=1a0843b9e710415797e0cc71c4d62c6a', null, false, null, 'A long-form construction management course linked from the Construction Contractors Hub''s public About page.', 'For contractors who want a structured, longer program on running projects.', array['Built2Bid links to this course; it is not hosted or copied here.']::text[], '{}'::text[], 'project_management', 'Hosted on Skool by its creator. Skool may ask you to sign in or join to view it.', 'link_only', null, '2026-11-18'::date, 'Course name and link read from the community''s public Skool About page links. Course content was not opened.', 'verified'),
  (md5('academy:resource:skool-accounting-for-contractors')::uuid, 'skool_community', 'Accounting for Contractors', 'Vasili Kulikov', null, 'Accounting for Contractors', 'Skool', 'https://www.skool.com/accounting-for-contractors-6711/about', null, false, null, 'A Skool community about the financial systems contractors use to control cash flow and improve job profitability.', 'Financial questions are where a contractor most needs an expert who knows construction.', array['Bring specific questions about job costing and cash flow.']::text[], '{}'::text[], 'accounting', 'Private community on Skool (join request required). No membership price was shown on its listing when checked.', 'link_only', null, '2026-11-18'::date, 'Name, owner and description read from the community''s public Skool About page. Not signed in; no member content accessed.', 'verified'),
  (md5('academy:resource:skool-stg-academy')::uuid, 'skool_community', 'STG Academy', 'Ryan Groth', null, 'STG Academy', 'Skool', 'https://www.skool.com/sales-transformation-group-774/about', null, false, null, 'A Skool community focused on building roofing and trade sales teams.', 'Useful once you''re hiring salespeople and need to train them consistently.', array['Most relevant for owners moving from selling every job themselves to leading a sales team.']::text[], array['roofing', 'siding', 'gutters', 'windows-doors']::text[], 'sales', 'Private community on Skool (join request required). No membership price was shown on its listing when checked.', 'link_only', null, '2026-11-18'::date, 'Name, owner and description read from the community''s public Skool About page. Not signed in; no member content accessed.', 'verified'),
  (md5('academy:resource:skool-roofing-skool')::uuid, 'skool_community', 'Roofing Skool', 'Roman Pearl', null, 'Roofing Skool', 'Skool', 'https://www.skool.com/roofing/about', null, false, null, 'A Skool community for roofers on leads, closing and scaling.', 'Roofing-specific peers for questions general sales communities can''t answer.', array['Compare its advice with your local market and insurance environment.']::text[], array['roofing']::text[], 'sales', 'Private community on Skool (join request required). No membership price was shown on its listing when checked.', 'link_only', null, '2026-11-18'::date, 'Name, owner and description read from the community''s public Skool About page. Not signed in; no member content accessed.', 'verified'),
  (md5('academy:resource:skool-restoration-referral')::uuid, 'skool_community', 'Restoration Referral System', 'Matt Danskin', null, 'Restoration Referral System', 'Skool', 'https://www.skool.com/restoration-referral-system/about', null, false, null, 'A Skool community on building referral partnerships for roofing and restoration contractors.', 'Referral partners (agents, insurers, property managers) can become a steady lead source when handled with integrity.', array['Referral partnerships take consistent follow-up; plan for it.']::text[], array['roofing', 'siding', 'gutters']::text[], 'growth', 'Public community on Skool. No membership price was shown on its listing when checked.', 'link_only', null, '2026-11-18'::date, 'Name, owner and description read from the community''s public Skool About page. Not signed in; no member content accessed.', 'verified'),
  (md5('academy:resource:skool-process-to-profits')::uuid, 'skool_community', 'Process to Profits', 'Chris Vazzana', null, 'Process to Profits', 'Skool', 'https://www.skool.com/process-to-profits-9980/about', null, false, null, 'A Skool community for patio, landscaping and holiday-lighting businesses focused on operations and profit.', 'Landscape and hardscape owners can compare operating systems with peers in the same seasons.', array['Good for seasonal scheduling and crew operations questions.']::text[], array['landscaping', 'concrete', 'masonry', 'fencing']::text[], 'growth', 'Private community on Skool (join request required). No membership price was shown on its listing when checked.', 'link_only', null, '2026-11-18'::date, 'Name, owner and description read from the community''s public Skool About page. Not signed in; no member content accessed.', 'verified'),
  (md5('academy:resource:skool-lawn-care-business-builders')::uuid, 'skool_community', 'Lawn Care Business Builders', 'Stuart Clifford', null, 'Lawn Care Business Builders', 'Skool', 'https://www.skool.com/lawnmowing101/about', null, false, null, 'A Skool community on local search visibility and winning lawn-care clients.', 'Recurring lawn routes depend on steady local leads.', array['Pairs well with the Google Business Profile resource in the Sales Academy.']::text[], array['landscaping']::text[], 'marketing', 'Public community on Skool. No membership price was shown on its listing when checked.', 'link_only', null, '2026-11-18'::date, 'Name, owner and description read from the community''s public Skool About page. Not signed in; no member content accessed.', 'verified'),
  (md5('academy:resource:skool-builders-circle')::uuid, 'skool_community', 'The Builders Circle', 'Preston Bond', null, 'The Builders Circle', 'Skool', 'https://www.skool.com/the-builders-circle/about', null, false, null, 'A Skool business-accelerator community for home remodelers and residential builders.', 'Remodelers selling larger projects can compare sales and marketing approaches with peers.', array['Most relevant for remodelers and residential builders.']::text[], array['kitchens', 'bathrooms', 'interior-remodeling', 'exterior-remodeling', 'additions', 'basements', 'general-contracting']::text[], 'sales', 'Private community on Skool (join request required). No membership price was shown on its listing when checked.', 'link_only', null, '2026-11-18'::date, 'Name, owner and description read from the community''s public Skool About page. Not signed in; no member content accessed.', 'verified'),
  (md5('academy:resource:skool-profitable-handyman')::uuid, 'skool_community', 'The Profitable Handyman Club', 'Jay Seel', null, 'The Profitable Handyman Club', 'Skool', 'https://www.skool.com/the-profitable-handyman-club-8640/about', null, false, null, 'A Skool community about handyman pricing, estimating, overhead and tracking real numbers.', 'Handyman work has many small jobs; pricing each one correctly decides whether the business is profitable.', array['Bring your overhead numbers; pricing advice depends on them.']::text[], array['handyman']::text[], 'estimating', 'Public community on Skool. Its listing describes it as free to join.', 'link_only', null, '2026-11-18'::date, 'Name, owner and description read from the community''s public Skool About page. Not signed in; no member content accessed.', 'verified'),
  (md5('academy:resource:skool-million-dollar-plumber')::uuid, 'skool_community', 'Million Dollar Plumber', 'Richard Behney', null, 'Million Dollar Plumber', 'Skool', 'https://www.skool.com/million-dollar-plumber/about', null, false, null, 'A Skool community for plumbing business owners building a profitable, self-sustaining company.', 'Plumbing-specific peers for service pricing, dispatch and hiring questions.', array['Most relevant for owners stepping back from the tools.']::text[], array['plumbing']::text[], 'growth', 'Private community on Skool (join request required). No membership price was shown on its listing when checked.', 'link_only', null, '2026-11-18'::date, 'Name, owner and description read from the community''s public Skool About page. Not signed in; no member content accessed.', 'verified'),
  (md5('academy:resource:skool-hvac-academy')::uuid, 'skool_community', 'HVAC Academy', 'Shaun Cartwright', null, 'HVAC Academy', 'Skool', 'https://www.skool.com/hvac-academy/about', null, false, null, 'A Skool community sharing business practices for HVAC contractors.', 'HVAC businesses run on maintenance agreements and seasonal demand; peers in the same model help.', array['Useful for maintenance-agreement and seasonal staffing questions.']::text[], array['hvac']::text[], 'growth', 'Private community on Skool (join request required). No membership price was shown on its listing when checked.', 'link_only', null, '2026-11-18'::date, 'Name, owner and description read from the community''s public Skool About page. Not signed in; no member content accessed.', 'verified'),
  (md5('academy:resource:skool-pressure-washing-101')::uuid, 'skool_community', 'PRESSURE WASHING 101', 'Perry Robinson', null, 'PRESSURE WASHING 101', 'Skool', 'https://www.skool.com/pressure-washing-101-2259/about', null, false, null, 'A field-focused Skool community run by working pressure-washing professionals.', 'Practical, in-the-field answers for exterior cleaning businesses.', array['Good for technique and equipment questions alongside business ones.']::text[], array['pressure-washing', 'soft-washing']::text[], 'getting_started', 'Private community on Skool (join request required). No membership price was shown on its listing when checked.', 'link_only', null, '2026-11-18'::date, 'Name, owner and description read from the community''s public Skool About page. Not signed in; no member content accessed.', 'verified'),
  (md5('academy:resource:skool-contractor-ads-university')::uuid, 'skool_community', 'Contractor Ads University', 'Patrick J Phillips', null, 'Contractor Ads University', 'Skool', 'https://www.skool.com/contractoradsu/about', null, false, null, 'A Skool community with advertising and marketing training for home-service contractors.', 'Paid ads can work for contractors, but they need tracking. Learn before you spend.', array['Set a test budget and track cost per booked appointment, not clicks.']::text[], '{}'::text[], 'marketing', 'Private community on Skool (join request required). No membership price was shown on its listing when checked.', 'link_only', null, '2026-11-18'::date, 'Name, owner and description read from the community''s public Skool About page. Not signed in; no member content accessed.', 'verified')
insert into public.academy_courses (id, slug, trade_slug, pillar, title, summary, description, level, access, status, content_class, cover_theme, featured, sort_order, planned_lessons, seo_title, seo_description, published_at) values
  (md5('academy:course:contractor-sales-academy')::uuid, 'contractor-sales-academy', null, 'sales', 'Contractor Sales Academy', 'Twelve practical lessons on winning the right jobs at the right price, from the first call to the referral.', 'A complete, trade-aware sales course for contractors who sell their own work. It follows the real order of a job: getting qualified leads, answering enquiries, running the walk-through, presenting the estimate, handling price objections, following up, closing without pressure, and turning finished jobs into referrals. Each lesson has an original Built2Bid write-up, practical takeaways, a checklist, notes for specific trades, credited expert videos, and a link to the Built2Bid tool that puts the lesson into practice.', 'beginner', 'public', 'published', 'mixed', 'cyan', true, 0, '{}'::text[], 'Contractor Sales Training: Free 12-Lesson Course', 'Free contractor sales course: finding leads, discovery, presenting estimates, price objections, follow-up, closing and referrals, with trade-specific examples.', now()),
  (md5('academy:course:roofing-getting-started')::uuid, 'roofing-getting-started', 'roofing', 'getting_started', 'Starting a Roofing Company: Licensing, Insurance and Bonding', 'Business basics for a roofing company, including licensing, liability insurance and when bonds are requested.', 'Roofing carries serious liability from falls, weather exposure, and damage to the property below. This course covers entity setup, workers'' comp and general liability coverage, and when customers or agencies ask for bonds. Licensing and bonding requirements vary by state and locality; confirm them with your licensing board and insurance agent before bidding.', 'beginner', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'slate', false, 10, array['Choosing a business structure for a roofing company', 'Contractor licensing requirements by state', 'General liability and workers'' comp basics', 'Bonding: when customers and agencies ask for it', 'Setting a service area and crew roles']::text[], 'Starting a Roofing Company: Licensing, Insurance and Bonding', 'Business basics for a roofing company, including licensing, liability insurance and when bonds are requested.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:roofing-sales')::uuid, 'roofing-sales', 'roofing', 'sales', 'Selling Roof Replacements When the Roof Looks Fine', 'Use inspection photos and a plain condition report so homeowners understand the scope before comparing prices.', 'Many homeowners say the roof looks fine from the ground, and some ask whether insurance or a deductible will cover the job. This course covers inspection photos, explaining repair versus replacement without pressure, and following up on storm and inspection leads. Insurance coverage depends on the policy and state; refer homeowners to their insurer for coverage questions.', 'intermediate', 'public', 'published', 'mixed', 'cyan', false, 20, array['Inspection photos that show condition clearly', 'Explaining repair versus replacement in plain terms', 'Handling the ''my roof is fine'' objection', 'Working with insurance adjusters without overpromising', 'Following up on storm and inspection leads']::text[], 'Selling Roof Replacements When the Roof Looks Fine', 'Use inspection photos and a plain condition report so homeowners understand the scope before comparing prices.', now()),
  (md5('academy:course:roofing-estimating')::uuid, 'roofing-estimating', 'roofing', 'estimating', 'Roofing Estimates by the Square: Tear-Off, Underlayment and Flashing', 'Build a roof bid from measured squares, pitch, layers, underlayment, flashing and ventilation so nothing is missed.', 'Roof area is measured in squares, and pitch, number of layers, valleys, penetrations and ventilation all change labor and materials. This course walks through a full takeoff, waste factors for hips and valleys, and pricing for disposal and dumpsters. Pricing decisions are yours; check local rules on debris disposal and permits.', 'intermediate', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'navy', false, 30, array['Measuring squares, pitch and roof plane area', 'Waste factors for hips, valleys and cut-up roofs', 'Tear-off, disposal and dumpster line items', 'Flashing, pipe boots and ventilation pricing', 'Pricing steep roofs and multi-story access']::text[], null, 'Build a roof bid from measured squares, pitch, layers, underlayment, flashing and ventilation so nothing is missed.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:roofing-project-management')::uuid, 'roofing-project-management', 'roofing', 'project_management', 'Scheduling Roof Jobs Around Weather, Crews and Material Drops', 'Plan tear-off days, deliveries, dumpster placement and inspections so a roof goes on without losing crew days to rain.', 'Roof work depends on dry weather, dumpster placement, material delivery timing, and inspection windows, and one missed day can ripple through the calendar. This course covers daily start plans, protecting driveways and landscaping, and keeping homeowners updated when weather moves the schedule. Inspection requirements vary by locality; confirm the steps before you book the crew.', 'intermediate', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'green', false, 40, array['Weather windows and rain-day decisions', 'Staging materials and dumpster placement', 'Coordinating gutter and ridge vent subs', 'Daily tarping, cleanup and magnetic sweeps', 'Homeowner updates when the schedule changes']::text[], null, 'Plan tear-off days, deliveries, dumpster placement and inspections so a roof goes on without losing crew days to rain.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:roofing-accounting')::uuid, 'roofing-accounting', 'roofing', 'accounting', 'Job Costing for Roofing: Labor, Materials and Dump Fees', 'Track each roof''s labor, material, disposal and equipment costs so you know what a job actually earned.', 'Roofing margins are often eaten by tear-off labor overruns, rework, returned materials, and dump fees that were not billed. This course shows how to set job cost codes, track crew hours by roof, and compare actual cost against the bid. Tax treatment of materials and labor varies by state; confirm details with your accountant.', 'intermediate', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'amber', false, 50, array['Setting job cost codes for each roof phase', 'Tracking crew hours and daily production', 'Recording dump fees and material returns', 'Comparing actual cost to the bid', 'Deposits and progress billing on roof jobs']::text[], 'Job Costing for Roofing: Labor, Materials and Dump Fees', 'Track each roof''s labor, material, disposal and equipment costs so you know what a job actually earned.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:roofing-hr')::uuid, 'roofing-hr', 'roofing', 'hr', 'Hiring and Training a Roofing Crew You Can Trust', 'Hire for reliability and ladder discipline, then train each person for tear-off, install or cleanup work.', 'A roofing crew is only as productive as its least careful ladder climber, and turnover makes schedules and quality harder to hold. This course covers recruiting laborers and installers, defining tear-off, install and cleanup roles, and training new hires in safe material handling. Wage, classification and overtime rules vary by state; confirm them with your accountant or an employment attorney.', 'beginner', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'rose', false, 60, array['Writing job posts for roofing laborers and installers', 'Defining tear-off, install and cleanup roles', 'Training new hires on material hoisting', 'Pay structure and worker classification basics', 'Keeping a crew through the slow season']::text[], 'Hiring and Training a Roofing Crew You Can Trust', 'Hire for reliability and ladder discipline, then train each person for tear-off, install or cleanup work.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:roofing-growth')::uuid, 'roofing-growth', 'roofing', 'growth', 'Building Repeat and Referral Work from Roof Replacements', 'Turn each roof into referrals, maintenance inspections and repeat work from neighbors and property managers.', 'Roofing is a large, infrequent purchase, so steady work comes from referrals, neighborhood jobs after a storm, and property managers who need routine repairs. This course covers post-job check-ins, annual inspection offers, and building relationships with property managers and HOA boards. Solicitation and advertising rules vary by locality.', 'intermediate', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'cyan', false, 70, array['Post-job check-ins that generate referrals', 'Neighborhood follow-up after a nearby install', 'Annual roof inspection and maintenance offers', 'Working with property managers and HOA boards', 'Tracking where your leads come from']::text[], 'Building Repeat and Referral Work from Roof Replacements', 'Turn each roof into referrals, maintenance inspections and repeat work from neighbors and property managers.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:roofing-safety')::uuid, 'roofing-safety', 'roofing', 'safety', 'Fall Protection, Ladders and Roof-Edge Safety', 'Fall protection, ladder setup, roof-edge work and hot-material safety for crews on steep and low-slope roofs.', 'Falls from roofs are among the most serious hazards in the trade, and hot materials, nail guns, and unstable decking add risk. This course covers ladder setup, guardrails and personal fall arrest systems, plus safe tear-off practices around skylights and openings. Fall protection and training requirements vary by state and locality; confirm the rules that apply to your jobs.', 'advanced', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'slate', false, 80, array['Choosing guardrails, nets or personal fall arrest', 'Ladder setup, extension and access rules', 'Roof-edge and skylight hazards during tear-off', 'Hot materials, tar and heat-related safety', 'Documenting safety training and toolbox talks']::text[], 'Fall Protection, Ladders and Roof-Edge Safety', 'Fall protection, ladder setup, roof-edge work and hot-material safety for crews on steep and low-slope roofs.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:siding-getting-started')::uuid, 'siding-getting-started', 'siding', 'getting_started', 'Starting a Siding Company: Licensing, Insurance and Warranties', 'Business basics for a siding company, including licensing, insurance and how manufacturer warranty rules shape your scope.', 'Siding work touches exterior walls, weather barriers, and occupied homes, so insurance and licensing matter from the first bid. This course covers business setup, manufacturer installer programs, and how warranty registration rules affect what you include in a quote. Licensing and home improvement contract rules vary by state; confirm them with your licensing board.', 'beginner', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'slate', false, 10, array['Entity setup and tax registration basics', 'Contractor licensing and home improvement contracts', 'General liability and workers'' comp for exterior crews', 'Manufacturer installer programs and warranty rules', 'Defining your service area and crew size']::text[], null, 'Business basics for a siding company, including licensing, insurance and how manufacturer warranty rules shape your scope.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:siding-sales')::uuid, 'siding-sales', 'siding', 'sales', 'Selling Siding Packages with Clear Trim and Wrap Lines', 'Show what the package includes, from house wrap and trim to flashing and disposal, so bids compare fairly.', 'Siding bids often look far apart because one includes house wrap, trim, and disposal and another does not. This course covers presenting a single package with clear sections, using samples and photos, and explaining color, profile, and trim options. Warranty terms should be written into the proposal; confirm what your suppliers allow you to offer.', 'intermediate', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'cyan', false, 20, array['Presenting a package with trim, wrap and disposal', 'Walking homeowners through color and profile samples', 'Answering the ''why is this higher'' question', 'Handling storm-damage and insurance questions', 'Writing proposals that match the walk-through']::text[], 'Selling Siding Packages with Clear Trim and Wrap Lines', 'Show what the package includes, from house wrap and trim to flashing and disposal, so bids compare fairly.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:siding-estimating')::uuid, 'siding-estimating', 'siding', 'estimating', 'Siding Takeoffs: Squares, Trim Footage and Accessories', 'Measure wall area, openings, corners and trim footage so the bid carries every accessory and waste factor.', 'Siding estimates depend on net wall area after windows and doors, corner and J-channel footage, soffit and fascia, and waste that climbs on complex elevations. This course covers measuring gables and openings, building a takeoff sheet by elevation, and pricing removal and substrate repair. Material prices change by supplier and region; verify them before you bid.', 'intermediate', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'navy', false, 30, array['Net wall area after windows and doors', 'Gables, corners and J-channel footage', 'Soffit, fascia and trim takeoff', 'Waste factors for complex elevations', 'Pricing removal, disposal and substrate repair']::text[], 'Siding Takeoffs: Squares, Trim Footage and Accessories', 'Measure wall area, openings, corners and trim footage so the bid carries every accessory and waste factor.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:siding-project-management')::uuid, 'siding-project-management', 'siding', 'project_management', 'Sequencing Siding Crews Around Weather and Trim Work', 'Plan removal, wrap, panel and trim sequences so each elevation is weathertight before the next rain.', 'Siding work exposes the house to weather, so each day''s wrap and panel installation has to close the wall before the crew leaves. This course covers sequencing by elevation, coordinating window and gutter installers, and managing dumpsters and material staging on tight lots. Permit and inspection requirements vary by locality; confirm them before scheduling.', 'intermediate', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'green', false, 40, array['Sequencing elevations to stay weathertight', 'Coordinating window, gutter and roofing subs', 'Material staging on tight lots', 'Weather delays and homeowner communication', 'Daily cleanup and magnetic debris sweeps']::text[], 'Sequencing Siding Crews Around Weather and Trim Work', 'Plan removal, wrap, panel and trim sequences so each elevation is weathertight before the next rain.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:siding-accounting')::uuid, 'siding-accounting', 'siding', 'accounting', 'Job Costing Siding Jobs by Elevation and Crew Hours', 'Track labor and material by elevation so you can see which kinds of siding jobs earn their keep.', 'Siding margins shift with waste on complex elevations, rot discovered under old siding, and crew hours spent on trim details. This course covers cost codes by phase, tracking hours by elevation, and recording change orders for hidden damage. Tax treatment of materials and subcontracts varies by state; confirm it with your accountant.', 'intermediate', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'amber', false, 50, array['Cost codes by phase: removal, wrap, install, trim', 'Tracking crew hours by elevation', 'Recording hidden rot and change orders', 'Comparing estimated and actual waste', 'Progress billing and deposits for siding jobs']::text[], 'Job Costing Siding Jobs by Elevation and Crew Hours', 'Track labor and material by elevation so you can see which kinds of siding jobs earn their keep.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:siding-hr')::uuid, 'siding-hr', 'siding', 'hr', 'Training Siding Installers for Consistent Trim and Flashing', 'Build installer skills for square corners, flashing order and trim joints so every elevation looks finished.', 'Siding quality shows at corners, window heads, and where trim meets the wall, and those details depend on installer habits. This course covers training a crew on flashing order, panel cutting and fastening, and a quality check before the crew leaves each day. Wage classification and overtime rules vary by state; confirm them with your accountant.', 'beginner', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'rose', false, 60, array['Flashing order at windows and doors', 'Cutting, expansion gaps and fastening panels', 'Corner and trim joint quality standards', 'Pairing new installers with experienced leads', 'Keeping installers between seasons']::text[], 'Training Siding Installers for Consistent Trim and Flashing', 'Build installer skills for square corners, flashing order and trim joints so every elevation looks finished.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:siding-growth')::uuid, 'siding-growth', 'siding', 'growth', 'Turning Siding Jobs into Referrals and Neighborhood Work', 'Use finished homes, before-and-after photos and neighborhood follow-up to build repeat and referral business.', 'Siding is a highly visible upgrade, so a finished house on a street is often the best advertisement a siding company has. This course covers documenting finished work with homeowner permission, neighborhood follow-up after an install, and working as a sub for remodelers and restoration companies. Marketing and door-to-door solicitation rules vary by locality.', 'intermediate', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'cyan', false, 70, array['Documenting finished work with permission', 'Neighborhood follow-up after a nearby install', 'Working as a sub for remodelers and builders', 'Storm-response planning and restoration partners', 'Asking for reviews and referrals at the right time']::text[], 'Turning Siding Jobs into Referrals and Neighborhood Work', 'Use finished homes, before-and-after photos and neighborhood follow-up to build repeat and referral business.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:siding-safety')::uuid, 'siding-safety', 'siding', 'safety', 'Ladder, Scaffold and Wall-Edge Safety for Siding Crews', 'Ladder and scaffold setup, fall hazards on two-story walls, and safe handling of long panels in wind.', 'Siding crews spend long hours on ladders and scaffolds, often handling long panels that catch wind and work near overhead power lines. This course covers scaffold setup and inspection, fall protection where required, and clearance from electrical lines. Scaffolding, fall protection and lead-paint precautions vary by state and locality; confirm the requirements that apply to your jobs.', 'advanced', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'slate', false, 80, array['Ladder and scaffold setup and inspection', 'Fall protection on two-story walls', 'Overhead power line clearance', 'Handling long panels in wind', 'Lead-paint precautions on older homes']::text[], 'Ladder, Scaffold and Wall-Edge Safety for Siding Crews', 'Ladder and scaffold setup, fall hazards on two-story walls, and safe handling of long panels in wind.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:decks-getting-started')::uuid, 'decks-getting-started', 'decks', 'getting_started', 'Starting a Deck and Porch Business: Permits and Insurance', 'Set up a deck and porch company with the licensing, permit and insurance basics that apply to elevated structures.', 'Decks and porches are elevated structures, so permits and inspections usually apply and falls are a real risk. This course covers business setup, how permits are typically pulled for footings and framing, and insurance for structural work. Permit rules and contractor licensing vary by locality; confirm them with your building department before quoting.', 'beginner', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'slate', false, 10, array['Business setup and tax registration', 'Permits for footings, framing and ledgers', 'Contractor licensing for structural work', 'Insurance for elevated and structural work', 'Building department relationships and inspections']::text[], 'Starting a Deck and Porch Business: Permits and Insurance', 'Set up a deck and porch company with the licensing, permit and insurance basics that apply to elevated structures.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:decks-sales')::uuid, 'decks-sales', 'decks', 'sales', 'Selling Deck Options Without Overwhelming Homeowners', 'Present decking, railing and stair options side by side so the homeowner can choose with confidence.', 'Homeowners weigh composite against pressure-treated wood, aluminum against wood railings, and a covered porch against an open deck. This course covers presenting two or three good options with clear price and maintenance differences, and site visits that surface grade, access, and sun exposure, all of which change the bid. Product warranties vary by manufacturer; state terms in writing.', 'intermediate', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'cyan', false, 20, array['Comparing composite and pressure-treated decking', 'Railing options and sightline tradeoffs', 'Site visit checklist: grade, access and sun', 'Presenting a covered porch versus an open deck', 'Writing a proposal that matches the design']::text[], 'Selling Deck Options Without Overwhelming Homeowners', 'Present decking, railing and stair options side by side so the homeowner can choose with confidence.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:decks-estimating')::uuid, 'decks-estimating', 'decks', 'estimating', 'Deck Estimates: Footings, Framing, Decking and Hardware', 'Build deck pricing from footing count, joist layout, decking square footage, stairs and every connector.', 'Deck pricing starts with footing count and depth, then flows through beams, joists, decking area, and stair stringers. Connectors such as joist hangers, post bases, and fasteners add up quickly and are easy to leave off a bid. This course covers takeoff by system, waste on picture-frame borders, and pricing for excavation and disposal; verify material prices before quoting.', 'intermediate', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'navy', false, 30, array['Footing count, depth and layout takeoff', 'Beam, joist and post sizing from engineered plans', 'Decking square footage and picture-frame waste', 'Stair stringers, landings and railing footage', 'Hardware, fasteners and connector counts']::text[], 'Deck Estimates: Footings, Framing, Decking and Hardware', 'Build deck pricing from footing count, joist layout, decking square footage, stairs and every connector.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:decks-project-management')::uuid, 'decks-project-management', 'decks', 'project_management', 'Scheduling Deck Builds Around Footing Inspections and Curing', 'Sequence footing inspections, concrete set time, framing and decking so the crew never waits on a sign-off.', 'A deck build usually pauses for footing and framing inspections, and footings need time to set before framing starts. This course covers sequencing dig, footing pour, inspection, framing and decking, plus scheduling stain or sealer once the wood has dried. Inspection steps and hold points vary by locality; confirm them early.', 'intermediate', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'green', false, 40, array['Footing layout and utility locate timing', 'Sequencing footings, inspection and framing', 'Ledger attachment and inspection hold points', 'Decking, railing and stair sequence', 'Scheduling stain or sealer after wood dries']::text[], 'Scheduling Deck Builds Around Footing Inspections and Curing', 'Sequence footing inspections, concrete set time, framing and decking so the crew never waits on a sign-off.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:decks-accounting')::uuid, 'decks-accounting', 'decks', 'accounting', 'Tracking Deck Job Costs: Hardware, Lumber and Railing', 'Keep material, hardware and subcontract costs organized by deck phase so you can tell which jobs made money.', 'Deck jobs carry many small hardware costs, and lumber prices can move between estimating and purchase. This course shows how to set phase cost codes, record lumber overages and returns, and track railing or stair subcontracts separately. Sales tax on materials varies by state; confirm treatment with your accountant.', 'intermediate', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'amber', false, 50, array['Phase cost codes: footings, framing, decking, rails', 'Recording lumber overages and returns', 'Tracking hardware as its own line', 'Subcontract costs for railing or stairs', 'Deposits and progress billing on deck jobs']::text[], 'Tracking Deck Job Costs: Hardware, Lumber and Railing', 'Keep material, hardware and subcontract costs organized by deck phase so you can tell which jobs made money.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:decks-hr')::uuid, 'decks-hr', 'decks', 'hr', 'Hiring Carpenters for Deck and Porch Crews', 'Hire and train carpenters who can lay out footings, set posts and flash ledgers accurately.', 'Deck work depends on accurate layout, plumb posts, and a properly flashed ledger, and those skills take time to develop. This course covers interviewing for layout and framing skill, training helpers on square and plumb checks, and building a crew that handles both wood and composite materials. Wage and classification rules vary by state; confirm them with your accountant.', 'beginner', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'rose', false, 60, array['Interviewing for layout and framing skill', 'Training helpers on square, plumb and level', 'Ledger and post installation standards', 'Handling composite and treated material', 'Keeping a crew busy between projects']::text[], 'Hiring Carpenters for Deck and Porch Crews', 'Hire and train carpenters who can lay out footings, set posts and flash ledgers accurately.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:decks-growth')::uuid, 'decks-growth', 'decks', 'growth', 'Building Maintenance and Repeat Work from Deck Owners', 'Offer cleaning, staining, railing repair and inspections to past deck customers each season.', 'Decks need periodic cleaning, sealing, board replacement, and railing tightening, which gives a deck company steady work after the build. This course covers seasonal maintenance packages, reminder timing for stain and sealer, and referral requests from satisfied homeowners. Solicitation and advertising rules vary by locality.', 'intermediate', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'cyan', false, 70, array['Seasonal maintenance packages for deck owners', 'Reminders for cleaning, sealing and staining', 'Post-build check-in and punch list', 'Referrals from landscapers and neighbors', 'Tracking repeat work in your customer list']::text[], 'Building Maintenance and Repeat Work from Deck Owners', 'Offer cleaning, staining, railing repair and inspections to past deck customers each season.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:decks-safety')::uuid, 'decks-safety', 'decks', 'safety', 'Fall Protection and Edge Safety During Deck Builds', 'Edge and opening fall protection, ladder use, and safe handling of posts, beams and railing sections.', 'Deck crews work at height around open framing and unfinished edges, and heavy beams can shift during setting. This course covers temporary guardrails, lifting beams safely with a crew, and fall protection near stair openings. Fall protection and temporary guardrail requirements vary by state and locality; confirm the rules for your jobs.', 'advanced', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'slate', false, 80, array['Temporary guardrails around open deck edges', 'Lifting and setting beams safely', 'Ladder use on framed decks', 'Fall protection near stair openings', 'Sawdust and cutting safety for treated lumber']::text[], 'Fall Protection and Edge Safety During Deck Builds', 'Edge and opening fall protection, ladder use, and safe handling of posts, beams and railing sections.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:concrete-getting-started')::uuid, 'concrete-getting-started', 'concrete', 'getting_started', 'Starting a Concrete Business: Licensing, Insurance and Permits', 'Business basics for a concrete company, including licensing, liability coverage and pour-related permits.', 'Concrete work involves heavy equipment, wet material, and public sidewalks or driveways that can create liability. This course covers entity setup, contractor licensing, general liability coverage, and when permits or right-of-way approvals apply to your jobs. Licensing and permit rules vary by state and locality; confirm them with your licensing board and local building department.', 'beginner', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'slate', false, 10, array['Entity setup and tax registration basics', 'Contractor licensing and classifications', 'General liability and equipment coverage', 'Permits and right-of-way for sidewalks and drives', 'Defining your service area and crew size']::text[], null, 'Business basics for a concrete company, including licensing, liability coverage and pour-related permits.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:concrete-sales')::uuid, 'concrete-sales', 'concrete', 'sales', 'Winning Concrete Bids Against Lower Competitors', 'Compare scopes line by line so a lower bid is seen for what it leaves out: base depth, mesh, joints or finish.', 'Customers often compare concrete bids by price per square foot without checking base depth, reinforcement, joint layout, or finish. This course covers writing scopes that list thickness, mesh or rebar, base material, and finish type, plus site visits that surface drainage and access issues. Explain your scope in writing so the comparison is fair.', 'intermediate', 'public', 'published', 'mixed', 'cyan', false, 20, array['Writing scopes with thickness and base depth', 'Explaining mesh, rebar and joint layout', 'Site visits: drainage, access and slope', 'Responding to a lower competing bid', 'Offering finish options with clear pricing']::text[], 'Winning Concrete Bids Against Lower Competitors', 'Compare scopes line by line so a lower bid is seen for what it leaves out: base depth, mesh, joints or finish.', now()),
  (md5('academy:course:concrete-estimating')::uuid, 'concrete-estimating', 'concrete', 'estimating', 'Concrete Estimating: Yardage, Forming, Finishing and Labor', 'Calculate cubic yards, forms, reinforcement, finish labor and base material for flatwork and structural pours.', 'Concrete estimates start with cubic yards from length, width, and thickness, then add waste, base material, forms, and reinforcement. Finishing labor changes with the finish type, pour size, and access, and pump or truck fees can dominate small jobs. This course covers yardage calculations, form takeoffs, and a finishing labor allowance that matches the pour.', 'intermediate', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'navy', false, 30, array['Cubic yards from thickness and waste factors', 'Form, stake and keyway takeoff', 'Mesh and rebar quantities and placement', 'Finishing labor by finish type and pour size', 'Pump, truck and short-load fees']::text[], 'Concrete Estimating: Yardage, Forming, Finishing and Labor', 'Calculate cubic yards, forms, reinforcement, finish labor and base material for flatwork and structural pours.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:concrete-project-management')::uuid, 'concrete-project-management', 'concrete', 'project_management', 'Pour-Day Scheduling: Ready-Mix Timing, Crews and Weather', 'Coordinate ready-mix deliveries, finishing crews, inspections and cure time so each pour starts and ends on plan.', 'Ready-mix trucks arrive on a clock, and hot, cold, or windy days change set time and finish windows. This course covers scheduling pours with the batch plant, lining up finishing crews and pump operators, and planning forms and inspections ahead of delivery. Cure and cold-weather requirements vary by locality and specification; confirm them with your engineer or supplier.', 'intermediate', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'green', false, 40, array['Coordinating ready-mix delivery windows', 'Finishing crew size for the pour', 'Inspections and forms before the truck arrives', 'Hot, cold and windy weather pour decisions', 'Cure, protection and backfill timing']::text[], 'Pour-Day Scheduling: Ready-Mix Timing, Crews and Weather', 'Coordinate ready-mix deliveries, finishing crews, inspections and cure time so each pour starts and ends on plan.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:concrete-accounting')::uuid, 'concrete-accounting', 'concrete', 'accounting', 'Concrete Job Costing: Yardage Overruns, Pumps and Waste', 'Track actual yards, pump and truck charges, and finishing hours so you can compare each pour against the bid.', 'Concrete margins move with yardage overruns, returned loads, pump minimums, and finishing hours that run longer than planned. This course shows how to record ticket yardage against the estimate, track finishing labor by pour, and bill changes such as extra base or unplanned access. Tax treatment of materials and subcontracts varies by state; confirm details with your accountant.', 'intermediate', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'amber', false, 50, array['Matching ready-mix tickets to the estimate', 'Tracking finishing hours by pour', 'Billing for extra base and access changes', 'Pump minimums and short-load charges', 'Deposits and progress billing on flatwork']::text[], 'Concrete Job Costing: Yardage Overruns, Pumps and Waste', 'Track actual yards, pump and truck charges, and finishing hours so you can compare each pour against the bid.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:concrete-hr')::uuid, 'concrete-hr', 'concrete', 'hr', 'Building a Concrete Finishing Crew That Stays Reliable', 'Hire and train finishers and laborers who can work fast, keep pace with the truck and hold a clean edge.', 'Concrete finishing is physical and time-sensitive, and a crew that is short one person can cost a whole pour. This course covers recruiting laborers and finishers, defining roles for screeding, bull floating, edging, and troweling, and training on joint placement and finish timing. Wage and overtime rules vary by state; confirm them with your accountant.', 'beginner', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'rose', false, 60, array['Recruiting laborers and finishers', 'Roles for screeding, floating and edging', 'Training on joint placement and finish timing', 'Pacing a crew with the ready-mix truck', 'Keeping finishers through the slow months']::text[], 'Building a Concrete Finishing Crew That Stays Reliable', 'Hire and train finishers and laborers who can work fast, keep pace with the truck and hold a clean edge.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:concrete-growth')::uuid, 'concrete-growth', 'concrete', 'growth', 'Repeat Concrete Work: Driveways, Patios and Commercial Flatwork', 'Build repeat business with homeowners, builders and property managers who need flatwork and repairs.', 'Concrete customers often need more work later, such as a patio after a driveway or repairs to a sidewalk after a utility dig. This course covers follow-up on finished pours, building relationships with builders and property managers, and offering repair and sealing work as a steady service. Solicitation and advertising rules vary by locality.', 'intermediate', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'cyan', false, 70, array['Follow-up after a driveway or patio pour', 'Working with builders on recurring flatwork', 'Repair and resealing as repeat service', 'Property manager relationships and bid lists', 'Asking for referrals from finished customers']::text[], null, 'Build repeat business with homeowners, builders and property managers who need flatwork and repairs.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:concrete-safety')::uuid, 'concrete-safety', 'concrete', 'safety', 'Concrete Safety: Chutes, Wet Cement Burns and Equipment', 'Protect crews from wet cement skin injuries, chute and pump hazards, and heavy equipment during pours.', 'Wet concrete can cause skin burns and eye injuries, and pumps, chutes, and vibrators add hazards that multiply on busy pour days. This course covers protective gear for wet material, safe chute and pump handling, and traffic control around trucks and excavation. Safety rules and training requirements vary by state and locality; confirm the requirements that apply to your jobs.', 'advanced', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'slate', false, 80, array['Protective gear for wet concrete', 'Chute, pump and hose handling', 'Traffic control around trucks and excavations', 'Vibrator and power trowel safety', 'Quality checks on rebar and form stability']::text[], 'Concrete Safety: Chutes, Wet Cement Burns and Equipment', 'Protect crews from wet cement skin injuries, chute and pump hazards, and heavy equipment during pours.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:kitchens-getting-started')::uuid, 'kitchens-getting-started', 'kitchens', 'getting_started', 'Starting a Kitchen Remodeling Company: Licensing and Insurance', 'Business basics for a kitchen remodeling company, including licensing, insurance and the trades you can self-perform.', 'Kitchens involve plumbing, electrical, and structural changes, so licensing and insurance requirements often depend on which trades you perform. This course covers business setup, deciding which work you self-perform and which you subcontract, and insurance for remodel work in occupied homes. Licensing scope and home improvement contract rules vary by state; confirm them with your licensing board.', 'beginner', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'slate', false, 10, array['Entity setup and tax registration basics', 'Which trades you self-perform versus sub', 'Contractor licensing and home improvement contracts', 'Liability coverage for occupied-home remodels', 'Choosing a service area and project size']::text[], null, 'Business basics for a kitchen remodeling company, including licensing, insurance and the trades you can self-perform.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:kitchens-sales')::uuid, 'kitchens-sales', 'kitchens', 'sales', 'Presenting Kitchen Designs with One Clear Total', 'Organize proposals by scope section so the homeowner sees cabinets, counters, trades and finishes in one clear package.', 'Kitchen clients fall for the design first, and then react to the total when plumbing, electrical, and finishes are added. This course covers presenting the design in scope sections, showing alternates for cabinets and counters, and walking the client through what each option changes in price. Design presentation tools and product choices are yours; warranty terms should be written into the contract.', 'intermediate', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'cyan', false, 20, array['Organizing proposals into scope sections', 'Presenting alternates for cabinets and counters', 'Showing what each finish option changes in price', 'Handling the ''what can we cut'' conversation', 'Confirming selections before ordering']::text[], 'Presenting Kitchen Designs with One Clear Total', 'Organize proposals by scope section so the homeowner sees cabinets, counters, trades and finishes in one clear package.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:kitchens-estimating')::uuid, 'kitchens-estimating', 'kitchens', 'estimating', 'Kitchen Estimates: Cabinets, Counters, Plumbing and Electrical', 'Build a kitchen estimate from separate trade sections, with allowances, selections and rough-in costs shown clearly.', 'Kitchen estimates combine cabinet linear footage, countertop square footage, plumbing and electrical rough-in, flooring, and finish allowances. Missing rough-in work or selection allowances is a common reason kitchen bids lose money. This course covers building the takeoff by section, setting allowances for selections, and pricing demolition and protection of finished spaces.', 'intermediate', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'navy', false, 30, array['Cabinet linear footage and fillers', 'Countertop templates and square footage', 'Plumbing and electrical rough-in sections', 'Allowances for fixtures and finishes', 'Demolition, protection and disposal pricing']::text[], null, 'Build a kitchen estimate from separate trade sections, with allowances, selections and rough-in costs shown clearly.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:kitchens-project-management')::uuid, 'kitchens-project-management', 'kitchens', 'project_management', 'Sequencing a Kitchen Remodel Across Trades and Deliveries', 'Coordinate demolition, rough-ins, inspections, cabinets, counters and finish work in the right order.', 'A kitchen remodel depends on trade order: rough-in plumbing and electrical must pass inspection before walls close, and countertops are templated only after cabinets are set. This course covers sequencing rough-ins, scheduling counter templates and fabrication lead times, and planning around the homeowner''s daily kitchen use. Inspection requirements vary by locality; confirm steps early.', 'intermediate', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'green', false, 40, array['Sequencing rough-in, inspection and close-up', 'Scheduling cabinet and counter lead times', 'Countertop templating and install timing', 'Keeping a working kitchen during the job', 'Managing selections and change orders']::text[], 'Sequencing a Kitchen Remodel Across Trades and Deliveries', 'Coordinate demolition, rough-ins, inspections, cabinets, counters and finish work in the right order.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:kitchens-accounting')::uuid, 'kitchens-accounting', 'kitchens', 'accounting', 'Kitchen Job Costing Across Multiple Trades', 'Track costs by scope section so you can see whether cabinets, trades or finish work drove any margin change.', 'Kitchen jobs mix many trades, so a margin problem in one section can be hidden inside a total. This course covers cost codes by section, tracking subcontractor invoices against scope, and recording change orders for selections, hidden conditions and added work. Tax treatment of materials, subcontracts and deposits varies by state; confirm details with your accountant.', 'intermediate', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'amber', false, 50, array['Cost codes by scope section', 'Tracking subcontractor invoices against scope', 'Recording selection and change orders', 'Deposits and progress billing for kitchens', 'Reviewing margin by section after each job']::text[], 'Kitchen Job Costing Across Multiple Trades', 'Track costs by scope section so you can see whether cabinets, trades or finish work drove any margin change.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:kitchens-hr')::uuid, 'kitchens-hr', 'kitchens', 'hr', 'Building a Kitchen Remodel Crew with Clear Roles', 'Hire carpenters and helpers who can work in occupied homes, protect finished surfaces and keep the job clean.', 'Kitchen crews work in tight, occupied spaces, where dust, scratches, and schedule slips frustrate homeowners. This course covers hiring carpenters and helpers, defining roles for demolition, carpentry and finish work, and training on protection and cleanliness standards. Wage and classification rules vary by state; confirm them with your accountant.', 'beginner', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'rose', false, 60, array['Hiring carpenters and helpers for remodels', 'Roles for demo, carpentry and finish work', 'Protection standards for occupied homes', 'Training on cabinet and counter handling', 'Retaining carpenters through slow periods']::text[], 'Building a Kitchen Remodel Crew with Clear Roles', 'Hire carpenters and helpers who can work in occupied homes, protect finished surfaces and keep the job clean.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:kitchens-growth')::uuid, 'kitchens-growth', 'kitchens', 'growth', 'Repeat and Referral Work After a Kitchen Remodel', 'Use a finished kitchen, photos and a clean punch list to win referrals, bathroom work and additional projects.', 'Kitchen clients are often ready for the next room and are happy to refer friends after a clean finish. This course covers a punch list and walkthrough that closes the job well, documenting finished work with the client''s permission, and asking for referrals and reviews at the right time. Marketing and advertising rules vary by locality.', 'intermediate', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'cyan', false, 70, array['Final walkthrough and punch list process', 'Documenting finished work with permission', 'Asking for referrals after the final walkthrough', 'Follow-up for the next room or project', 'Working with designers and real estate referral sources']::text[], 'Repeat and Referral Work After a Kitchen Remodel', 'Use a finished kitchen, photos and a clean punch list to win referrals, bathroom work and additional projects.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:kitchens-safety')::uuid, 'kitchens-safety', 'kitchens', 'safety', 'Kitchen Remodel Safety: Dust, Cutting and Live Circuits', 'Control dust, manage tool and cutting hazards, and keep workers away from live circuits during demolition.', 'Kitchen demolition creates dust, sharp edges, and hidden hazards such as live wiring and old plumbing lines. This course covers containing dust and protecting occupants, de-energizing circuits before work, and safe handling of countertops and heavy cabinets. Requirements for dust control and lead or asbestos checks vary by state and locality; confirm them before demolition.', 'advanced', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'slate', false, 80, array['Dust containment and occupant protection', 'Lock-out and de-energizing before demolition', 'Handling heavy cabinets and stone counters', 'Checking older homes for lead and asbestos', 'Hidden hazards behind walls and under floors']::text[], 'Kitchen Remodel Safety: Dust, Cutting and Live Circuits', 'Control dust, manage tool and cutting hazards, and keep workers away from live circuits during demolition.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:bathrooms-getting-started')::uuid, 'bathrooms-getting-started', 'bathrooms', 'getting_started', 'Starting a Bathroom Remodeling Business: Licensing and Insurance', 'Business basics for a bath remodeling company, including licensing, insurance and plumbing permit coordination.', 'Bathroom remodels combine demolition, plumbing, electrical, and waterproofing in small, occupied spaces. This course covers business setup, licensing scope for plumbing and electrical work, and insurance for remodels in occupied homes. Licensing and permit rules vary by state and locality; confirm them with your licensing board before bidding plumbing or electrical scope.', 'beginner', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'slate', false, 10, array['Entity setup and tax registration basics', 'Licensing scope for plumbing and electrical work', 'Insurance for occupied-home bath remodels', 'Permits for plumbing moves and vent changes', 'Choosing which trades you self-perform']::text[], null, 'Business basics for a bath remodeling company, including licensing, insurance and plumbing permit coordination.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:bathrooms-sales')::uuid, 'bathrooms-sales', 'bathrooms', 'sales', 'Selling Tub-to-Shower Conversions and Full Bath Remodels', 'Show what sits behind the tile, from blocking and waterproofing to drain changes, so the price is understood.', 'Homeowners often picture the finished tile and fixtures, not the blocking, waterproofing, drain relocation, and pressure-balance valve work behind them. This course covers site walkthroughs that find hidden conditions, presenting tub-to-shower and full remodel options side by side, and writing fixture and tile selections into the contract. Product warranties and manufacturer terms vary; state them in writing.', 'intermediate', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'cyan', false, 20, array['What sits behind a finished shower wall', 'Presenting tub-to-shower versus full remodel', 'Fixture and tile selections in the contract', 'Handling the ''big-box kit'' price comparison', 'Walkthroughs that surface hidden conditions']::text[], 'Selling Tub-to-Shower Conversions and Full Bath Remodels', 'Show what sits behind the tile, from blocking and waterproofing to drain changes, so the price is understood.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:bathrooms-estimating')::uuid, 'bathrooms-estimating', 'bathrooms', 'estimating', 'Bathroom Estimates: Waterproofing, Tile, Fixtures and Vanity', 'Price a bath remodel by system: demolition, waterproofing, plumbing, tile, fixtures, vanity and finish work.', 'Bathroom bids are sensitive to tile square footage, waste on small rooms, waterproofing membranes, and fixture rough-in changes. This course covers takeoffs for tile, backer board and membrane, plumbing and electrical rough-in allowances, and vanity and fixture allowances. Pricing for demolition, disposal and protection of adjacent rooms belongs in the same estimate.', 'intermediate', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'navy', false, 30, array['Tile square footage and waste on small rooms', 'Backer board, membrane and waterproofing', 'Plumbing and fan rough-in pricing', 'Vanity, mirror and fixture allowances', 'Demolition, disposal and protection pricing']::text[], 'Bathroom Estimates: Waterproofing, Tile, Fixtures and Vanity', 'Price a bath remodel by system: demolition, waterproofing, plumbing, tile, fixtures, vanity and finish work.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:bathrooms-project-management')::uuid, 'bathrooms-project-management', 'bathrooms', 'project_management', 'Sequencing a Bath Remodel: Rough-In, Tile Cure and Fixture Installs', 'Order rough-ins, waterproofing, tile setting, cure time and fixture installs so each trade starts on a ready surface.', 'Bathroom remodels depend on sequence: waterproofing must be tested before tile, and tile needs cure time before grout and fixtures go in. This course covers rough-in inspection timing, scheduling tile setters and plumbers in the right order, and protecting finished work during the final weeks. Inspection and waterproofing test requirements vary by locality; confirm them early.', 'intermediate', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'green', false, 40, array['Rough-in inspection and close-up timing', 'Waterproofing test before tile', 'Tile setting, cure time and grouting', 'Fixture and vanity installation order', 'Protecting finished work until final walkthrough']::text[], null, 'Order rough-ins, waterproofing, tile setting, cure time and fixture installs so each trade starts on a ready surface.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:bathrooms-accounting')::uuid, 'bathrooms-accounting', 'bathrooms', 'accounting', 'Job Costing Bathroom Remodels: Trades, Tile and Change Orders', 'Track each bath''s costs by trade and phase, and record the change orders that hidden conditions create.', 'Bathroom margins tend to slip when hidden conditions, rot behind tubs, or drain problems turn into unbilled work. This course shows how to set cost codes by trade and phase, track tile and fixture overages, and document change orders before work starts. Tax treatment of materials and subcontracts varies by state; confirm details with your accountant.', 'intermediate', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'amber', false, 50, array['Cost codes by trade and phase', 'Tracking tile and fixture overages', 'Documenting hidden conditions as change orders', 'Plumbing and electrical subcontract tracking', 'Deposits and progress billing for baths']::text[], null, 'Track each bath''s costs by trade and phase, and record the change orders that hidden conditions create.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:bathrooms-hr')::uuid, 'bathrooms-hr', 'bathrooms', 'hr', 'Training Crew for Tile, Waterproofing and Finish Quality', 'Build crew habits for membrane details, tile layout and finish cleanliness in small, tight bathrooms.', 'Bathroom quality is judged in details like membrane laps, level tile, and clean caulk lines, and those depend on crew habits. This course covers training helpers and carpenters on waterproofing details, tile layout, and quality checks before a crew leaves. Wage and classification rules vary by state; confirm them with your accountant.', 'beginner', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'rose', false, 60, array['Membrane laps and corner details', 'Tile layout and level checks', 'Caulk and grout quality standards', 'Training helpers in small, tight spaces', 'Keeping a skilled crew through slow months']::text[], 'Training Crew for Tile, Waterproofing and Finish Quality', 'Build crew habits for membrane details, tile layout and finish cleanliness in small, tight bathrooms.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:bathrooms-growth')::uuid, 'bathrooms-growth', 'bathrooms', 'growth', 'Repeat and Referral Work from Bathroom Remodels', 'Use finished baths, care guides and follow-up calls to win referrals and the next room in the house.', 'Bathroom clients often want the next room done after a good experience, and their neighbors notice a clean finish. This course covers final walkthroughs and care guides for grout and caulk, post-job follow-up, and referral requests from clients and designers. Marketing and solicitation rules vary by locality.', 'intermediate', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'cyan', false, 70, array['Care guides for grout, caulk and fixtures', 'Post-job follow-up and warranty check-in', 'Asking for referrals and reviews', 'Working with designers and real estate referrals', 'Planning the next room with past clients']::text[], 'Repeat and Referral Work from Bathroom Remodels', 'Use finished baths, care guides and follow-up calls to win referrals and the next room in the house.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:bathrooms-safety')::uuid, 'bathrooms-safety', 'bathrooms', 'safety', 'Bathroom Remodel Safety: Electrical Near Water and Demolition Hazards', 'Manage electrical work near water, dust from tile and plaster, and hazards in old bathroom materials.', 'Bathrooms combine water and electrical hazards, and demolition can release dust and expose old materials. This course covers de-energizing circuits near wet areas, GFCI and fan requirements as they apply to your jobs, and dust control during tile removal. Electrical, ventilation, and lead or asbestos rules vary by state and locality; confirm requirements before demolition.', 'advanced', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'slate', false, 80, array['De-energizing circuits near wet areas', 'GFCI and fan requirements by locality', 'Dust control during tile and plaster removal', 'Checking older bathrooms for lead and asbestos', 'Safe handling of heavy tubs and stone']::text[], null, 'Manage electrical work near water, dust from tile and plaster, and hazards in old bathroom materials.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:interior-remodeling-getting-started')::uuid, 'interior-remodeling-getting-started', 'interior-remodeling', 'getting_started', 'Starting an Interior Remodeling Company: Licensing and Insurance', 'Business basics for an interior remodeling company, including licensing, insurance and which trades you perform.', 'Interior remodels often include structural changes, electrical moves, and plumbing relocations, so the scope you can legally perform depends on your license. This course covers business setup, deciding which trades to self-perform, and insurance for work in occupied homes. Licensing scope and home improvement contract rules vary by state; confirm them with your licensing board.', 'beginner', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'slate', false, 10, array['Entity setup and tax registration basics', 'Licensing scope when walls or circuits change', 'Insurance for occupied-home remodels', 'Choosing trades to self-perform or sub', 'Contracts for multi-room and whole-floor work']::text[], null, 'Business basics for an interior remodeling company, including licensing, insurance and which trades you perform.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:interior-remodeling-sales')::uuid, 'interior-remodeling-sales', 'interior-remodeling', 'sales', 'Scoping Multi-Room Interior Work with Homeowners', 'Walk each room, record the goals, and agree on phases so the homeowner knows what they are buying.', 'Interior remodels often grow as homeowners see possibilities, so a vague ''refresh the floor'' can turn into a much bigger job. This course covers room-by-room walkthroughs, writing goals and must-haves into the scope, and presenting phased options so the homeowner can decide what comes first. Selections and allowances should be confirmed in writing.', 'intermediate', 'public', 'published', 'mixed', 'cyan', false, 20, array['Room-by-room walkthrough and goals', 'Writing must-haves and nice-to-haves', 'Presenting phased options with clear totals', 'Setting allowances for selections', 'Confirming scope before demolition']::text[], 'Scoping Multi-Room Interior Work with Homeowners', 'Walk each room, record the goals, and agree on phases so the homeowner knows what they are buying.', now()),
  (md5('academy:course:interior-remodeling-estimating')::uuid, 'interior-remodeling-estimating', 'interior-remodeling', 'estimating', 'Phased Interior Estimates: Framing, Drywall, Trim, Flooring and Paint', 'Estimate interior work by phase or room, with framing changes, finish trades and allowances in separate sections.', 'Interior estimates depend on how many walls change, how much drywall and trim each room needs, and how flooring and paint fit into the sequence. This course covers takeoffs by phase or room, allowances for flooring and fixtures, and contingency language for hidden conditions. Pricing decisions are yours; keep allowances visible so the client can see where money can move.', 'intermediate', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'navy', false, 30, array['Takeoffs by room or by phase', 'Framing changes and header sizing', 'Drywall, trim and paint quantities', 'Flooring and fixture allowances', 'Contingency language for hidden conditions']::text[], null, 'Estimate interior work by phase or room, with framing changes, finish trades and allowances in separate sections.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:interior-remodeling-project-management')::uuid, 'interior-remodeling-project-management', 'interior-remodeling', 'project_management', 'Sequencing Interior Remodels Room by Room', 'Plan framing, rough-ins, drywall, trim and paint so each room moves forward without rework.', 'Interior remodels stack trades in a fixed order, and paint or flooring started too early gets damaged by the trades that follow. This course covers sequencing framing and rough-ins, scheduling drywall finish and paint, and keeping a whole floor usable for the homeowner. Inspection requirements vary by locality; confirm them before closing walls.', 'intermediate', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'green', false, 40, array['Framing and rough-in sequence', 'Drywall finish scheduling and dust control', 'Trim, flooring and paint order', 'Keeping a home usable during the remodel', 'Managing inspections and close-up timing']::text[], 'Sequencing Interior Remodels Room by Room', 'Plan framing, rough-ins, drywall, trim and paint so each room moves forward without rework.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:interior-remodeling-accounting')::uuid, 'interior-remodeling-accounting', 'interior-remodeling', 'accounting', 'Job Costing Interior Remodels: Phases, Change Orders and Allowances', 'Track costs by phase and room, and document change orders and allowance overruns as they happen.', 'Interior jobs drift when allowances run over, hidden conditions appear, and client-driven changes pile up without paperwork. This course covers cost codes by phase or room, tracking allowance use against the estimate, and documenting change orders before work begins. Tax treatment of materials and subcontracts varies by state; confirm details with your accountant.', 'intermediate', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'amber', false, 50, array['Cost codes by phase or room', 'Tracking allowance use against the estimate', 'Writing change orders before work begins', 'Subcontract and material tracking', 'Progress billing tied to completed phases']::text[], null, 'Track costs by phase and room, and document change orders and allowance overruns as they happen.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:interior-remodeling-hr')::uuid, 'interior-remodeling-hr', 'interior-remodeling', 'hr', 'Building a Remodel Crew for Framing, Drywall and Finish Work', 'Hire and train carpenters and finishers who can move through a home without damaging finished rooms.', 'Interior remodels need carpenters, drywall finishers, and painters who respect each other''s sequence and protect finished work. This course covers hiring for multi-skill crews, defining roles for framing, finish and paint, and training on protection standards. Wage and classification rules vary by state; confirm them with your accountant.', 'beginner', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'rose', false, 60, array['Hiring carpenters with finish experience', 'Defining roles across framing and finish', 'Protection standards for occupied homes', 'Training crews on dust and cleanup', 'Retaining skilled crew between remodels']::text[], 'Building a Remodel Crew for Framing, Drywall and Finish Work', 'Hire and train carpenters and finishers who can move through a home without damaging finished rooms.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:interior-remodeling-growth')::uuid, 'interior-remodeling-growth', 'interior-remodeling', 'growth', 'Repeat Interior Work from Homeowners and Property Managers', 'Turn a finished remodel into the next room, a referral or a recurring turnover contract with a property manager.', 'Interior remodels lead naturally to the next room, and property managers often need steady turnover work. This course covers final walkthroughs, post-job check-ins, and offering periodic refresh or turnover work to property managers. Marketing and contract rules vary by locality; confirm terms before offering recurring work.', 'intermediate', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'cyan', false, 70, array['Final walkthrough and punch list', 'Post-job check-in for the next room', 'Turnover work for property managers', 'Referral requests from finished clients', 'Tracking repeat clients and their projects']::text[], 'Repeat Interior Work from Homeowners and Property Managers', 'Turn a finished remodel into the next room, a referral or a recurring turnover contract with a property manager.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:interior-remodeling-safety')::uuid, 'interior-remodeling-safety', 'interior-remodeling', 'safety', 'Interior Remodel Safety: Dust, Hidden Wiring and Opened Walls', 'Control dust, avoid hidden wiring and plumbing, and manage open walls and floors in occupied homes.', 'Opening walls and floors can reveal live wiring, old plumbing, and materials that need special handling. This course covers locating utilities before cutting, dust control and protection for occupants, and fall and trip hazards on open floor systems. Lead, asbestos, and dust rules vary by state and locality; confirm requirements before demolition.', 'advanced', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'slate', false, 80, array['Locating wiring and plumbing before cutting', 'Dust control and occupant protection', 'Trip and fall hazards on open floors', 'Checking older homes for lead and asbestos', 'Ladder and lift safety for ceiling work']::text[], null, 'Control dust, avoid hidden wiring and plumbing, and manage open walls and floors in occupied homes.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:exterior-remodeling-getting-started')::uuid, 'exterior-remodeling-getting-started', 'exterior-remodeling', 'getting_started', 'Starting an Exterior Remodeling Company: Scope and Licensing', 'Business basics for an exterior remodeling company, including licensing, insurance and which trades you self-perform.', 'Exterior remodels combine siding, windows, doors, roofing edges, and paint, and each trade can have its own licensing and insurance rules. This course covers business setup, deciding which exterior trades you perform yourself, and insurance for work on occupied homes at height. Licensing scope and home improvement contract rules vary by state; confirm them with your licensing board.', 'beginner', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'slate', false, 10, array['Entity setup and tax registration basics', 'Which exterior trades you self-perform', 'Licensing scope for multi-trade exterior work', 'Insurance for work at height on occupied homes', 'Defining your service area and typical projects']::text[], 'Starting an Exterior Remodeling Company: Scope and Licensing', 'Business basics for an exterior remodeling company, including licensing, insurance and which trades you self-perform.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:exterior-remodeling-sales')::uuid, 'exterior-remodeling-sales', 'exterior-remodeling', 'sales', 'Selling Curb-Appeal Packages Without Piecemeal Quotes', 'Present exterior upgrades as one package with an order of work, so the homeowner sees the whole picture.', 'Many homeowners ask for a single item, like a front door, and only later realize the trim, paint, and siding around it need work too. This course covers walking the exterior with the homeowner, presenting a package with phases, and explaining why some items should go first. Warranty and product terms vary by manufacturer; state them in writing.', 'intermediate', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'cyan', false, 20, array['Walking the exterior with the homeowner', 'Presenting a package with phases', 'Explaining why some items go first', 'Handling the ''just the door'' request', 'Writing a proposal that shows the full elevation']::text[], 'Selling Curb-Appeal Packages Without Piecemeal Quotes', 'Present exterior upgrades as one package with an order of work, so the homeowner sees the whole picture.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:exterior-remodeling-estimating')::uuid, 'exterior-remodeling-estimating', 'exterior-remodeling', 'estimating', 'Exterior Remodel Estimates: Siding, Trim, Windows and Paint', 'Build one estimate with separate sections for siding, trim, openings, gutters and paint, each with its own takeoff.', 'Exterior estimates combine wall area, trim footage, window and door counts, gutter runs, and paint coverage, and rot found under old materials changes the scope. This course covers building a single estimate with sections, allowances for hidden rot, and pricing that lets the homeowner see each piece. Material prices vary by supplier and region; verify them before bidding.', 'intermediate', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'navy', false, 30, array['Takeoffs for siding, trim and openings', 'Gutter and downspout runs', 'Paint coverage and prep scope', 'Allowances for hidden rot and repair', 'Presenting sections in one proposal']::text[], 'Exterior Remodel Estimates: Siding, Trim, Windows and Paint', 'Build one estimate with separate sections for siding, trim, openings, gutters and paint, each with its own takeoff.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:exterior-remodeling-project-management')::uuid, 'exterior-remodeling-project-management', 'exterior-remodeling', 'project_management', 'Coordinating Exterior Trades in the Right Order', 'Sequence windows, doors, siding, trim, gutters and paint so each trade protects the work that comes before it.', 'Exterior remodels depend on order: windows and doors must be flashed before siding, and paint should follow trim and caulk. This course covers coordinating subs in the right sequence, weather planning for paint and sealant cure, and the walkthrough that closes each phase. Permit and inspection requirements vary by locality; confirm them before scheduling.', 'intermediate', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'green', false, 40, array['Window and door flashing before siding', 'Trim, caulk and paint sequence', 'Weather planning for paint and sealant', 'Coordinating gutter and roofing subs', 'Phase walkthroughs and homeowner sign-off']::text[], 'Coordinating Exterior Trades in the Right Order', 'Sequence windows, doors, siding, trim, gutters and paint so each trade protects the work that comes before it.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:exterior-remodeling-accounting')::uuid, 'exterior-remodeling-accounting', 'exterior-remodeling', 'accounting', 'Job Costing Exterior Remodels by Trade and Phase', 'Track labor and materials by trade and phase so you can see which exterior packages earn their margin.', 'Exterior margins slip when rot repairs, subcontract changes, and paint prep run longer than the estimate allowed. This course covers cost codes by trade and phase, tracking subs against scope, and documenting change orders for hidden damage. Tax treatment of materials and subcontracts varies by state; confirm it with your accountant.', 'intermediate', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'amber', false, 50, array['Cost codes by trade and phase', 'Tracking subcontract invoices against scope', 'Documenting rot repairs as change orders', 'Paint prep labor tracking', 'Deposits and progress billing for exterior packages']::text[], 'Job Costing Exterior Remodels by Trade and Phase', 'Track labor and materials by trade and phase so you can see which exterior packages earn their margin.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:exterior-remodeling-hr')::uuid, 'exterior-remodeling-hr', 'exterior-remodeling', 'hr', 'Training Exterior Crews Across Carpentry, Paint and Finish', 'Hire and train carpenters and painters who can work at height and keep trim and paint details clean.', 'Exterior remodel crews move between carpentry, finish, and paint, and each needs different skills and ladder habits. This course covers hiring for multi-skill exterior crews, defining roles for trim, window and door work, and training on detail quality. Wage and classification rules vary by state; confirm them with your accountant.', 'beginner', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'rose', false, 60, array['Hiring for multi-skill exterior crews', 'Roles for trim, doors and window installs', 'Paint and caulk detail standards', 'Ladder and height habits for new hires', 'Keeping crews busy across seasons']::text[], 'Training Exterior Crews Across Carpentry, Paint and Finish', 'Hire and train carpenters and painters who can work at height and keep trim and paint details clean.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:exterior-remodeling-growth')::uuid, 'exterior-remodeling-growth', 'exterior-remodeling', 'growth', 'Repeat Exterior Work from Neighborhood and Storm Follow-Up', 'Build repeat business from neighbors who see a finished front elevation and from property managers who need exterior repairs.', 'A finished exterior is highly visible, so neighbors often ask for quotes on their own homes. This course covers neighborhood follow-up after a project, documenting finished work with permission, and building relationships with property managers who need repairs and repaints. Marketing and solicitation rules vary by locality.', 'intermediate', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'cyan', false, 70, array['Neighborhood follow-up after a visible project', 'Documenting finished work with permission', 'Property manager repair and repaint work', 'Storm-response planning for exterior clients', 'Asking for referrals from completed clients']::text[], 'Repeat Exterior Work from Neighborhood and Storm Follow-Up', 'Build repeat business from neighbors who see a finished front elevation and from property managers who need exterior repairs.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:exterior-remodeling-safety')::uuid, 'exterior-remodeling-safety', 'exterior-remodeling', 'safety', 'Exterior Remodel Safety: Height, Scaffold and Lead-Paint Work', 'Manage fall exposure on exterior walls, scaffold setup, and lead-paint precautions on older homes.', 'Exterior remodels put crews on ladders, scaffolds, and rolling access, and paint removal on older homes can expose workers to lead. This course covers scaffold setup and inspection, fall protection where required, and lead-paint precautions during scraping and sanding. Scaffolding, fall protection, and lead-paint rules vary by state and locality; confirm the requirements for your jobs.', 'advanced', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'slate', false, 80, array['Scaffold and rolling access setup', 'Fall protection for exterior work at height', 'Lead-paint precautions during scraping', 'Containing paint dust and debris', 'Overhead power line clearance on exterior jobs']::text[], null, 'Manage fall exposure on exterior walls, scaffold setup, and lead-paint precautions on older homes.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:drywall-getting-started')::uuid, 'drywall-getting-started', 'drywall', 'getting_started', 'Starting a Drywall Business: Licensing, Insurance and Subcontracting', 'Business basics for a drywall company, including licensing, insurance and how you work as a sub for builders.', 'Drywall businesses often work as subcontractors for builders and remodelers, and general contractors usually require proof of insurance. This course covers business setup, licensing or registration for drywall work, liability and workers'' comp coverage, and how sub agreements shape your scope. Licensing and registration rules vary by state and locality; confirm them with your licensing board.', 'beginner', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'slate', false, 10, array['Entity setup and tax registration basics', 'Licensing or registration for drywall work', 'Liability and workers'' comp for crews', 'Sub agreements and insurance certificates', 'Choosing residential or commercial work']::text[], null, 'Business basics for a drywall company, including licensing, insurance and how you work as a sub for builders.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:drywall-sales')::uuid, 'drywall-sales', 'drywall', 'sales', 'Explaining Drywall Finish Levels to Homeowners', 'Use photos and written finish levels so homeowners know what smooth means before the work starts.', 'Finish expectations cause most drywall disputes, and homeowners often assume the wall will look like a showroom at the lowest price. This course covers explaining finish levels with photos under the right lighting, identifying walls that need primer or skim coat, and writing finish expectations into the proposal. Standards and finish descriptions vary by company; define yours in writing.', 'intermediate', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'cyan', false, 20, array['Finish levels explained with photos', 'Walls that need skim coat or primer', 'Writing finish expectations into proposals', 'Handling the ''why isn''t it perfect'' question', 'Walkthroughs with painters and homeowners']::text[], 'Explaining Drywall Finish Levels to Homeowners', 'Use photos and written finish levels so homeowners know what smooth means before the work starts.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:drywall-estimating')::uuid, 'drywall-estimating', 'drywall', 'estimating', 'Drywall Estimates: Sheets, Mud, Tape and Labor by Square Foot', 'Count sheets, joint compound, tape, corner bead and labor by square foot, with waste and finish levels built in.', 'Drywall estimates start with square footage and sheet count, then add waste, joint compound, tape, corner bead, and fasteners. Labor changes with finish level, ceiling height, and the number of coats needed. This course covers sheet takeoffs, waste factors for cut-up walls, and pricing for finish levels and texture.', 'intermediate', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'navy', false, 30, array['Sheet counts and waste on cut-up walls', 'Joint compound, tape and corner bead', 'Labor rates by finish level and height', 'Pricing texture and skim coat', 'Pricing repairs and patch work']::text[], null, 'Count sheets, joint compound, tape, corner bead and labor by square foot, with waste and finish levels built in.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:drywall-project-management')::uuid, 'drywall-project-management', 'drywall', 'project_management', 'Sequencing Drywall Hang, Tape and Finish Across the House', 'Schedule hang, tape, coats and sanding so each phase gets a clean surface and the painters can start on time.', 'Drywall moves through hang, tape, multiple coats, and sanding, and each coat needs drying time before the next. This course covers sequencing rooms for hang and finish, scheduling dry time between coats, and coordinating with electricians and painters. Fire-rated and inspection requirements vary by locality; confirm them before closing walls.', 'intermediate', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'green', false, 40, array['Hang sequence and room order', 'Drying time between coats', 'Sanding and dust control scheduling', 'Coordinating with electricians and painters', 'Inspection and fire-rated assembly timing']::text[], 'Sequencing Drywall Hang, Tape and Finish Across the House', 'Schedule hang, tape, coats and sanding so each phase gets a clean surface and the painters can start on time.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:drywall-accounting')::uuid, 'drywall-accounting', 'drywall', 'accounting', 'Drywall Job Costing: Sheets, Labor and Waste Tracking', 'Track sheets, compound and labor hours by job so you can see where the finish work ran longer than planned.', 'Drywall margins are tight, and finish work often runs longer than the estimate because of hard-to-sand walls or extra coats. This course covers recording sheet and compound use against the takeoff, tracking labor hours by phase, and billing change orders for finish upgrades. Tax treatment of materials and subcontracts varies by state; confirm details with your accountant.', 'intermediate', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'amber', false, 50, array['Matching sheet use to the takeoff', 'Tracking labor hours by phase', 'Recording waste and damaged material', 'Billing extra coats and finish upgrades', 'Progress billing for hang and finish phases']::text[], 'Drywall Job Costing: Sheets, Labor and Waste Tracking', 'Track sheets, compound and labor hours by job so you can see where the finish work ran longer than planned.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:drywall-hr')::uuid, 'drywall-hr', 'drywall', 'hr', 'Hiring Hangers and Finishers Who Produce Clean Walls', 'Recruit hangers and finishers who can hit production targets while keeping seams and corners straight.', 'Drywall crews are small, fast, and specialized, and a single weak finisher can slow a whole job. This course covers hiring for hanging and finishing skills, defining roles between hangers and taper finishers, and training on seam and corner quality. Wage and classification rules vary by state; confirm them with your accountant.', 'beginner', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'rose', false, 60, array['Interviewing for hang and finish skills', 'Roles for hangers and taper finishers', 'Seam and corner quality standards', 'Training helpers on sanding and dust', 'Retaining finishers through slow periods']::text[], 'Hiring Hangers and Finishers Who Produce Clean Walls', 'Recruit hangers and finishers who can hit production targets while keeping seams and corners straight.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:drywall-growth')::uuid, 'drywall-growth', 'drywall', 'growth', 'Building Repeat Work with Builders, Remodelers and Repair Clients', 'Earn repeat sub work from builders and remodelers, and steady repair calls from homeowners after water damage.', 'Drywall work repeats with builders on new construction and with remodelers and restoration companies after water or fire damage. This course covers building relationships with builders and remodelers, responding quickly to repair calls, and asking past clients for referrals. Solicitation and advertising rules vary by locality.', 'intermediate', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'cyan', false, 70, array['Building relationships with builders', 'Working with remodelers and restoration companies', 'Fast response for repair calls', 'Following up with past clients', 'Tracking which sources send repeat work']::text[], null, 'Earn repeat sub work from builders and remodelers, and steady repair calls from homeowners after water damage.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:drywall-safety')::uuid, 'drywall-safety', 'drywall', 'safety', 'Drywall Safety: Dust, Lifting Sheets and Ladder Work', 'Control dust from sanding, handle heavy sheets safely and work at height without overreaching.', 'Drywall work creates fine dust from sanding and involves lifting heavy sheets overhead, which causes strains and falls. This course covers dust control and respiratory protection, safe sheet handling and lifting technique, and ladder and scaffold use for ceilings. Respiratory protection and dust rules vary by state and locality; confirm the requirements that apply to your jobs.', 'advanced', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'slate', false, 80, array['Dust control for sanding and joint work', 'Respiratory protection basics', 'Safe sheet lifting and overhead hanging', 'Ladder and scaffold use for ceilings', 'Fire-rated assembly quality checks']::text[], 'Drywall Safety: Dust, Lifting Sheets and Ladder Work', 'Control dust from sanding, handle heavy sheets safely and work at height without overreaching.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:painting-getting-started')::uuid, 'painting-getting-started', 'painting', 'getting_started', 'Starting a Painting Business: Licensing, Insurance and Lead Rules', 'Business basics for a painting company, including licensing, insurance and lead-safe rules for older homes.', 'Painting companies work inside occupied homes and often handle older paint that may contain lead. This course covers business setup, licensing requirements, liability and workers'' comp coverage, and the lead-safe work rules that apply to older homes. Licensing and lead-safe rules vary by state and locality; confirm them with your licensing board and the agencies that govern your area.', 'beginner', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'slate', false, 10, array['Entity setup and tax registration basics', 'Licensing requirements for painting work', 'Liability and workers'' comp for painters', 'Lead-safe practices for older homes', 'Choosing residential, commercial or both']::text[], null, 'Business basics for a painting company, including licensing, insurance and lead-safe rules for older homes.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:painting-sales')::uuid, 'painting-sales', 'painting', 'sales', 'Selling Prep and Workmanship, Not Just Gallons', 'Explain how prep, primer, and coats affect the finish, so the price reflects a professional result.', 'Homeowners often assume paint is the main cost, when prep, repairs, and masking usually take more time. This course covers walkthroughs that identify prep needs, explaining primer and coat counts in plain language, and presenting color and sheen options. Warranty and product terms vary by manufacturer; state them in writing.', 'intermediate', 'public', 'published', 'mixed', 'cyan', false, 20, array['Walkthroughs that identify prep needs', 'Explaining primer and coat counts', 'Presenting color and sheen options', 'Handling the ''just paint it'' request', 'Writing proposals that separate prep from paint']::text[], 'Selling Prep and Workmanship, Not Just Gallons', 'Explain how prep, primer, and coats affect the finish, so the price reflects a professional result.', now()),
  (md5('academy:course:painting-estimating')::uuid, 'painting-estimating', 'painting', 'estimating', 'Painting Estimates: Prep, Masking, Primer, Paint and Labor', 'Price interior and exterior paint jobs by prep scope, surface area, coats, and labor, with materials shown separately.', 'Paint estimates start with surface area and the number of coats, then add prep, masking, primer, and ceiling or trim work. Surface condition can change labor more than the paint itself, so inspection shapes the bid. This course covers wall and trim takeoffs, prep pricing by condition, and materials and labor presented as clear line items.', 'intermediate', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'navy', false, 30, array['Surface area and coat count takeoffs', 'Pricing prep by surface condition', 'Masking, protection and primer', 'Trim, ceiling and door line items', 'Separating materials from labor in bids']::text[], 'Painting Estimates: Prep, Masking, Primer, Paint and Labor', 'Price interior and exterior paint jobs by prep scope, surface area, coats, and labor, with materials shown separately.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:painting-project-management')::uuid, 'painting-project-management', 'painting', 'project_management', 'Scheduling Paint Work Around Drying, Occupancy and Weather', 'Plan prep, primer, coats and cure time so rooms and exteriors are finished without rework or delays.', 'Paint schedules depend on drying time, humidity and temperature, and homeowners living in the house add scheduling constraints. This course covers sequencing prep, primer, and finish coats, planning around weather for exteriors, and coordinating with other trades on finished surfaces. Product temperature guidance varies by manufacturer; check labels before scheduling.', 'intermediate', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'green', false, 40, array['Prep and primer sequencing', 'Drying times and recoat windows', 'Exterior weather and temperature planning', 'Coordinating with drywall and trim trades', 'Working around occupants and pets']::text[], 'Scheduling Paint Work Around Drying, Occupancy and Weather', 'Plan prep, primer, coats and cure time so rooms and exteriors are finished without rework or delays.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:painting-accounting')::uuid, 'painting-accounting', 'painting', 'accounting', 'Painting Job Costing: Materials, Labor Hours and Prep Overruns', 'Track paint, supplies and crew hours per job so you can see whether prep ran longer than the estimate.', 'Paint margins shrink when prep takes longer than planned, when extra coats are needed, or when materials are wasted. This course covers tracking paint and supply use against the estimate, recording labor hours by phase, and billing extra prep or coats as change orders. Tax treatment of materials and labor varies by state; confirm details with your accountant.', 'intermediate', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'amber', false, 50, array['Tracking paint and supplies by job', 'Recording labor hours by phase', 'Billing extra prep and coats', 'Handling returned or wasted paint', 'Deposits and progress billing for paint jobs']::text[], null, 'Track paint, supplies and crew hours per job so you can see whether prep ran longer than the estimate.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:painting-hr')::uuid, 'painting-hr', 'painting', 'hr', 'Building a Painting Crew with Consistent Prep and Finish Skills', 'Hire and train painters who can prep consistently, cut clean lines and protect the home while they work.', 'Painting quality comes from prep consistency and clean cut lines, which new painters often learn slowly. This course covers hiring painters, training helpers on prep and masking, and setting quality checks before a crew leaves a room. Wage and classification rules vary by state; confirm them with your accountant.', 'beginner', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'rose', false, 60, array['Hiring painters with prep and cut-in skill', 'Training helpers on prep and masking', 'Quality checks before leaving a room', 'Protection standards for furniture and floors', 'Keeping painters busy between seasons']::text[], null, 'Hire and train painters who can prep consistently, cut clean lines and protect the home while they work.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:painting-growth')::uuid, 'painting-growth', 'painting', 'growth', 'Repaint Cycles and Repeat Work from Past Painting Clients', 'Offer periodic repaints, touch-ups and cabinet refreshes to clients and property managers who want steady work.', 'Painted surfaces need periodic touch-ups and repaints, which gives a painting company natural repeat work. This course covers maintenance reminders, touch-up packages, and property manager agreements for turnover painting. Marketing and solicitation rules vary by locality; confirm terms before offering recurring service.', 'intermediate', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'cyan', false, 70, array['Maintenance reminders and touch-up packages', 'Property manager turnover painting', 'Repeat work from finished clients', 'Referral requests after a clean finish', 'Tracking repeat clients and their next projects']::text[], 'Repaint Cycles and Repeat Work from Past Painting Clients', 'Offer periodic repaints, touch-ups and cabinet refreshes to clients and property managers who want steady work.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:painting-safety')::uuid, 'painting-safety', 'painting', 'safety', 'Painting Safety: Ladders, Solvents, Ventilation and Lead', 'Manage ladder work, solvent and spray hazards, ventilation, and lead-paint precautions on older surfaces.', 'Painters work on ladders and scaffolds, use solvents and spray equipment, and often disturb older paint. This course covers ladder and scaffold setup, ventilation and respiratory protection around solvents and spray, and lead-safe methods for sanding and scraping. Lead-safe, ventilation, and respiratory rules vary by state and locality; confirm the requirements for your jobs.', 'advanced', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'slate', false, 80, array['Ladder and scaffold setup for painters', 'Ventilation around solvents and spray', 'Respiratory protection basics', 'Lead-safe sanding and scraping methods', 'Storing and disposing of paint and rags']::text[], 'Painting Safety: Ladders, Solvents, Ventilation and Lead', 'Manage ladder work, solvent and spray hazards, ventilation, and lead-paint precautions on older surfaces.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:electrical-getting-started')::uuid, 'electrical-getting-started', 'electrical', 'getting_started', 'Starting an Electrical Contracting Business: Licensing and Insurance', 'Business basics for an electrical company, including licensing, master or journeyman roles and liability coverage.', 'Electrical work carries serious shock, fire, and liability risks, and licensing rules are strict in most places. This course covers business setup, the difference between journeyman and master licensing, insurance for electrical contractors, and how to qualify for permits. Licensing requirements vary by state and locality; confirm them with your licensing board before bidding.', 'beginner', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'slate', false, 10, array['Entity setup and tax registration basics', 'Journeyman and master licensing differences', 'Insurance for electrical contractors', 'Qualifying for permits in your area', 'Choosing residential, commercial or service work']::text[], null, 'Business basics for an electrical company, including licensing, master or journeyman roles and liability coverage.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:electrical-sales')::uuid, 'electrical-sales', 'electrical', 'sales', 'Explaining Panel Upgrades and Permitted Electrical Work', 'Describe what a panel upgrade includes and why permits and inspections protect the homeowner''s insurance and resale.', 'Homeowners often ask why a panel upgrade costs so much, or whether a permit is really necessary. This course covers explaining load calculations and service upgrades in plain language, what inspections verify, and how to address do-it-yourself requests without arguing. Insurance and resale considerations vary; direct homeowners to their insurer and agent for those questions.', 'intermediate', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'cyan', false, 20, array['Explaining what a panel upgrade includes', 'Why permits and inspections matter to homeowners', 'Handling do-it-yourself requests', 'Presenting EV charger options and load limits', 'Writing proposals with clear scope and exclusions']::text[], 'Explaining Panel Upgrades and Permitted Electrical Work', 'Describe what a panel upgrade includes and why permits and inspections protect the homeowner''s insurance and resale.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:electrical-estimating')::uuid, 'electrical-estimating', 'electrical', 'estimating', 'Electrical Estimates: Wire, Devices, Panels, Labor and Testing', 'Price circuits, devices, fixtures, panel work, permits and testing as separate line items that match the job.', 'Electrical estimates build from wire footage, device counts, fixtures, and panel components, then add labor for rough-in and trim-out. Service upgrades and EV charger work often need load calculations and utility coordination that change the price. This course covers takeoff by circuit and room, pricing permits and testing, and allowances for fixtures the homeowner selects later.', 'intermediate', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'navy', false, 30, array['Wire footage and circuit takeoffs', 'Device and fixture counts by room', 'Panel work and service upgrade pricing', 'Permit, testing and inspection line items', 'Fixture allowances and homeowner selections']::text[], null, 'Price circuits, devices, fixtures, panel work, permits and testing as separate line items that match the job.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:electrical-project-management')::uuid, 'electrical-project-management', 'electrical', 'project_management', 'Sequencing Rough-In, Inspection and Trim-Out on Electrical Jobs', 'Coordinate rough-in, inspections, drywall and trim-out so the homeowner gets a working, approved system.', 'Electrical work happens in phases: rough-in before walls close, inspection before energizing, and trim-out after drywall and paint. This course covers coordinating with framers, drywall crews, and utility companies for service changes, and scheduling inspections around the build. Inspection and utility coordination rules vary by locality; confirm them before scheduling.', 'intermediate', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'green', false, 40, array['Rough-in sequence and close-up timing', 'Scheduling electrical inspections', 'Coordinating with utility service changes', 'Trim-out after drywall and paint', 'Final testing and homeowner walkthrough']::text[], null, 'Coordinate rough-in, inspections, drywall and trim-out so the homeowner gets a working, approved system.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:electrical-accounting')::uuid, 'electrical-accounting', 'electrical', 'accounting', 'Electrical Job Costing: Materials, Labor Hours and Change Orders', 'Track wire, devices, panel components and crew hours by job so you can compare each job to its estimate.', 'Electrical margins can shrink when rough-in takes longer than planned, when hidden conditions require rework, or when material pulls are not tracked. This course covers setting cost codes by phase, tracking wire and device use against the takeoff, and documenting change orders. Tax treatment of materials and labor varies by state; confirm details with your accountant.', 'intermediate', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'amber', false, 50, array['Cost codes by rough-in and trim phase', 'Tracking wire and device use', 'Recording hidden conditions as change orders', 'Permit and inspection fee tracking', 'Deposits and progress billing for electrical work']::text[], null, 'Track wire, devices, panel components and crew hours by job so you can compare each job to its estimate.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:electrical-hr')::uuid, 'electrical-hr', 'electrical', 'hr', 'Hiring and Training Electricians Under a Licensed Supervisor', 'Build a crew of apprentices and journeymen with clear supervision, training paths and documented skills.', 'Electrical businesses depend on supervised apprentices and journeymen, and supervision rules differ by state. This course covers hiring apprentices, planning a training path toward licensing, and setting supervision expectations on each job. Apprenticeship, supervision, and wage rules vary by state; confirm them with your licensing board and accountant.', 'beginner', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'rose', false, 60, array['Hiring apprentices and journeymen', 'Supervision rules and job-site oversight', 'Planning a training path toward licensing', 'Wage and classification basics', 'Retaining electricians in a tight labor market']::text[], 'Hiring and Training Electricians Under a Licensed Supervisor', 'Build a crew of apprentices and journeymen with clear supervision, training paths and documented skills.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:electrical-growth')::uuid, 'electrical-growth', 'electrical', 'growth', 'Repeat Electrical Work: Service Calls, Upgrades and Maintenance', 'Build repeat business with service calls, panel and EV charger upgrades, and maintenance for property owners.', 'Electrical customers return for service calls, added circuits, and upgrades as their homes and vehicles change. This course covers service-call pricing, follow-up after a panel upgrade, and offering inspections and maintenance to property managers and commercial clients. Marketing, advertising, and service rules vary by locality; confirm requirements before advertising.', 'intermediate', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'cyan', false, 70, array['Service-call pricing and dispatch', 'Follow-up after a panel upgrade', 'EV charger and home upgrade referrals', 'Maintenance agreements for property owners', 'Building relationships with builders and GCs']::text[], null, 'Build repeat business with service calls, panel and EV charger upgrades, and maintenance for property owners.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:electrical-safety')::uuid, 'electrical-safety', 'electrical', 'safety', 'Electrical Safety: Lockout, Arc Flash Awareness and Live Work Limits', 'Lock out circuits, respect arc flash hazards and set clear limits on live work for your crew.', 'Electrical work exposes workers to shock, arc flash, and energized equipment, especially during panel work. This course covers lockout and tagout, verifying circuits are dead before work, and setting limits for live work with PPE and training. Electrical safety rules and PPE requirements vary by state and locality; confirm the standards that apply to your jobs.', 'advanced', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'slate', false, 80, array['Lockout and tagout for circuits', 'Verifying circuits dead before work', 'Arc flash awareness at the panel', 'Limits and PPE for any live work', 'Ladder and attic safety on electrical jobs']::text[], null, 'Lock out circuits, respect arc flash hazards and set clear limits on live work for your crew.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:plumbing-getting-started')::uuid, 'plumbing-getting-started', 'plumbing', 'getting_started', 'Starting a Plumbing Company: Licensing, Insurance and Permits', 'Business basics for a plumbing company, including licensing, liability insurance and permit requirements.', 'Plumbing work touches potable water, drainage, and gas on some jobs, so licensing and inspection rules are strict. This course covers business setup, licensing for plumbing work, liability and workers'' comp coverage, and how permits are pulled for water heaters and repipes. Licensing and permit rules vary by state and locality; confirm them with your licensing board before bidding.', 'beginner', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'slate', false, 10, array['Entity setup and tax registration basics', 'Licensing for plumbing work and supervision', 'Liability and workers'' comp for plumbers', 'Permits for water heaters and repipes', 'Choosing residential, commercial or service work']::text[], null, 'Business basics for a plumbing company, including licensing, liability insurance and permit requirements.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:plumbing-sales')::uuid, 'plumbing-sales', 'plumbing', 'sales', 'Presenting Repair Versus Repipe Options Clearly', 'Show the homeowner the short-term repair, the longer-term fix and what each one covers before they choose.', 'Homeowners facing leaks or old galvanized lines often want the cheapest fix today, and that can delay a larger job. This course covers using photos and camera inspections to show condition, presenting repair and repipe options side by side, and explaining what each option leaves in place. Warranty terms vary by manufacturer and product; state them in writing.', 'intermediate', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'cyan', false, 20, array['Using photos and camera inspections', 'Presenting repair and repipe options side by side', 'Explaining what each option leaves in place', 'Handling urgent repair requests', 'Writing proposals that match the chosen option']::text[], 'Presenting Repair Versus Repipe Options Clearly', 'Show the homeowner the short-term repair, the longer-term fix and what each one covers before they choose.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:plumbing-estimating')::uuid, 'plumbing-estimating', 'plumbing', 'estimating', 'Plumbing Estimates: Supply, Drain, Fixtures and Water Heaters', 'Build a plumbing bid from supply and drain footage, fixtures, water heaters, fittings, labor and permits.', 'Plumbing estimates start with pipe footage by material, fixture counts, and fittings, then add labor for rough-in and trim-out. Water heater and repipe jobs also carry access, cutting, and patching costs that are easy to miss. This course covers takeoffs by system, pricing for fixtures and allowances, and permit and inspection line items.', 'intermediate', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'navy', false, 30, array['Supply and drain footage by material', 'Fixture counts and rough-in pricing', 'Water heater replacement line items', 'Access, cutting and patching allowances', 'Permit and inspection line items']::text[], null, 'Build a plumbing bid from supply and drain footage, fixtures, water heaters, fittings, labor and permits.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:plumbing-project-management')::uuid, 'plumbing-project-management', 'plumbing', 'project_management', 'Sequencing Rough-In, Pressure Tests and Trim-Out', 'Coordinate rough-in, pressure tests, inspections and finish work so the system is approved before walls close.', 'Plumbing rough-in has to pass pressure tests and inspection before walls close, and fixtures wait until finish work is done. This course covers sequencing rough-in with framers and drywall crews, scheduling pressure tests and inspections, and coordinating fixture delivery. Inspection and testing requirements vary by locality; confirm them before scheduling.', 'intermediate', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'green', false, 40, array['Rough-in sequence with framers', 'Scheduling pressure tests and inspections', 'Coordinating fixture and water heater delivery', 'Trim-out and fixture set order', 'Final testing and homeowner walkthrough']::text[], 'Sequencing Rough-In, Pressure Tests and Trim-Out', 'Coordinate rough-in, pressure tests, inspections and finish work so the system is approved before walls close.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:plumbing-accounting')::uuid, 'plumbing-accounting', 'plumbing', 'accounting', 'Plumbing Job Costing: Pipe, Fixtures, Permits and Return Trips', 'Track pipe, fixtures, permit fees and crew hours so return trips and rework show up in your numbers.', 'Plumbing margins are often lost on return trips, rework, and fixtures that arrive damaged or the wrong size. This course covers tracking materials by job, recording permit and inspection fees, and billing return trips caused by hidden conditions. Tax treatment of materials and labor varies by state; confirm details with your accountant.', 'intermediate', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'amber', false, 50, array['Tracking pipe and fittings by job', 'Recording fixture returns and damage', 'Permit and inspection fee tracking', 'Billing return trips and hidden conditions', 'Deposits and progress billing for plumbing']::text[], null, 'Track pipe, fixtures, permit fees and crew hours so return trips and rework show up in your numbers.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:plumbing-hr')::uuid, 'plumbing-hr', 'plumbing', 'hr', 'Training Plumbers and Helpers for Repeatable Quality', 'Build apprentice and helper skills for solder, press and pipe joints, and set quality checks before a crew leaves a job.', 'Plumbing quality depends on consistent joints and clean fixture installs, and apprentices need supervised practice. This course covers hiring plumbers and helpers, training on joint methods and fixture setting, and documenting quality checks before a crew leaves. Apprenticeship, supervision, and wage rules vary by state; confirm them with your licensing board and accountant.', 'beginner', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'rose', false, 60, array['Hiring plumbers and helpers', 'Training on joint methods and fixture setting', 'Supervised practice for apprentices', 'Quality checklists before leaving a job', 'Keeping plumbers through busy seasons']::text[], 'Training Plumbers and Helpers for Repeatable Quality', 'Build apprentice and helper skills for solder, press and pipe joints, and set quality checks before a crew leaves a job.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:plumbing-growth')::uuid, 'plumbing-growth', 'plumbing', 'growth', 'Service Agreements and Repeat Plumbing Work', 'Turn one-time repairs into recurring service with water heater maintenance, inspections and property manager accounts.', 'Plumbing customers return for emergencies and maintenance, and property managers often need steady service. This course covers building maintenance agreements for water heaters and fixtures, reminder systems for service intervals, and property manager accounts. Marketing and service-agreement rules vary by locality; confirm terms before offering recurring service.', 'intermediate', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'cyan', false, 70, array['Water heater maintenance agreements', 'Reminder systems for service intervals', 'Property manager accounts and priority service', 'Follow-up after emergency repairs', 'Referrals from builders and real estate contacts']::text[], 'Service Agreements and Repeat Plumbing Work', 'Turn one-time repairs into recurring service with water heater maintenance, inspections and property manager accounts.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:plumbing-safety')::uuid, 'plumbing-safety', 'plumbing', 'safety', 'Plumbing Safety: Gas Work, Hot Water and Confined Trenches', 'Manage gas and scalding hazards, trench and confined-space risks, and safe handling of heavy water heaters.', 'Plumbing work can involve gas lines, scalding hot water, trenches, and crawlspaces where air and footing are limited. This course covers gas line precautions and testing, safe handling of heavy water heaters, and trench and crawlspace hazards. Gas, trenching, and confined-space rules vary by state and locality; confirm the requirements that apply to your jobs.', 'advanced', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'slate', false, 80, array['Gas line precautions and leak testing', 'Scalding risk during water heater work', 'Trench and excavation hazards for sewer work', 'Crawlspace and confined-space awareness', 'Lifting and moving heavy water heaters']::text[], 'Plumbing Safety: Gas Work, Hot Water and Confined Trenches', 'Manage gas and scalding hazards, trench and confined-space risks, and safe handling of heavy water heaters.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:hvac-getting-started')::uuid, 'hvac-getting-started', 'hvac', 'getting_started', 'Starting an HVAC Business: Licensing, Certifications and Insurance', 'Business basics for an HVAC company, including licensing, technician certifications and refrigerant handling rules.', 'HVAC work involves gas, electrical connections and refrigerants, and licensing and certification rules apply to many tasks. This course covers business setup, licensing for install and service work, technician certifications, and insurance for install and service crews. Licensing, certification, and refrigerant rules vary by state and locality; confirm them with your licensing board.', 'beginner', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'slate', false, 10, array['Entity setup and tax registration basics', 'Licensing for install and service work', 'Technician certifications and refrigerant rules', 'Insurance for install and service crews', 'Choosing residential, light commercial or both']::text[], null, 'Business basics for an HVAC company, including licensing, technician certifications and refrigerant handling rules.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:hvac-sales')::uuid, 'hvac-sales', 'hvac', 'sales', 'Selling Equipment Replacements Based on the Home, Not the Price', 'Explain load, efficiency and ductwork in plain terms, so the customer compares systems that fit their home.', 'Customers often compare furnaces and air conditioners by sticker price and ask for the lowest bid. This course covers load calculations, efficiency ratings, ductwork and airflow, and presenting good, better, and best options with the tradeoffs spelled out. Equipment incentives and warranty terms vary by manufacturer and location; state them in writing.', 'intermediate', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'cyan', false, 20, array['Explaining load calculations to customers', 'Efficiency ratings and what they mean', 'Good, better, best options with tradeoffs', 'Handling the ''just swap the unit'' request', 'Writing proposals that match the system']::text[], null, 'Explain load, efficiency and ductwork in plain terms, so the customer compares systems that fit their home.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:hvac-estimating')::uuid, 'hvac-estimating', 'hvac', 'estimating', 'HVAC Estimates: Equipment, Line Sets, Ductwork and Controls', 'Price equipment, line sets, ductwork, controls, startup and labor as clear sections in one proposal.', 'HVAC estimates include equipment, line sets, electrical and gas connections, ductwork modifications, controls, and startup. Ductwork and line set length change labor more than customers expect, and unseen conditions in attics and crawlspaces add risk. This course covers building a takeoff by system, allowances for duct work, and pricing for startup and commissioning.', 'intermediate', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'navy', false, 30, array['Equipment and matched-system pricing', 'Line set length and refrigerant charge', 'Ductwork modification allowances', 'Controls, thermostats and smart add-ons', 'Startup, commissioning and warranty registration']::text[], 'HVAC Estimates: Equipment, Line Sets, Ductwork and Controls', 'Price equipment, line sets, ductwork, controls, startup and labor as clear sections in one proposal.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:hvac-project-management')::uuid, 'hvac-project-management', 'hvac', 'project_management', 'Scheduling Equipment Changeouts and Ductwork Around Seasons', 'Plan changeouts, ductwork and startup around the heating and cooling season so customers are not left without comfort.', 'HVAC demand peaks in extreme weather, and changeouts need to be scheduled so customers are not left without heat or cooling. This course covers planning equipment deliveries, sequencing ductwork and line sets, and coordinating electrical and gas connections with other trades. Permit and inspection requirements vary by locality; confirm them before scheduling.', 'intermediate', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'green', false, 40, array['Seasonal demand and scheduling capacity', 'Sequencing equipment, line sets and ducts', 'Coordinating electrical and gas connections', 'Planning around customers without heat', 'Startup and handoff timing']::text[], 'Scheduling Equipment Changeouts and Ductwork Around Seasons', 'Plan changeouts, ductwork and startup around the heating and cooling season so customers are not left without comfort.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:hvac-accounting')::uuid, 'hvac-accounting', 'hvac', 'accounting', 'HVAC Job Costing: Equipment, Refrigerant, Labor and Service Calls', 'Track equipment, refrigerant, line sets and labor by job so you can see which installs and service calls earn margin.', 'HVAC margins depend on equipment costs, refrigerant usage, and labor hours that vary with access and duct conditions. This course covers tracking equipment and refrigerant by job, recording service call and return visit costs, and billing change orders for hidden conditions. Tax treatment of equipment and refrigerant varies by state; confirm details with your accountant.', 'intermediate', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'amber', false, 50, array['Tracking equipment and refrigerant by job', 'Recording service call and return visit costs', 'Billing change orders for hidden conditions', 'Maintenance agreement revenue tracking', 'Deposits and progress billing for installs']::text[], null, 'Track equipment, refrigerant, line sets and labor by job so you can see which installs and service calls earn margin.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:hvac-hr')::uuid, 'hvac-hr', 'hvac', 'hr', 'Hiring and Training HVAC Technicians for Install and Service', 'Recruit and train install helpers and service technicians, with clear paths toward certification.', 'HVAC companies need install helpers and service technicians who can work independently and communicate well with customers. This course covers hiring for mechanical aptitude, training helpers on install and service, and planning certification steps. Wage, classification, and on-call pay rules vary by state; confirm them with your accountant.', 'beginner', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'rose', false, 60, array['Hiring install helpers and service techs', 'Training on install and service procedures', 'Planning certification steps', 'On-call and after-hours pay considerations', 'Retaining technicians through peak seasons']::text[], 'Hiring and Training HVAC Technicians for Install and Service', 'Recruit and train install helpers and service technicians, with clear paths toward certification.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:hvac-growth')::uuid, 'hvac-growth', 'hvac', 'growth', 'Maintenance Agreements and Repeat HVAC Service', 'Build recurring revenue with seasonal tune-ups, filter reminders and maintenance agreements for homes and businesses.', 'Equipment needs seasonal maintenance, which gives HVAC companies recurring revenue from tune-ups and agreements. This course covers designing maintenance agreements, reminder systems for seasonal visits, and renewal and referral programs for satisfied customers. Maintenance agreement terms and consumer contract rules vary by state; confirm them with your attorney.', 'intermediate', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'cyan', false, 70, array['Designing seasonal maintenance agreements', 'Reminder systems for tune-ups and filters', 'Renewal and referral programs', 'Upselling repairs found on maintenance visits', 'Tracking agreement renewals and churn']::text[], 'Maintenance Agreements and Repeat HVAC Service', 'Build recurring revenue with seasonal tune-ups, filter reminders and maintenance agreements for homes and businesses.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:hvac-safety')::uuid, 'hvac-safety', 'hvac', 'safety', 'HVAC Safety: Refrigerants, Gas Connections and Electrical Work', 'Handle refrigerants safely, check gas connections for leaks and lock out electrical work on equipment.', 'HVAC work exposes technicians to refrigerants, gas connections, high-voltage equipment, and tight attic and crawlspace spaces. This course covers refrigerant handling and recovery, leak checks on gas connections, lockout before electrical service, and safe access in attics and crawlspaces. Refrigerant, gas, and electrical rules vary by state and locality; confirm the requirements that apply to your work.', 'advanced', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'slate', false, 80, array['Refrigerant handling and recovery basics', 'Gas connection leak checks', 'Lockout before electrical service', 'Attic and crawlspace access safety', 'Rooftop and condenser pad lifting safety']::text[], null, 'Handle refrigerants safely, check gas connections for leaks and lock out electrical work on equipment.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:flooring-getting-started')::uuid, 'flooring-getting-started', 'flooring', 'getting_started', 'Starting a Flooring Business: Licensing, Insurance and Registration', 'Business basics for a flooring company, including licensing, liability coverage and registration for sub work.', 'Flooring businesses work in occupied homes and often install over subfloors that hide moisture or structural issues. This course covers business setup, licensing or registration requirements, liability coverage, and sub agreements with builders and remodelers. Licensing and registration rules vary by state and locality; confirm them with your licensing board.', 'beginner', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'slate', false, 10, array['Entity setup and tax registration basics', 'Licensing or registration for flooring work', 'Liability coverage for installs in occupied homes', 'Sub agreements with builders and remodelers', 'Choosing residential, commercial or both']::text[], null, 'Business basics for a flooring company, including licensing, liability coverage and registration for sub work.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:flooring-sales')::uuid, 'flooring-sales', 'flooring', 'sales', 'Selling Flooring Scope with Prep, Transitions and Waste Included', 'Show subfloor prep, underlayment, transitions and trim as their own lines so flooring quotes compare fairly.', 'Homeowners compare flooring quotes by material price per square foot and often miss subfloor repair, moisture testing, and transition strips. This course covers site visits that check subfloor and moisture, presenting material choices with installed price, and explaining why waste is part of the quantity. Material warranties vary by manufacturer; state them in writing.', 'intermediate', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'cyan', false, 20, array['Site visits that check subfloor and moisture', 'Presenting material choices with installed price', 'Explaining waste and why it is in the quantity', 'Transitions, trim and stair nosing scope', 'Writing proposals that show prep as its own line']::text[], null, 'Show subfloor prep, underlayment, transitions and trim as their own lines so flooring quotes compare fairly.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:flooring-estimating')::uuid, 'flooring-estimating', 'flooring', 'estimating', 'Flooring Estimates: Square Feet, Waste, Underlayment and Transitions', 'Measure rooms, add waste for patterns and diagonals, and price underlayment, transitions, trim and removal.', 'Flooring estimates start with room measurements, then add waste for diagonal and patterned installs, underlayment, adhesives, and transitions. Removal and subfloor repair change the price more than many customers expect. This course covers room-by-room takeoffs, waste factors by install pattern, and pricing for removal and disposal.', 'intermediate', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'navy', false, 30, array['Room-by-room square foot takeoffs', 'Waste factors for patterns and diagonals', 'Underlayment, adhesive and fastener quantities', 'Transitions, stairs and trim pieces', 'Removal, disposal and subfloor repair pricing']::text[], null, 'Measure rooms, add waste for patterns and diagonals, and price underlayment, transitions, trim and removal.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:flooring-project-management')::uuid, 'flooring-project-management', 'flooring', 'project_management', 'Sequencing Flooring Installs with Trim, Paint and Acclimation', 'Plan removal, subfloor prep, acclimation, installation and trim so flooring goes in after the heavy trades finish.', 'Flooring should go in after painting and heavy trades, and many materials need time to acclimate before installation. This course covers sequencing flooring with drywall, paint, and cabinet installs, planning acclimation time, and coordinating trim and transition work. Manufacturer acclimation and moisture guidance varies by product; follow the instructions for each material.', 'intermediate', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'green', false, 40, array['Sequencing flooring after paint and trades', 'Planning acclimation time for materials', 'Coordinating trim and transition installs', 'Protecting finished floors during construction', 'Walkthrough and care instructions at handoff']::text[], null, 'Plan removal, subfloor prep, acclimation, installation and trim so flooring goes in after the heavy trades finish.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:flooring-accounting')::uuid, 'flooring-accounting', 'flooring', 'accounting', 'Flooring Job Costing: Material Overages, Labor and Subfloor Surprises', 'Track material overages, install labor and subfloor repair by job so margins are visible on every floor.', 'Flooring margins shrink when waste runs higher than planned, subfloor repairs appear mid-job, or install labor takes longer. This course covers tracking material use against the takeoff, recording labor hours by room, and billing subfloor repairs as change orders. Tax treatment of materials and subcontracts varies by state; confirm details with your accountant.', 'intermediate', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'amber', false, 50, array['Tracking material use against the takeoff', 'Recording labor hours by room', 'Billing subfloor repairs as change orders', 'Recording leftover and returned material', 'Deposits and progress billing for floor jobs']::text[], null, 'Track material overages, install labor and subfloor repair by job so margins are visible on every floor.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:flooring-hr')::uuid, 'flooring-hr', 'flooring', 'hr', 'Hiring Floor Installers and Training Them for Consistent Seams', 'Recruit installers and helpers, then train for layout, seam quality, transitions and clean handoffs.', 'Flooring quality depends on layout, seam alignment, and clean transitions, and installers often learn these skills on the job. This course covers hiring installers and helpers, training on layout and cutting, and quality checks before a crew leaves a room. Wage and classification rules vary by state; confirm them with your accountant.', 'beginner', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'rose', false, 60, array['Hiring floor installers and helpers', 'Layout, cutting and seam alignment', 'Transition and threshold quality checks', 'Training on subfloor and moisture checks', 'Keeping installers through slow seasons']::text[], null, 'Recruit installers and helpers, then train for layout, seam quality, transitions and clean handoffs.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:flooring-growth')::uuid, 'flooring-growth', 'flooring', 'growth', 'Repeat Flooring Work from Builders, Realtors and Homeowners', 'Build repeat flooring work with builders, real estate contacts and homeowners who return for additional rooms.', 'Flooring work repeats with homeowners adding rooms, builders needing reliable subs, and real estate contacts preparing homes for sale. This course covers building relationships with builders and agents, following up after installs, and offering care or refinishing as repeat service. Marketing and advertising rules vary by locality.', 'intermediate', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'cyan', false, 70, array['Relationships with builders and sub lists', 'Working with real estate agents on listings', 'Follow-up after install and care instructions', 'Refinishing as repeat work', 'Tracking repeat clients by project type']::text[], 'Repeat Flooring Work from Builders, Realtors and Homeowners', 'Build repeat flooring work with builders, real estate contacts and homeowners who return for additional rooms.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:flooring-safety')::uuid, 'flooring-safety', 'flooring', 'safety', 'Flooring Safety: Adhesives, Dust, Heavy Material and Tools', 'Manage adhesive fumes, dust from sanding and cutting, heavy-material lifting and power tool hazards.', 'Flooring work involves adhesives with solvent fumes, dust from sanding and cutting, heavy rolls and planks, and power tools. This course covers ventilation around adhesives, dust control for sanding and refinishing, safe lifting and carrying, and tool guards for saws and nailers. Ventilation and dust rules vary by state and locality; confirm requirements for your materials.', 'advanced', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'slate', false, 80, array['Ventilation around adhesives and solvents', 'Dust control for sanding and refinishing', 'Safe lifting of rolls and heavy planks', 'Saw and nailer safety on install sites', 'Checking older floors for hazardous materials']::text[], 'Flooring Safety: Adhesives, Dust, Heavy Material and Tools', 'Manage adhesive fumes, dust from sanding and cutting, heavy-material lifting and power tool hazards.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:tile-getting-started')::uuid, 'tile-getting-started', 'tile', 'getting_started', 'Starting a Tile Business: Licensing, Insurance and Waterproofing', 'Business basics for a tile company, including licensing, liability coverage and the waterproofing methods you use.', 'Tile work often sits over wet areas where a failed membrane causes costly damage, so insurance and workmanship matter from the start. This course covers business setup, licensing or registration for tile work, liability coverage, and choosing the waterproofing methods your jobs require. Licensing and registration rules vary by state and locality; confirm them with your licensing board.', 'beginner', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'slate', false, 10, array['Entity setup and tax registration basics', 'Licensing or registration for tile work', 'Liability coverage for wet-area installs', 'Choosing waterproofing methods by job', 'Sub agreements with remodelers and builders']::text[], null, 'Business basics for a tile company, including licensing, liability coverage and the waterproofing methods you use.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:tile-sales')::uuid, 'tile-sales', 'tile', 'sales', 'Selling Large-Format and Specialty Tile Installs', 'Explain substrate flatness, layout and extra labor so large-format and specialty tile are priced honestly.', 'Large-format porcelain and specialty tile demand flatter substrates, more careful layout, and slower setting, and homeowners often do not see that in a tile price. This course covers site visits that check substrate flatness, presenting layout options and their waste, and writing prep and leveling into the scope. Material warranties vary by manufacturer; state them in writing.', 'intermediate', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'cyan', false, 20, array['Checking substrate flatness before quoting', 'Layout options and their waste', 'Explaining leveling and prep for large tile', 'Presenting mosaic and specialty tile options', 'Writing prep scope into the proposal']::text[], 'Selling Large-Format and Specialty Tile Installs', 'Explain substrate flatness, layout and extra labor so large-format and specialty tile are priced honestly.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:tile-estimating')::uuid, 'tile-estimating', 'tile', 'estimating', 'Tile Estimates: Backer Board, Membrane, Setting Materials and Labor', 'Price tile by square foot with backer board, waterproofing, setting materials, trim pieces and labor shown separately.', 'Tile estimates include tile area with waste, backer board, membrane, thinset, grout, and trim pieces, and labor changes with layout and pattern. Small rooms and niche work increase waste and cutting time. This course covers takeoffs by surface, waste for patterns and cut-heavy rooms, and pricing for membrane, setting materials and grout.', 'intermediate', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'navy', false, 30, array['Tile area and waste by pattern', 'Backer board and membrane quantities', 'Thinset, grout and sealer quantities', 'Trim pieces, niches and bullnose pricing', 'Labor by layout complexity']::text[], null, 'Price tile by square foot with backer board, waterproofing, setting materials, trim pieces and labor shown separately.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:tile-project-management')::uuid, 'tile-project-management', 'tile', 'project_management', 'Sequencing Tile Work Around Waterproofing, Cure and Fixtures', 'Plan substrate, membrane, setting, cure and grout so tile is not set over an untested surface or walked on too soon.', 'Tile needs a sound substrate, a tested membrane, and cure time before grout and fixtures go in. This course covers sequencing tile with plumbing and drywall, scheduling membrane tests and cure, and coordinating grout and sealing before final fixtures. Waterproofing test and cure requirements vary by product and locality; follow the manufacturer and local rules.', 'intermediate', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'green', false, 40, array['Substrate prep before membrane', 'Membrane test and cure scheduling', 'Setting, cure and grout timing', 'Coordinating fixtures after grout', 'Sealing and final cleaning']::text[], 'Sequencing Tile Work Around Waterproofing, Cure and Fixtures', 'Plan substrate, membrane, setting, cure and grout so tile is not set over an untested surface or walked on too soon.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:tile-accounting')::uuid, 'tile-accounting', 'tile', 'accounting', 'Tile Job Costing: Tile Overages, Setting Materials and Labor Hours', 'Track tile overages, setting materials and labor hours per job so you can see which tile work earns margin.', 'Tile margins slip with broken tile, unexpected leveling materials, and labor that runs over on tight layouts. This course covers tracking tile and setting material use, recording labor by phase, and billing substrate repairs and extra leveling as change orders. Tax treatment of materials and subcontracts varies by state; confirm details with your accountant.', 'intermediate', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'amber', false, 50, array['Tracking tile use and breakage', 'Setting materials and leveling products', 'Labor hours by phase and layout', 'Billing substrate repairs as change orders', 'Deposits and progress billing for tile jobs']::text[], null, 'Track tile overages, setting materials and labor hours per job so you can see which tile work earns margin.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:tile-hr')::uuid, 'tile-hr', 'tile', 'hr', 'Hiring Tile Setters and Training Them on Layout and Waterproofing', 'Recruit tile setters and helpers, then train on layout, lippage control and membrane details.', 'Tile quality depends on layout, lippage control, and waterproofing details, and skilled setters are hard to find. This course covers hiring tile setters and helpers, training on layout and cutting, and quality checks for flatness and grout lines. Wage and classification rules vary by state; confirm them with your accountant.', 'beginner', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'rose', false, 60, array['Interviewing for layout and cutting skill', 'Training helpers on mixing and setting', 'Lippage and flatness quality checks', 'Membrane detail standards', 'Retaining skilled setters']::text[], null, 'Recruit tile setters and helpers, then train on layout, lippage control and membrane details.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:tile-growth')::uuid, 'tile-growth', 'tile', 'growth', 'Repeat Tile Work from Remodelers, Builders and Homeowners', 'Earn steady tile work from remodelers, builders and homeowners who return for backsplashes and additional baths.', 'Tile work repeats with remodelers and builders who need dependable setters, and homeowners return for backsplashes and additional baths. This course covers building remodeler relationships, follow-up after installs, and care guides for grout and sealer. Marketing and advertising rules vary by locality.', 'intermediate', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'cyan', false, 70, array['Building relationships with remodelers', 'Dependable sub work for builders', 'Care guides for grout and sealer', 'Follow-up for backsplash and bath clients', 'Referral requests from finished customers']::text[], 'Repeat Tile Work from Remodelers, Builders and Homeowners', 'Earn steady tile work from remodelers, builders and homeowners who return for backsplashes and additional baths.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:tile-safety')::uuid, 'tile-safety', 'tile', 'safety', 'Tile Safety: Cutting Dust, Wet Saws and Heavy Slabs', 'Control silica dust from cutting, use wet saws safely and lift heavy tile and slabs without strain.', 'Tile cutting produces crystalline silica dust, wet saws carry electrical risk, and large-format tile and slabs are heavy. This course covers dust control for cutting, wet saw setup and electrical safety, and safe lifting and handling of large tile. Silica dust and workplace exposure rules vary by state and locality; confirm the requirements that apply to your work.', 'advanced', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'slate', false, 80, array['Dust control for dry and wet cutting', 'Wet saw setup and electrical safety', 'Respiratory protection for silica dust', 'Lifting and moving large-format tile', 'Handling slabs and vertical installs safely']::text[], 'Tile Safety: Cutting Dust, Wet Saws and Heavy Slabs', 'Control silica dust from cutting, use wet saws safely and lift heavy tile and slabs without strain.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:framing-getting-started')::uuid, 'framing-getting-started', 'framing', 'getting_started', 'Starting a Framing Business: Licensing, Insurance and Sub Work', 'Business basics for a framing company, including licensing, insurance and how you work as a sub for builders.', 'Framing crews usually work as subcontractors for builders and remodelers, and general contractors often require proof of insurance. This course covers business setup, licensing or registration for framing work, liability and workers'' comp coverage, and writing a sub agreement that defines the scope. Licensing and registration rules vary by state and locality; confirm them with your licensing board.', 'beginner', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'slate', false, 10, array['Entity setup and tax registration basics', 'Licensing or registration for framing work', 'Liability and workers'' comp for framing crews', 'Writing sub agreements that define scope', 'Choosing residential, commercial or both']::text[], null, 'Business basics for a framing company, including licensing, insurance and how you work as a sub for builders.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:framing-sales')::uuid, 'framing-sales', 'framing', 'sales', 'Quoting Framing Packages Against the Plans', 'Tie each framing quote to a plan set and stated assumptions so builders compare the same scope.', 'Builders often ask for framing numbers before plans are final, and quotes without stated assumptions are hard to compare. This course covers reading plan sets for framing scope, listing lumber grade and engineered-product assumptions, and handling changes after the plans are revised. Requirements for grade and engineered products vary by project and locality; follow the plans and the engineer''s specifications.', 'intermediate', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'cyan', false, 20, array['Reading plan sets for framing scope', 'Stating lumber grade and assumptions', 'Quoting from revised or incomplete plans', 'Handling engineered-product requirements', 'Writing packages that match the builder''s schedule']::text[], 'Quoting Framing Packages Against the Plans', 'Tie each framing quote to a plan set and stated assumptions so builders compare the same scope.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:framing-estimating')::uuid, 'framing-estimating', 'framing', 'estimating', 'Framing Takeoffs by System: Walls, Floors, Roofs and Hardware', 'Count lumber, sheathing, hardware and labor by system so each framing package is priced as a whole.', 'Framing takeoffs work best by system: wall linear footage, floor joist counts, roof rafter or truss counts, and sheathing area. Hardware such as hangers, straps, and connectors is easy to undercount and adds up across a house. This course covers building a takeoff by system, waste for cut-heavy walls, and pricing for hardware and engineered connectors.', 'intermediate', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'navy', false, 30, array['Wall linear footage and stud counts', 'Floor joist and beam takeoffs', 'Roof framing and truss counts', 'Sheathing area and waste factors', 'Hardware, straps and connector counts']::text[], null, 'Count lumber, sheathing, hardware and labor by system so each framing package is priced as a whole.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:framing-project-management')::uuid, 'framing-project-management', 'framing', 'project_management', 'Sequencing Framing with Foundations, Trusses and Inspections', 'Coordinate framing with foundation completion, truss deliveries, inspections and the next trade''s start date.', 'Framing depends on finished foundations, timely truss or lumber deliveries, and inspections before the next trade starts. This course covers scheduling framing crews around foundation completion, coordinating delivery windows, and planning sheathing and inspection holds. Inspection and engineered-product requirements vary by locality; confirm them with the building department and engineer.', 'intermediate', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'green', false, 40, array['Starting framing after foundation completion', 'Truss and lumber delivery coordination', 'Sheathing and weather-protection sequence', 'Framing inspection holds and approvals', 'Handing off to roofing, windows and MEP trades']::text[], 'Sequencing Framing with Foundations, Trusses and Inspections', 'Coordinate framing with foundation completion, truss deliveries, inspections and the next trade''s start date.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:framing-accounting')::uuid, 'framing-accounting', 'framing', 'accounting', 'Framing Job Costing: Lumber, Hardware and Crew Hours', 'Track lumber, sheathing, hardware and crew hours per framing job so you can see where the bid drifted.', 'Framing margins are sensitive to lumber prices, waste on complex plans, and hardware that was not in the bid. This course covers tracking lumber and hardware against the takeoff, recording crew hours by system, and billing changes when plans are revised. Tax treatment of materials and subcontracts varies by state; confirm details with your accountant.', 'intermediate', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'amber', false, 50, array['Matching lumber deliveries to the takeoff', 'Tracking hardware as its own line', 'Recording crew hours by system', 'Billing plan revisions as change orders', 'Progress billing tied to framing milestones']::text[], 'Framing Job Costing: Lumber, Hardware and Crew Hours', 'Track lumber, sheathing, hardware and crew hours per framing job so you can see where the bid drifted.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:framing-hr')::uuid, 'framing-hr', 'framing', 'hr', 'Building a Framing Crew That Reads Plans Accurately', 'Hire framers and helpers who read plans well, cut accurately and work safely at height.', 'Framing crews need people who read plans accurately, cut consistently, and move fast without sacrificing safety. This course covers hiring framers and helpers, training on plan reading and layout, and building a crew that can work in both wood and engineered products. Wage, classification, and overtime rules vary by state; confirm them with your accountant.', 'beginner', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'rose', false, 60, array['Interviewing framers for plan reading', 'Training helpers on layout and square', 'Working with engineered lumber and connectors', 'Pacing crews to a builder''s schedule', 'Keeping a framing crew through seasons']::text[], 'Building a Framing Crew That Reads Plans Accurately', 'Hire framers and helpers who read plans well, cut accurately and work safely at height.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:framing-growth')::uuid, 'framing-growth', 'framing', 'growth', 'Repeat Framing Work with Builders and Remodelers', 'Build a steady stream of framing work with production builders, custom builders and remodelers.', 'Framing work repeats with builders who run multiple houses and remodelers who need framing for additions and openings. This course covers building a reliable record with builder superintendents, following up after each framing phase, and offering framing for repairs and additions. Marketing and bidding rules vary by locality.', 'intermediate', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'cyan', false, 70, array['Building a record with builder superintendents', 'Bidding on repeat builder plans', 'Framing for remodelers and additions', 'Repair framing after storm or water damage', 'Tracking which builders send repeat work']::text[], 'Repeat Framing Work with Builders and Remodelers', 'Build a steady stream of framing work with production builders, custom builders and remodelers.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:framing-safety')::uuid, 'framing-safety', 'framing', 'safety', 'Framing Safety: Fall Protection, Lifting Walls and Temporary Bracing', 'Manage fall exposure on floors and roofs, safe wall lifting, and temporary bracing until sheathing is in.', 'Framing crews work on open floors and edges, lift heavy wall sections, and depend on temporary bracing until sheathing is in place. This course covers fall protection on floors and roof edges, crew lifts and bracing for walls, and nail gun safety. Fall protection and temporary bracing requirements vary by state and locality; confirm the rules that apply to your projects.', 'advanced', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'slate', false, 80, array['Fall protection on floors and roof edges', 'Lifting and bracing wall sections', 'Temporary bracing until sheathing is up', 'Nail gun and fastener safety', 'Working around open floor openings']::text[], null, 'Manage fall exposure on floors and roofs, safe wall lifting, and temporary bracing until sheathing is in.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:finish-carpentry-getting-started')::uuid, 'finish-carpentry-getting-started', 'finish-carpentry', 'getting_started', 'Starting a Finish Carpentry Business: Shop Setup and Insurance', 'Business basics for a finish carpentry company, including insurance, shop setup and licensing for remodel work.', 'Finish carpenters often work in occupied homes and run shops with power tools and finished materials. This course covers business setup, licensing or registration for remodel work, insurance for shop and jobsite operations, and planning a shop layout that supports installs. Licensing and home improvement rules vary by state and locality; confirm them with your licensing board.', 'beginner', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'slate', false, 10, array['Entity setup and tax registration basics', 'Licensing for remodel and trim work', 'Insurance for shop and jobsite operations', 'Planning a shop layout for installs', 'Choosing residential, commercial or both']::text[], null, 'Business basics for a finish carpentry company, including insurance, shop setup and licensing for remodel work.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:finish-carpentry-sales')::uuid, 'finish-carpentry-sales', 'finish-carpentry', 'sales', 'Presenting Trim and Millwork Proposals by Room', 'Show profile, material and labor for each room so trim proposals read as craft and not just linear feet.', 'Trim and millwork proposals are easy to misread when priced only by linear foot or by door count. This course covers presenting profiles and materials with photos, pricing by room or by system, and explaining the difference between painted and stained finishes. Material and finish warranties vary; state them in writing.', 'intermediate', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'cyan', false, 20, array['Profile and material samples for clients', 'Pricing by room or by system', 'Painted versus stained finish options', 'Presenting built-ins with drawings', 'Writing proposals that show the craft']::text[], 'Presenting Trim and Millwork Proposals by Room', 'Show profile, material and labor for each room so trim proposals read as craft and not just linear feet.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:finish-carpentry-estimating')::uuid, 'finish-carpentry-estimating', 'finish-carpentry', 'estimating', 'Finish Carpentry Estimates: Linear Footage, Doors and Built-Ins', 'Price trim by linear footage, doors and built-ins by unit, with cutting, fitting and finish time shown.', 'Finish carpentry estimates combine linear footage of trim, door counts, and built-in units, plus the cutting and fitting time that real rooms require. Out-of-square walls, scribing, and difficult corners add hours that are easy to miss. This course covers takeoffs by room, pricing for doors and hardware, and allowances for built-ins and custom millwork.', 'intermediate', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'navy', false, 30, array['Linear footage takeoffs by room', 'Door and hardware counts', 'Scribing and out-of-square allowances', 'Built-in units and custom millwork', 'Finish, stain and touch-up time']::text[], null, 'Price trim by linear footage, doors and built-ins by unit, with cutting, fitting and finish time shown.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:finish-carpentry-project-management')::uuid, 'finish-carpentry-project-management', 'finish-carpentry', 'project_management', 'Sequencing Trim and Doors Around Paint, Flooring and Final Inspections', 'Install finish carpentry after drywall and before paint, then coordinate final inspections and touch-up.', 'Finish carpentry usually follows drywall and comes before paint and flooring, and the order decides how much touch-up is needed. This course covers sequencing trim and doors within the build, coordinating with painters and flooring installers, and planning punch-list visits. Final inspection timing varies by locality; confirm the requirements before scheduling.', 'intermediate', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'green', false, 40, array['Trim and door timing relative to paint', 'Coordinating with flooring installers', 'Prefinishing and when to do it', 'Punch-list visits and touch-up scheduling', 'Final walkthrough and homeowner handoff']::text[], null, 'Install finish carpentry after drywall and before paint, then coordinate final inspections and touch-up.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:finish-carpentry-accounting')::uuid, 'finish-carpentry-accounting', 'finish-carpentry', 'accounting', 'Finish Carpentry Job Costing: Materials, Waste and Shop Hours', 'Track millwork materials, shop hours and install hours per job so you know which trim packages make money.', 'Finish carpentry margins shift with material waste, shop hours that run long, and installs that need return visits. This course covers tracking lumber and millwork by job, recording shop and install hours separately, and billing change orders for owner-driven changes. Tax treatment of materials and shop expenses varies by state; confirm details with your accountant.', 'intermediate', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'amber', false, 50, array['Tracking millwork materials by job', 'Separating shop hours from install hours', 'Recording waste and returned stock', 'Billing owner-driven changes', 'Deposits and progress billing for trim work']::text[], null, 'Track millwork materials, shop hours and install hours per job so you know which trim packages make money.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:finish-carpentry-hr')::uuid, 'finish-carpentry-hr', 'finish-carpentry', 'hr', 'Training Finish Carpenters in Cuts, Fit and Shop Practice', 'Build finish carpenters who cut clean miters, scribe accurately and keep the shop organized.', 'Finish quality depends on clean miters, accurate scribing, and tidy shop practice, and those skills take years to develop. This course covers hiring for finish skill, training helpers on cutting and fitting, and building a shop routine that keeps materials organized. Wage and classification rules vary by state; confirm them with your accountant.', 'beginner', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'rose', false, 60, array['Interviewing for finish carpentry skill', 'Cutting miters and coped joints', 'Scribing to uneven walls', 'Shop routine and material organization', 'Keeping skilled finish carpenters']::text[], 'Training Finish Carpenters in Cuts, Fit and Shop Practice', 'Build finish carpenters who cut clean miters, scribe accurately and keep the shop organized.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:finish-carpentry-growth')::uuid, 'finish-carpentry-growth', 'finish-carpentry', 'growth', 'Repeat Trim and Built-In Work from Remodelers and Homeowners', 'Earn repeat work from remodelers, designers and homeowners who return for built-ins and interior doors.', 'Finish carpentry work repeats with remodelers who need reliable trim crews, designers who specify custom millwork, and homeowners adding built-ins over time. This course covers building remodeler and designer relationships, follow-up after installs, and offering maintenance such as door adjustments. Marketing and advertising rules vary by locality.', 'intermediate', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'cyan', false, 70, array['Building relationships with remodelers', 'Working with interior designers', 'Follow-up and door adjustment visits', 'Referrals from finished homeowners', 'Portfolio photos with client permission']::text[], 'Repeat Trim and Built-In Work from Remodelers and Homeowners', 'Earn repeat work from remodelers, designers and homeowners who return for built-ins and interior doors.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:finish-carpentry-safety')::uuid, 'finish-carpentry-safety', 'finish-carpentry', 'safety', 'Finish Carpentry Safety: Power Tools, Dust and Ladder Work', 'Use table and miter saws safely, control wood dust and manage ladder and overhead work during installs.', 'Finish carpenters rely on table saws, miter saws, routers, and nailers, and wood dust and ladder work create hazards during installs. This course covers saw guards and push tools, dust collection and respiratory protection, and safe ladder use for trim and door work. Shop and jobsite safety rules vary by state and locality; confirm requirements that apply to your business.', 'advanced', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'slate', false, 80, array['Table saw and miter saw guards', 'Push tools and kickback prevention', 'Wood dust collection and respiratory protection', 'Ladder use for trim and door work', 'Nailer and router safety on site']::text[], 'Finish Carpentry Safety: Power Tools, Dust and Ladder Work', 'Use table and miter saws safely, control wood dust and manage ladder and overhead work during installs.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:cabinets-countertops-getting-started')::uuid, 'cabinets-countertops-getting-started', 'cabinets-countertops', 'getting_started', 'Starting a Cabinet and Countertop Business: Licensing and Insurance', 'Business basics for a cabinet and countertop company, including licensing, insurance and fabricator relationships.', 'Cabinet and countertop businesses handle heavy materials, stone, and plumbing or electrical cutouts that touch other trades. This course covers business setup, licensing or registration for cabinet and countertop installation, insurance for installs, and relationships with stone fabricators. Licensing rules vary by state and locality; confirm them with your licensing board.', 'beginner', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'slate', false, 10, array['Entity setup and tax registration basics', 'Licensing for cabinet and counter installation', 'Insurance for installs in occupied homes', 'Working with stone fabricators', 'Choosing residential, commercial or both']::text[], null, 'Business basics for a cabinet and countertop company, including licensing, insurance and fabricator relationships.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:cabinets-countertops-sales')::uuid, 'cabinets-countertops-sales', 'cabinets-countertops', 'sales', 'Making Cabinet and Countertop Selections Obvious in the Proposal', 'Spell out cabinet lines, counter material, edge profile and cutouts so the customer knows what is being bought.', 'Cabinet and countertop proposals fail when selections are vague, and customers only see the real cost once cutouts or edge profiles are added. This course covers writing selections with model, finish, edge profile, and cutouts, presenting alternates, and confirming choices before fabrication. Product warranties vary by manufacturer; state terms in writing.', 'intermediate', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'cyan', false, 20, array['Writing selections with finish and model', 'Presenting edge profiles and cutout options', 'Alternates for cabinet and counter upgrades', 'Confirming selections before fabrication', 'Handling the ''showroom sample'' expectation']::text[], null, 'Spell out cabinet lines, counter material, edge profile and cutouts so the customer knows what is being bought.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:cabinets-countertops-estimating')::uuid, 'cabinets-countertops-estimating', 'cabinets-countertops', 'estimating', 'Cabinet and Countertop Estimates: Linear Feet, Fillers and Cutouts', 'Price cabinet linear footage, fillers, hardware, counter square footage, cutouts and install labor line by line.', 'Cabinet estimates depend on linear footage, fillers, hardware, and install time, and countertop estimates depend on square footage, edges, and cutouts. Templating and fabrication lead times can change the schedule as much as the price. This course covers takeoffs for cabinets and counters, pricing cutouts and backsplash, and allowances for selections not yet made.', 'intermediate', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'navy', false, 30, array['Cabinet linear footage and filler pieces', 'Counter square footage and edge profiles', 'Cutouts for sinks, cooktops and faucets', 'Backsplash and wall-tile line items', 'Allowances for selections not yet made']::text[], null, 'Price cabinet linear footage, fillers, hardware, counter square footage, cutouts and install labor line by line.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:cabinets-countertops-project-management')::uuid, 'cabinets-countertops-project-management', 'cabinets-countertops', 'project_management', 'Scheduling Templating, Fabrication and Install Around Other Trades', 'Coordinate cabinet install, counter templating, fabrication lead times and plumbing and electrical rough-in.', 'Counter templating happens only after cabinets are set, and fabrication lead times set the calendar for the final install. This course covers sequencing cabinet install with plumbing and electrical rough-in, scheduling templates and fabrication, and coordinating sink and cooktop delivery. Schedules depend on fabricator and supplier lead times; confirm them before committing a date.', 'intermediate', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'green', false, 40, array['Cabinet install after rough-in', 'Templating after cabinets are set', 'Fabrication lead times and delivery windows', 'Coordinating sink and appliance delivery', 'Final counter install and plumbing hookup']::text[], null, 'Coordinate cabinet install, counter templating, fabrication lead times and plumbing and electrical rough-in.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:cabinets-countertops-accounting')::uuid, 'cabinets-countertops-accounting', 'cabinets-countertops', 'accounting', 'Cabinet and Countertop Job Costing: Stone, Fabrication and Returns', 'Track stone, cabinet and fabrication costs per job so margins are clear after returns, remakes and cutouts.', 'Stone and cabinet margins slip with remakes, damaged slabs, and fabrication changes made after templating. This course covers tracking cabinet and stone costs by job, recording remakes and damage, and billing selection changes as change orders. Tax treatment of materials and fabrication varies by state; confirm details with your accountant.', 'intermediate', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'amber', false, 50, array['Tracking cabinet and stone costs by job', 'Recording remakes and damaged slabs', 'Billing selection and template changes', 'Fabricator invoices against the estimate', 'Deposits and progress billing for cabinet jobs']::text[], null, 'Track stone, cabinet and fabrication costs per job so margins are clear after returns, remakes and cutouts.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:cabinets-countertops-hr')::uuid, 'cabinets-countertops-hr', 'cabinets-countertops', 'hr', 'Training Installers for Cabinets, Counters and Careful Handling', 'Build installers who level and shim cabinets, set counters and protect finished surfaces during the install.', 'Cabinet and counter quality depends on leveling, shimming, and protecting finished surfaces during install. This course covers training installers on cabinet leveling and fastening, counter setting and seam alignment, and handling stone safely. Wage and classification rules vary by state; confirm them with your accountant.', 'beginner', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'rose', false, 60, array['Cabinet leveling, shimming and fastening', 'Counter setting and seam alignment', 'Protecting finished surfaces during install', 'Handling stone slabs and tops', 'Keeping installers through slow periods']::text[], null, 'Build installers who level and shim cabinets, set counters and protect finished surfaces during the install.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:cabinets-countertops-growth')::uuid, 'cabinets-countertops-growth', 'cabinets-countertops', 'growth', 'Repeat Cabinet and Counter Work from Designers and Remodelers', 'Earn repeat work from designers, remodelers and homeowners who return for laundry rooms, baths and refacing.', 'Cabinet and counter work repeats with designers who specify lines, remodelers who need reliable installers, and homeowners who add laundry or bath cabinets later. This course covers relationships with designers and remodelers, follow-up after installs, and refacing as a repeat service. Marketing and advertising rules vary by locality.', 'intermediate', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'cyan', false, 70, array['Relationships with interior designers', 'Reliable install work for remodelers', 'Follow-up after cabinet and counter installs', 'Refacing as repeat work', 'Referrals from finished kitchens and baths']::text[], null, 'Earn repeat work from designers, remodelers and homeowners who return for laundry rooms, baths and refacing.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:cabinets-countertops-safety')::uuid, 'cabinets-countertops-safety', 'cabinets-countertops', 'safety', 'Cabinet and Stone Safety: Heavy Lifts, Silica Dust and Tools', 'Lift heavy tops and cabinets safely, control stone dust during cutting and handle tools and adhesives properly.', 'Installing stone tops and heavy cabinets involves lifting hazards, and cutting stone creates silica dust. This course covers team lifts and mechanical aids for tops, dust control when cutting or drilling stone, and safe use of saws, drills, and adhesives. Silica dust and lifting rules vary by state and locality; confirm the requirements that apply to your work.', 'advanced', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'slate', false, 80, array['Team lifts and aids for stone tops', 'Dust control when cutting or drilling stone', 'Respiratory protection for silica dust', 'Safe use of saws, drills and adhesives', 'Securing tall cabinets during install']::text[], 'Cabinet and Stone Safety: Heavy Lifts, Silica Dust and Tools', 'Lift heavy tops and cabinets safely, control stone dust during cutting and handle tools and adhesives properly.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:windows-doors-getting-started')::uuid, 'windows-doors-getting-started', 'windows-doors', 'getting_started', 'Starting a Window and Door Business: Licensing and Insurance', 'Business basics for a window and door company, including licensing, insurance and manufacturer warranty rules.', 'Window and door installers work in building envelopes, where a poor install can cause water intrusion that shows up years later. This course covers business setup, licensing or registration for installation, insurance for work at height, and manufacturer installer programs and warranty rules. Licensing and home improvement contract rules vary by state and locality; confirm them with your licensing board.', 'beginner', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'slate', false, 10, array['Entity setup and tax registration basics', 'Licensing or registration for window installs', 'Insurance for work at height', 'Manufacturer installer programs and warranty', 'Choosing residential, commercial or both']::text[], 'Starting a Window and Door Business: Licensing and Insurance', 'Business basics for a window and door company, including licensing, insurance and manufacturer warranty rules.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:windows-doors-sales')::uuid, 'windows-doors-sales', 'windows-doors', 'sales', 'Choosing Per-Unit or Package Pricing for Window Quotes', 'Decide how customers see your pricing, then present unit, install and trim costs in a way that matches that choice.', 'Some customers want per-window pricing so they can choose units, while others prefer one package that covers all openings. This course covers the tradeoffs of each approach, presenting options with clear install and trim lines, and explaining why a low unit price can leave out flashing or disposal. Warranty terms vary by manufacturer; state them in writing.', 'intermediate', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'cyan', false, 20, array['Per-unit versus package pricing tradeoffs', 'Presenting install, trim and flashing lines', 'Explaining why a low unit price excludes work', 'Handling the ''I can buy the windows myself'' request', 'Writing proposals with clear openings schedule']::text[], 'Choosing Per-Unit or Package Pricing for Window Quotes', 'Decide how customers see your pricing, then present unit, install and trim costs in a way that matches that choice.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:windows-doors-estimating')::uuid, 'windows-doors-estimating', 'windows-doors', 'estimating', 'Window and Door Estimates: Units, Installation, Trim and Disposal', 'Price each opening with its unit, install labor, flashing, trim and old-unit disposal in one organized schedule.', 'Window and door estimates start with an opening schedule, then add units, install labor, flashing materials, interior and exterior trim, and disposal of removed units. Rough opening condition and the need for framing repair change labor more than many customers expect. This course covers measuring openings, building an opening schedule, and pricing removal, flashing, and repairs.', 'intermediate', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'navy', false, 30, array['Building an opening schedule', 'Measuring rough openings and checking square', 'Flashing materials and labor by opening', 'Trim, sill and exterior casing pricing', 'Removal, disposal and framing repair allowances']::text[], null, 'Price each opening with its unit, install labor, flashing, trim and old-unit disposal in one organized schedule.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:windows-doors-project-management')::uuid, 'windows-doors-project-management', 'windows-doors', 'project_management', 'Ordering and Scheduling Window and Door Installs', 'Plan order lead times, delivery checks and install days so openings are protected from weather.', 'Window and door units often have long lead times, and an opening left open overnight risks water damage. This course covers verifying measurements before ordering, scheduling deliveries around install days, and planning temporary weather protection for openings not yet completed. Lead times vary by manufacturer; confirm them when you quote.', 'intermediate', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'green', false, 40, array['Verifying measurements before ordering', 'Lead times and delivery coordination', 'Install day sequencing by floor or elevation', 'Temporary weather protection for openings', 'Coordinating with siding and trim trades']::text[], 'Ordering and Scheduling Window and Door Installs', 'Plan order lead times, delivery checks and install days so openings are protected from weather.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:windows-doors-accounting')::uuid, 'windows-doors-accounting', 'windows-doors', 'accounting', 'Window and Door Job Costing: Units, Returns and Installation Time', 'Track unit costs, return and replacement charges, and install hours so you can see what each job earned.', 'Window and door margins shrink with wrong-size units, damaged glass, and installs that take longer than planned. This course covers tracking unit costs by opening, recording returns and replacements, and billing changes for hidden rough-opening problems. Tax treatment of materials and subcontracts varies by state; confirm details with your accountant.', 'intermediate', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'amber', false, 50, array['Tracking unit costs by opening', 'Recording wrong-size and damaged units', 'Install hours by opening and floor', 'Billing rough-opening change orders', 'Deposits and progress billing for unit orders']::text[], null, 'Track unit costs, return and replacement charges, and install hours so you can see what each job earned.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:windows-doors-hr')::uuid, 'windows-doors-hr', 'windows-doors', 'hr', 'Training Window and Door Installers in Flashing and Squaring', 'Build installer habits for flashing order, squaring units and checking operation before the crew leaves.', 'Window and door quality depends on flashing order, square and plumb setting, and checking operation before leaving. This course covers training installers on flashing sequence, shimming and fastening, and a final operation and seal check. Wage and classification rules vary by state; confirm them with your accountant.', 'beginner', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'rose', false, 60, array['Flashing sequence for new installers', 'Shimming, squaring and fastening units', 'Operation and seal checks before leaving', 'Pairing new installers with leads', 'Keeping installers through the season']::text[], 'Training Window and Door Installers in Flashing and Squaring', 'Build installer habits for flashing order, squaring units and checking operation before the crew leaves.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:windows-doors-growth')::uuid, 'windows-doors-growth', 'windows-doors', 'growth', 'Repeat Window and Door Work from Homeowners and Builders', 'Build repeat work from homeowners who add openings, builders who need reliable installers and service calls.', 'Window and door work repeats with homeowners who upgrade whole floors, builders who need reliable installers, and service calls for adjustments and hardware. This course covers follow-up after installs, adjustment and service visits, and relationships with builders and remodelers. Marketing and warranty service rules vary by locality and manufacturer.', 'intermediate', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'cyan', false, 70, array['Follow-up after the install is complete', 'Adjustment and warranty service visits', 'Working with builders on recurring orders', 'Referrals from finished homes', 'Tracking repeat clients by project']::text[], 'Repeat Window and Door Work from Homeowners and Builders', 'Build repeat work from homeowners who add openings, builders who need reliable installers and service calls.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:windows-doors-safety')::uuid, 'windows-doors-safety', 'windows-doors', 'safety', 'Window and Door Install Safety: Glass Handling, Ladders and Lifting', 'Handle glass and heavy units safely, manage ladder and lift work at height and protect crews from debris.', 'Window and door installs involve heavy, fragile glass, ladder and lift work at height, and debris from removed units. This course covers team lifts and carts for large units, glass handling, ladder and lift setup, and debris control around the work zone. Safety rules for lifts and glass handling vary by state and locality; confirm the requirements for your jobs.', 'advanced', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'slate', false, 80, array['Team lifts and carts for large units', 'Safe glass handling and transport', 'Ladder and lift setup for upper openings', 'Debris control around the work zone', 'Protecting occupants and pets during installs']::text[], null, 'Handle glass and heavy units safely, manage ladder and lift work at height and protect crews from debris.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:insulation-getting-started')::uuid, 'insulation-getting-started', 'insulation', 'getting_started', 'Starting an Insulation Business: Licensing and Insurance', 'Business basics for an insulation company, including licensing, insurance and manufacturer certifications.', 'Insulation work happens in attics, walls, and crawlspaces, and spray foam requires specific equipment and training. This course covers business setup, licensing or registration for insulation work, liability coverage, and manufacturer certifications required for some products. Licensing and certification rules vary by state and locality; confirm them with your licensing board.', 'beginner', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'slate', false, 10, array['Entity setup and tax registration basics', 'Licensing or registration for insulation', 'Liability coverage for attic and crawlspace work', 'Manufacturer certifications for spray foam', 'Choosing residential, commercial or both']::text[], 'Starting an Insulation Business: Licensing and Insurance', 'Business basics for an insulation company, including licensing, insurance and manufacturer certifications.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:insulation-sales')::uuid, 'insulation-sales', 'insulation', 'sales', 'Explaining Air Sealing, Baffles and Insulation Depth', 'Show customers why air sealing and baffles come before insulation depth, so the bid covers what makes the job perform.', 'Homeowners often want a deeper blanket of insulation and do not know that air leaks and blocked soffit vents can undo much of the benefit. This course covers attic inspections, explaining air sealing and baffles in plain terms, and presenting insulation depth options with their tradeoffs. Energy program and incentive eligibility vary by location; confirm details with the program administrator.', 'intermediate', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'cyan', false, 20, array['Attic inspections and what to photograph', 'Air sealing before insulation depth', 'Baffles and ventilation pathways explained', 'Presenting depth and material options', 'Handling energy incentive questions']::text[], 'Explaining Air Sealing, Baffles and Insulation Depth', 'Show customers why air sealing and baffles come before insulation depth, so the bid covers what makes the job perform.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:insulation-estimating')::uuid, 'insulation-estimating', 'insulation', 'estimating', 'Insulation Estimates: Square Feet, Depth, Air Sealing and Materials', 'Price insulation by square foot and target depth, with air sealing, baffles and material yields shown clearly.', 'Insulation estimates depend on area, target R-value or depth, material yield, and the air sealing and baffle work the attic or wall needs. Existing insulation removal and obstructions add labor that is often missed. This course covers area and depth takeoffs, material yield calculations, and pricing for air sealing, baffles, and removal.', 'intermediate', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'navy', false, 30, array['Square footage and target depth takeoffs', 'Material yield and coverage calculations', 'Air sealing and penetration pricing', 'Baffles and vent pathway allowances', 'Old insulation removal and disposal']::text[], null, 'Price insulation by square foot and target depth, with air sealing, baffles and material yields shown clearly.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:insulation-project-management')::uuid, 'insulation-project-management', 'insulation', 'project_management', 'Sequencing Insulation Work with Air Sealing, Drywall and Inspections', 'Coordinate air sealing, insulation, inspections and drywall so the envelope is sealed before walls close.', 'Insulation and air sealing should happen before drywall in new work, and in existing homes they often follow electrical or plumbing repairs. This course covers scheduling air sealing and insulation around other trades, coordinating inspections before closing walls, and planning attic access and occupant protection. Inspection and energy code requirements vary by locality; confirm them early.', 'intermediate', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'green', false, 40, array['Air sealing before drywall in new work', 'Coordinating with electricians and plumbers', 'Inspection timing before walls close', 'Attic access and occupant protection', 'Scheduling blown-in and spray foam days']::text[], null, 'Coordinate air sealing, insulation, inspections and drywall so the envelope is sealed before walls close.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:insulation-accounting')::uuid, 'insulation-accounting', 'insulation', 'accounting', 'Insulation Job Costing: Material Yield, Labor and Disposal', 'Track material yield, crew hours and removal costs per job so you can see what each insulation job earned.', 'Insulation margins depend on material yield, crew productivity in tight spaces, and removal and disposal of old material. This course covers tracking material use against yield estimates, recording labor hours by space, and billing removal and obstruction changes as change orders. Tax treatment of materials and subcontracts varies by state; confirm details with your accountant.', 'intermediate', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'amber', false, 50, array['Tracking material use against yield', 'Recording labor hours by attic and wall area', 'Pricing removal and disposal separately', 'Billing obstruction changes', 'Deposits and progress billing for insulation jobs']::text[], 'Insulation Job Costing: Material Yield, Labor and Disposal', 'Track material yield, crew hours and removal costs per job so you can see what each insulation job earned.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:insulation-hr')::uuid, 'insulation-hr', 'insulation', 'hr', 'Training Insulation Installers for Coverage and Air Sealing Quality', 'Build installers who achieve even coverage, seal penetrations correctly and document work for inspection.', 'Insulation performance depends on even coverage, complete air sealing, and clean documentation for inspections. This course covers training installers on coverage checks, sealing penetrations, and photographing work before it is covered. Wage, classification, and overtime rules vary by state; confirm them with your accountant.', 'beginner', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'rose', false, 60, array['Coverage checks and depth markers', 'Sealing penetrations and top plates', 'Photographing work before it is covered', 'Working in tight attic and crawlspace spaces', 'Keeping installers through slow seasons']::text[], null, 'Build installers who achieve even coverage, seal penetrations correctly and document work for inspection.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:insulation-growth')::uuid, 'insulation-growth', 'insulation', 'growth', 'Repeat Insulation Work from Energy Upgrades and Builders', 'Build repeat work from energy upgrade projects, builders and homeowners who return after a first job.', 'Insulation work repeats with homeowners who upgrade in stages, builders who need reliable crews, and energy auditors who refer work. This course covers building relationships with builders and auditors, follow-up after installs, and offering follow-up inspections. Energy program rules and marketing requirements vary by location; confirm them with program administrators.', 'intermediate', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'cyan', false, 70, array['Relationships with builders and auditors', 'Follow-up inspections after installs', 'Staged upgrades for returning homeowners', 'Referrals from finished projects', 'Tracking repeat clients and project types']::text[], 'Repeat Insulation Work from Energy Upgrades and Builders', 'Build repeat work from energy upgrade projects, builders and homeowners who return after a first job.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:insulation-safety')::uuid, 'insulation-safety', 'insulation', 'safety', 'Insulation Safety: Respiratory Protection and Attic Heat', 'Protect crews from insulation dust and fibers, manage attic heat and handle spray foam chemicals safely.', 'Insulation work exposes crews to fibers and dust, hot attics, and spray foam chemicals that require ventilation and protective gear. This course covers respiratory protection and protective clothing, managing heat stress in attics and crawlspaces, and safe handling of spray foam. Respiratory and chemical handling rules vary by state and locality; confirm the requirements that apply to your work.', 'advanced', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'slate', false, 80, array['Respiratory protection for fibers and dust', 'Protective clothing for insulation work', 'Heat stress management in attics', 'Spray foam chemical handling and ventilation', 'Crawlspace access and moisture hazards']::text[], 'Insulation Safety: Respiratory Protection and Attic Heat', 'Protect crews from insulation dust and fibers, manage attic heat and handle spray foam chemicals safely.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:gutters-getting-started')::uuid, 'gutters-getting-started', 'gutters', 'getting_started', 'Starting a Gutter Company: Licensing, Insurance and Service Area', 'Business basics for a gutter company, including licensing, insurance and choosing your service area.', 'Gutter installers work at height on occupied homes and often install around roofing and siding. This course covers business setup, licensing or registration for exterior work, insurance for ladder and lift work, and choosing a service area that fits your crew. Licensing and registration rules vary by state and locality; confirm them with your licensing board.', 'beginner', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'slate', false, 10, array['Entity setup and tax registration basics', 'Licensing or registration for exterior work', 'Insurance for ladder and lift work', 'Choosing a service area and crew size', 'Seasonal planning for a gutter business']::text[], null, 'Business basics for a gutter company, including licensing, insurance and choosing your service area.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:gutters-sales')::uuid, 'gutters-sales', 'gutters', 'sales', 'Presenting Gutter Quotes with Guards, Downspouts and Removal Clear', 'Show each gutter line item, from guards and downspout extensions to removal, so the customer compares fairly.', 'Gutter quotes are easy to misread when a per-foot price leaves out guards, downspout extensions, and removal of old gutters. This course covers presenting gutter options with clear line items, explaining guard types and their maintenance needs, and walking the customer through drainage and grading issues found on site. Warranty terms vary by manufacturer; state them in writing.', 'intermediate', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'cyan', false, 20, array['Presenting line items for guards and extensions', 'Explaining guard types and maintenance', 'Removing and disposing of old gutters', 'Drainage and grading issues found on site', 'Writing proposals that show every line']::text[], null, 'Show each gutter line item, from guards and downspout extensions to removal, so the customer compares fairly.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:gutters-estimating')::uuid, 'gutters-estimating', 'gutters', 'estimating', 'Gutter Estimates: Linear Feet, Downspouts, Corners and Guards', 'Price gutter runs by linear foot with downspouts, end caps, corners, hangers and guards shown separately.', 'Gutter estimates start with linear feet of run, then add downspouts, outlets, corners, end caps, hangers, and guards. Complex rooflines and multiple stories change access time and the number of corners. This course covers measuring runs and roof edges, counting downspouts and outlets, and pricing for guards, removal, and access.', 'intermediate', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'navy', false, 30, array['Linear feet and run measurements', 'Downspout and outlet counts', 'Corners, end caps and hanger spacing', 'Guard types and their pricing', 'Access and multi-story pricing']::text[], null, 'Price gutter runs by linear foot with downspouts, end caps, corners, hangers and guards shown separately.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:gutters-project-management')::uuid, 'gutters-project-management', 'gutters', 'project_management', 'Scheduling Gutter Installs Around Roofing and Siding Work', 'Coordinate gutter installs after roofing and siding, and plan weather days and pickup of removed material.', 'Gutters usually go on after roofing and siding are finished, and roofing crews can damage new gutters if the order is wrong. This course covers sequencing gutter installs with roofing and siding subs, planning around weather for seamless fabrication, and coordinating debris removal. Permit and inspection requirements vary by locality; confirm them before scheduling.', 'intermediate', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'green', false, 40, array['Sequencing gutters after roofing and siding', 'Protecting new gutters from other trades', 'Weather planning for seamless fabrication', 'Coordinating debris removal and cleanup', 'Final drainage check with the homeowner']::text[], 'Scheduling Gutter Installs Around Roofing and Siding Work', 'Coordinate gutter installs after roofing and siding, and plan weather days and pickup of removed material.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:gutters-accounting')::uuid, 'gutters-accounting', 'gutters', 'accounting', 'Gutter Job Costing: Material Runs, Guards and Labor Hours', 'Track material runs, guard use and crew hours by job so you can compare each gutter job to its bid.', 'Gutter margins shift with run length, guard costs, and labor on complex rooflines. This course covers tracking material by run and job, recording guard and accessory use, and billing extra access or repairs found during install. Tax treatment of materials and subcontracts varies by state; confirm details with your accountant.', 'intermediate', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'amber', false, 50, array['Tracking material by run and job', 'Recording guard and accessory use', 'Labor hours by roofline complexity', 'Billing repairs found during install', 'Deposits and progress billing for gutter work']::text[], 'Gutter Job Costing: Material Runs, Guards and Labor Hours', 'Track material runs, guard use and crew hours by job so you can compare each gutter job to its bid.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:gutters-hr')::uuid, 'gutters-hr', 'gutters', 'hr', 'Training Gutter Installers for Pitch, Seams and Clean Work', 'Build installer skills for correct pitch, tight seams and clean finishes on every downspout run.', 'Gutter quality depends on correct pitch, sealed seams, and tidy downspout runs, and those details take practice. This course covers training installers on pitch and drainage, seam and joint sealing, and quality checks before a crew leaves a home. Wage and classification rules vary by state; confirm them with your accountant.', 'beginner', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'rose', false, 60, array['Pitch and drainage fundamentals', 'Seam and joint sealing', 'Downspout routing and attachment', 'Quality checks before leaving a home', 'Keeping installers through the season']::text[], 'Training Gutter Installers for Pitch, Seams and Clean Work', 'Build installer skills for correct pitch, tight seams and clean finishes on every downspout run.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:gutters-growth')::uuid, 'gutters-growth', 'gutters', 'growth', 'Gutter Cleaning, Guard Service and Repeat Work', 'Offer seasonal cleaning, guard service and repairs to past gutter customers, plus referrals from roofers and neighbors.', 'Gutters need seasonal cleaning and repairs, which gives a gutter company steady repeat work after the install. This course covers seasonal cleaning and inspection packages, reminders for leaf season and storm checks, and referral relationships with roofers and home inspectors. Marketing and solicitation rules vary by locality.', 'intermediate', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'cyan', false, 70, array['Seasonal cleaning and inspection packages', 'Reminders for leaf season and storm checks', 'Repair and guard service calls', 'Referral relationships with roofers', 'Tracking repeat clients and service dates']::text[], 'Gutter Cleaning, Guard Service and Repeat Work', 'Offer seasonal cleaning, guard service and repairs to past gutter customers, plus referrals from roofers and neighbors.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:gutters-safety')::uuid, 'gutters-safety', 'gutters', 'safety', 'Ladder and Roofline Safety for Gutter Crews', 'Set up ladders and lifts safely, manage roofline work near power lines and protect crews on wet surfaces.', 'Gutter installers work on ladders and lifts at the roofline, often near overhead power lines and on wet surfaces. This course covers ladder setup and three-point contact, lift operation, clearances from power lines, and fall protection where the work requires it. Ladder, lift, and fall protection rules vary by state and locality; confirm the requirements for your jobs.', 'advanced', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'slate', false, 80, array['Ladder setup and three-point contact', 'Lift operation and setup on uneven ground', 'Overhead power line clearance', 'Working on wet or icy surfaces', 'Fall protection when work requires it']::text[], 'Ladder and Roofline Safety for Gutter Crews', 'Set up ladders and lifts safely, manage roofline work near power lines and protect crews on wet surfaces.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:fencing-getting-started')::uuid, 'fencing-getting-started', 'fencing', 'getting_started', 'Starting a Fence Company: Licensing, Insurance and Permits', 'Business basics for a fence company, including licensing, liability insurance and when fence permits apply.', 'Fence work depends on property lines, utility locations, and local setback rules, and mistakes can lead to disputes with neighbors. This course covers business setup, licensing or registration for fence work, liability coverage, and when permits and property survey information are needed. Licensing and permit rules vary by state and locality; confirm them with your licensing board and building department.', 'beginner', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'slate', false, 10, array['Entity setup and tax registration basics', 'Licensing or registration for fence work', 'Liability coverage for installs', 'Permits, setbacks and property line rules', 'Choosing residential, agricultural or commercial work']::text[], 'Starting a Fence Company: Licensing, Insurance and Permits', 'Business basics for a fence company, including licensing, liability insurance and when fence permits apply.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:fencing-sales')::uuid, 'fencing-sales', 'fencing', 'sales', 'Explaining Fence Pricing by Post, Panel, Gate and Concrete', 'Show what makes up the fence price, so customers see why style, height and gate count change the bid.', 'Customers compare fences by linear foot and often miss the cost of gates, concrete, rot-resistant posts, and removal of an old fence. This course covers presenting fence options with the parts shown separately, explaining style and height tradeoffs, and walking the customer through the property line and utility marks. Product warranties vary by manufacturer; state terms in writing.', 'intermediate', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'cyan', false, 20, array['Presenting posts, panels and gates separately', 'Style and height tradeoffs for customers', 'Explaining concrete and post setting', 'Property line and HOA questions', 'Writing proposals that show every part']::text[], 'Explaining Fence Pricing by Post, Panel, Gate and Concrete', 'Show what makes up the fence price, so customers see why style, height and gate count change the bid.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:fencing-estimating')::uuid, 'fencing-estimating', 'fencing', 'estimating', 'Fence Estimates: Linear Feet, Posts, Panels, Gates and Concrete', 'Count posts, panels or pickets, gates, concrete bags and removal by the linear foot and by each gate.', 'Fence estimates start with linear footage and post spacing, then add panels or pickets, rails, gates, and concrete. Slopes, rocky soil, and removal of an old fence change labor more than material. This course covers takeoffs by run, post and panel counts, gate pricing, and allowances for soil and grade conditions.', 'intermediate', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'navy', false, 30, array['Linear footage and post spacing', 'Panel, picket and rail counts', 'Gate pricing by type and width', 'Concrete quantities and soil allowances', 'Removal and disposal of old fence']::text[], null, 'Count posts, panels or pickets, gates, concrete bags and removal by the linear foot and by each gate.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:fencing-project-management')::uuid, 'fencing-project-management', 'fencing', 'project_management', 'Sequencing Fence Installs with Locates, Concrete and Gate Hardware', 'Plan utility locates, post setting, concrete cure and gate hardware so the crew can finish a run in one visit.', 'Fence installs begin with utility locates and layout, then post setting, concrete cure, and gate hardware. A missed locate or a post set before the concrete cures can delay the whole run. This course covers scheduling locates, sequencing posts and panels, and planning gate hardware and final adjustments around cure time.', 'intermediate', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'green', false, 40, array['Utility locate requests before digging', 'Layout from survey and property markers', 'Post setting and concrete cure sequence', 'Panel and rail installation order', 'Gate hardware and final adjustment']::text[], null, 'Plan utility locates, post setting, concrete cure and gate hardware so the crew can finish a run in one visit.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:fencing-accounting')::uuid, 'fencing-accounting', 'fencing', 'accounting', 'Fence Job Costing: Material, Concrete, Labor and Removal', 'Track posts, panels, concrete, gate hardware and crew hours by job so each fence bid can be compared to actuals.', 'Fence margins shift with soil conditions, concrete use, and removal work that was not in the bid. This course covers tracking material by run and job, recording concrete use against the estimate, and billing removal and rock or root obstructions as change orders. Tax treatment of materials and subcontracts varies by state; confirm details with your accountant.', 'intermediate', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'amber', false, 50, array['Tracking material by run and job', 'Concrete use against the estimate', 'Recording rock and root obstructions', 'Billing removal and change orders', 'Deposits and progress billing for fence jobs']::text[], 'Fence Job Costing: Material, Concrete, Labor and Removal', 'Track posts, panels, concrete, gate hardware and crew hours by job so each fence bid can be compared to actuals.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:fencing-hr')::uuid, 'fencing-hr', 'fencing', 'hr', 'Hiring Fence Installers and Training Them on Layout', 'Build installers who can lay out straight runs, set posts plumb and hang gates that close square.', 'Fence quality shows in straight runs, plumb posts, and gates that close smoothly, and those skills improve with practice. This course covers hiring installers and helpers, training on layout and post setting, and quality checks for gate operation before a crew leaves. Wage and classification rules vary by state; confirm them with your accountant.', 'beginner', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'rose', false, 60, array['Hiring installers and helpers', 'Layout and string lines for straight runs', 'Setting posts plumb and in alignment', 'Hanging gates that close square', 'Keeping crews busy between seasons']::text[], 'Hiring Fence Installers and Training Them on Layout', 'Build installers who can lay out straight runs, set posts plumb and hang gates that close square.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:fencing-growth')::uuid, 'fencing-growth', 'fencing', 'growth', 'Repeat Fence Work: Repairs, Replacements and Pool Fence Inspections', 'Build repeat work from repairs, gate service, pool fence inspections and property managers with fence portfolios.', 'Fences need repairs, gate adjustments, and eventual replacement, and pool fences are inspected on a schedule set by local rules. This course covers repair and gate service packages, pool fence inspection offers, and relationships with property managers and builders. Pool fence and solicitation rules vary by locality; confirm requirements before offering inspections.', 'intermediate', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'cyan', false, 70, array['Repair and gate service packages', 'Pool fence inspection and compliance offers', 'Property manager and builder relationships', 'Follow-up after a new fence install', 'Referrals from neighbors and HOAs']::text[], null, 'Build repeat work from repairs, gate service, pool fence inspections and property managers with fence portfolios.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:fencing-safety')::uuid, 'fencing-safety', 'fencing', 'safety', 'Fence Safety: Utility Lines, Post Hole Digging and Heavy Panels', 'Clear utility lines before digging, manage post-hole hazards and handle heavy panels and rolls safely.', 'Fence work involves digging near buried utilities, overhead power lines, and heavy panels and rolls of wire. This course covers utility locates and clearances before any digging, safe post-hole digging with augers, and lifting and handling heavy materials. Utility locate and clearance rules vary by state and locality; confirm the requirements that apply to your jobs.', 'advanced', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'slate', false, 80, array['Utility locates and clearance before digging', 'Overhead power line clearance for fence crews', 'Auger safety and post-hole hazards', 'Lifting heavy panels and rolls', 'Tool and vehicle safety on residential lots']::text[], null, 'Clear utility lines before digging, manage post-hole hazards and handle heavy panels and rolls safely.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:landscaping-getting-started')::uuid, 'landscaping-getting-started', 'landscaping', 'getting_started', 'Starting a Landscaping Business: Licensing, Insurance and Seasons', 'Business basics for a landscaping company, including licensing, insurance and planning around seasonal cash flow.', 'Landscaping work is seasonal in most regions and involves mowers, trucks, and chemicals that create liability. This course covers business setup, licensing or registration for landscape and pesticide work, liability and equipment coverage, and planning for slower seasons. Licensing, pesticide application, and irrigation rules vary by state and locality; confirm them with your licensing board.', 'beginner', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'slate', false, 10, array['Entity setup and tax registration basics', 'Licensing for landscape and pesticide work', 'Liability and equipment coverage', 'Planning for seasonal cash flow', 'Choosing residential, commercial or both']::text[], null, 'Business basics for a landscaping company, including licensing, insurance and planning around seasonal cash flow.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:landscaping-sales')::uuid, 'landscaping-sales', 'landscaping', 'sales', 'Selling Landscape Installs with Soil, Grading and Planting Shown', 'Present soil prep, grading and planting as proposal sections so customers see the work behind the plants.', 'Homeowners often compare installs to plant lists from a garden center and miss the soil amendments, grading, and planting labor. This course covers site visits that check drainage and sun, presenting planting plans with sections, and explaining why soil prep and grading matter for long-term results. Plant and product warranties vary by supplier; state terms in writing.', 'intermediate', 'public', 'published', 'mixed', 'cyan', false, 20, array['Site visits for drainage and sun exposure', 'Presenting planting plans in sections', 'Soil prep and grading explained', 'Handling the ''garden center price'' comparison', 'Writing proposals with plant and warranty terms']::text[], null, 'Present soil prep, grading and planting as proposal sections so customers see the work behind the plants.', now()),
  (md5('academy:course:landscaping-estimating')::uuid, 'landscaping-estimating', 'landscaping', 'estimating', 'Landscape Estimates: Plants, Soil, Mulch, Edging, Sod and Labor', 'Price plants, soil, mulch, edging and sod by area and quantity, with planting and grading labor as separate sections.', 'Landscape estimates combine plant counts, bed square footage, soil and mulch volumes, edging footage, and sod area, with labor for prep and planting. Grading, irrigation changes, and disposal of old material can outweigh the plants. This course covers takeoffs by bed and zone, mulch and soil volume calculations, and pricing for sod and edging.', 'intermediate', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'navy', false, 30, array['Bed square footage and plant counts', 'Soil and mulch volume calculations', 'Edging footage and material choices', 'Sod area and delivery pricing', 'Grading and disposal allowances']::text[], null, 'Price plants, soil, mulch, edging and sod by area and quantity, with planting and grading labor as separate sections.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:landscaping-project-management')::uuid, 'landscaping-project-management', 'landscaping', 'project_management', 'Scheduling Landscape Installs Around Planting Windows and Sod', 'Sequence grading, planting, sod and irrigation around planting seasons and watering needs after install.', 'Landscape installs depend on planting windows, sod delivery timing, and watering schedules after the crew leaves. This course covers sequencing grading, irrigation, planting, and sod, scheduling deliveries, and planning the first weeks of watering with the homeowner. Irrigation and water-use rules vary by locality; confirm them before installing systems.', 'intermediate', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'green', false, 40, array['Grading and soil prep before planting', 'Planting windows by season and region', 'Sod delivery and installation timing', 'First-month watering plan for homeowners', 'Coordinating irrigation and hardscape subs']::text[], null, 'Sequence grading, planting, sod and irrigation around planting seasons and watering needs after install.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:landscaping-accounting')::uuid, 'landscaping-accounting', 'landscaping', 'accounting', 'Landscape Job Costing: Plant Losses, Material Overages and Crew Hours', 'Track plants, soil, mulch and crew hours per job so you can see where installs ran over the estimate.', 'Landscape margins shift with plant losses, mulch and soil overages, and crew hours that run long on heavy grading. This course covers tracking material by bed and job, recording plant replacements under warranty, and billing grading and disposal changes. Tax treatment of plant and material purchases varies by state; confirm details with your accountant.', 'intermediate', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'amber', false, 50, array['Tracking material by bed and job', 'Recording plant losses and replacements', 'Crew hours for grading and heavy work', 'Billing grading and disposal changes', 'Deposits and progress billing for installs']::text[], null, 'Track plants, soil, mulch and crew hours per job so you can see where installs ran over the estimate.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:landscaping-hr')::uuid, 'landscaping-hr', 'landscaping', 'hr', 'Hiring Landscape Crews for Planting, Mowing and Maintenance', 'Hire and train crew members for install and maintenance, with clear roles for mowing, planting and equipment care.', 'Landscape crews work outdoors in heat and cold and need a mix of planting, mowing, and equipment skills. This course covers hiring for seasonal and year-round roles, defining crew roles for install and maintenance, and training on plant care and equipment upkeep. Wage, classification, and seasonal employment rules vary by state; confirm them with your accountant.', 'beginner', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'rose', false, 60, array['Hiring for seasonal and year-round roles', 'Roles for planting, mowing and irrigation', 'Training on plant care and identification', 'Equipment upkeep and daily checks', 'Keeping crew through the off season']::text[], 'Hiring Landscape Crews for Planting, Mowing and Maintenance', 'Hire and train crew members for install and maintenance, with clear roles for mowing, planting and equipment care.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:landscaping-growth')::uuid, 'landscaping-growth', 'landscaping', 'growth', 'Building Recurring Lawn-Care and Maintenance Revenue', 'Convert install customers into weekly mowing, seasonal cleanups and recurring bed care under a maintenance agreement.', 'Landscape installs can turn into recurring maintenance, which steadies revenue through the year. This course covers designing maintenance packages by visit frequency, offering seasonal cleanups and bed care, and presenting a maintenance agreement at the end of the install. Contract, pesticide, and advertising rules vary by locality; confirm terms before offering recurring service.', 'intermediate', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'cyan', false, 70, array['Designing maintenance packages by frequency', 'Seasonal cleanups and bed care', 'Presenting maintenance at the install handoff', 'Renewal and referral programs', 'Tracking recurring accounts and route density']::text[], 'Building Recurring Lawn-Care and Maintenance Revenue', 'Convert install customers into weekly mowing, seasonal cleanups and recurring bed care under a maintenance agreement.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:landscaping-safety')::uuid, 'landscaping-safety', 'landscaping', 'safety', 'Landscape Equipment and Chemical Safety for Crews', 'Use mowers, trimmers and blowers safely, handle chemicals with the right training and protect crews in heat.', 'Landscape crews use mowers, trimmers, blowers, and chemicals, and heat and fatigue increase the risk of injury. This course covers safe use of powered equipment and guards, handling and storing chemicals per label and local rules, and heat illness prevention. Pesticide application and worker protection rules vary by state and locality; confirm the requirements that apply to your work.', 'advanced', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'slate', false, 80, array['Mower and trimmer safety and guards', 'Blower and debris hazards near people', 'Chemical storage and label compliance', 'Heat illness prevention and breaks', 'Lifting bags of soil and mulch safely']::text[], 'Landscape Equipment and Chemical Safety for Crews', 'Use mowers, trimmers and blowers safely, handle chemicals with the right training and protect crews in heat.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:pressure-washing-getting-started')::uuid, 'pressure-washing-getting-started', 'pressure-washing', 'getting_started', 'Starting a Pressure Washing Business: Insurance and Water Rules', 'Business basics for a pressure washing company, including liability insurance, equipment choices and water-use rules.', 'Pressure washing creates spray, runoff, and property damage risk, and some areas restrict runoff and water use. This course covers business setup, liability insurance for property damage, equipment choices for your work, and local rules on runoff and water. Licensing, runoff, and chemical rules vary by state and locality; confirm them with your licensing board and environmental agency.', 'beginner', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'slate', false, 10, array['Entity setup and tax registration basics', 'Liability insurance for property damage', 'Choosing equipment for your typical jobs', 'Local runoff and water-use rules', 'Setting service area and minimum job size']::text[], null, 'Business basics for a pressure washing company, including liability insurance, equipment choices and water-use rules.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:pressure-washing-sales')::uuid, 'pressure-washing-sales', 'pressure-washing', 'sales', 'Quoting Driveways, Patios and Decks Without Surprises', 'Note the surface, its condition and the access before quoting, so the customer knows what the price covers.', 'Customers often expect a low flat price for a whole house and are surprised by the cost of stains, worn wood, and access limits. This course covers site walks that note surface type and condition, presenting pricing by square foot, flat rate, or custom line items, and explaining what stain removal and sealing are not included. Chemical and warranty terms vary; state them in writing.', 'intermediate', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'cyan', false, 20, array['Site walks that note surface and condition', 'Pricing by square foot versus flat rate', 'Custom line items for stains and sealing', 'Explaining what the base price excludes', 'Writing proposals with a minimum job charge']::text[], 'Quoting Driveways, Patios and Decks Without Surprises', 'Note the surface, its condition and the access before quoting, so the customer knows what the price covers.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:pressure-washing-estimating')::uuid, 'pressure-washing-estimating', 'pressure-washing', 'estimating', 'Pressure Washing Estimates: Square Feet, Surface Type and Minimums', 'Measure each surface, adjust for condition and access, and apply a minimum job charge that covers setup time.', 'Pressure washing estimates start with the square footage of each surface, then adjust for surface type, staining, and access. Small jobs can lose money without a minimum charge that covers setup and travel. This course covers measuring driveways, walks, patios, and fences, adjusting price for condition, and setting minimums and add-on line items.', 'intermediate', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'navy', false, 30, array['Measuring driveways, walks and patios', 'Adjusting for surface type and condition', 'Fence and deck measurement by linear and square feet', 'Minimum job charges and setup time', 'Add-on items for stains and rust']::text[], null, 'Measure each surface, adjust for condition and access, and apply a minimum job charge that covers setup time.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:pressure-washing-project-management')::uuid, 'pressure-washing-project-management', 'pressure-washing', 'project_management', 'Routing Pressure Washing Jobs Across the Week', 'Group jobs by neighborhood, plan water supply and schedule around weather and dry-time for the surfaces you clean.', 'Pressure washing jobs depend on dry weather, water supply, and surfaces that need time to dry before sealing or staining. This course covers routing jobs by neighborhood to reduce travel time, planning water access on each site, and scheduling seal or stain follow-up after cleaning. Local water-use and runoff rules vary; confirm them before routing jobs.', 'intermediate', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'green', false, 40, array['Routing jobs by neighborhood', 'Water access and supply planning', 'Weather and dry-time scheduling', 'Sealing and staining follow-up visits', 'Protecting plants and property during jobs']::text[], 'Routing Pressure Washing Jobs Across the Week', 'Group jobs by neighborhood, plan water supply and schedule around weather and dry-time for the surfaces you clean.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:pressure-washing-accounting')::uuid, 'pressure-washing-accounting', 'pressure-washing', 'accounting', 'Pressure Washing Job Costing: Chemicals, Fuel, Travel and Time', 'Track chemical use, fuel, travel and crew time per job so you can see which services earn their time.', 'Pressure washing margins depend on travel time, chemical use, fuel, and the time spent on jobs that run longer than quoted. This course covers tracking job time and travel by route, recording chemical and fuel costs, and billing add-ons such as stain removal. Tax treatment of equipment and supplies varies by state; confirm details with your accountant.', 'intermediate', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'amber', false, 50, array['Tracking time and travel by route', 'Recording chemical and fuel costs', 'Equipment depreciation basics', 'Billing add-ons such as stain removal', 'Deposits and payment terms for recurring jobs']::text[], null, 'Track chemical use, fuel, travel and crew time per job so you can see which services earn their time.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:pressure-washing-hr')::uuid, 'pressure-washing-hr', 'pressure-washing', 'hr', 'Hiring and Training Pressure Washing Technicians', 'Build technicians who measure accurately, use wands and chemicals safely and protect customer property.', 'Pressure washing quality depends on wand technique, chemical mixing, and protecting plants and property during the job. This course covers hiring technicians, training on wand technique and surface care, and setting standards for measuring and documenting each job. Wage and classification rules vary by state; confirm them with your accountant.', 'beginner', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'rose', false, 60, array['Hiring technicians for exterior cleaning', 'Wand technique by surface type', 'Mixing and handling cleaning chemicals', 'Protecting plants and property', 'Documenting jobs with before and after photos']::text[], 'Hiring and Training Pressure Washing Technicians', 'Build technicians who measure accurately, use wands and chemicals safely and protect customer property.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:pressure-washing-growth')::uuid, 'pressure-washing-growth', 'pressure-washing', 'growth', 'Recurring Cleaning Plans and Repeat Pressure Washing Work', 'Turn one-time cleanings into scheduled plans for driveways, fences and commercial walkways.', 'Pressure washing customers often need the same surfaces cleaned on a schedule, which makes recurring plans a steady revenue source. This course covers building annual cleaning plans, reminders for seasonal cleaning, and offering commercial walkway and storefront work to property managers. Marketing and solicitation rules vary by locality.', 'intermediate', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'cyan', false, 70, array['Annual cleaning plans for homes', 'Seasonal reminders and scheduling', 'Commercial walkway and storefront accounts', 'Referrals from real estate and property contacts', 'Tracking recurring accounts by route']::text[], 'Recurring Cleaning Plans and Repeat Pressure Washing Work', 'Turn one-time cleanings into scheduled plans for driveways, fences and commercial walkways.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:pressure-washing-safety')::uuid, 'pressure-washing-safety', 'pressure-washing', 'safety', 'Pressure Washing Safety: Spray Injuries, Ladders and Electrical', 'Prevent high-pressure injuries, manage ladder and roof-edge work and keep water away from electrical equipment.', 'High-pressure spray can cause serious injury, and crews work on ladders and near electrical outlets during cleaning. This course covers safe wand handling and nozzle choice, ladder and height safety for multi-story work, and keeping water and cords away from electrical equipment. Equipment, chemical, and worksite safety rules vary by state and locality; confirm the requirements that apply to your work.', 'advanced', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'slate', false, 80, array['High-pressure injury prevention', 'Nozzle choice and wand handling', 'Ladder and height safety on two-story jobs', 'Keeping water away from electrical outlets', 'Chemical handling and PPE basics']::text[], null, 'Prevent high-pressure injuries, manage ladder and roof-edge work and keep water away from electrical equipment.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:soft-washing-getting-started')::uuid, 'soft-washing-getting-started', 'soft-washing', 'getting_started', 'Soft Washing Business Setup: Licensing, Insurance and Chemicals', 'Business basics for a soft washing company, including licensing, liability insurance and chemical application rules.', 'Soft washing uses cleaning solutions on roofs, walls and landscaping, so chemical handling, runoff and liability rules apply. This course covers business setup, licensing for chemical application where required, liability insurance for property and plant damage, and local runoff rules. Licensing and chemical rules vary by state and locality; confirm them with your licensing board and environmental agency.', 'beginner', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'slate', false, 10, array['Entity setup and tax registration basics', 'Licensing for chemical application', 'Liability insurance for property and plant damage', 'Runoff and environmental rules by locality', 'Setting a service area and minimum job']::text[], null, 'Business basics for a soft washing company, including licensing, liability insurance and chemical application rules.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:soft-washing-sales')::uuid, 'soft-washing-sales', 'soft-washing', 'sales', 'Explaining Whole-House and Roof Soft Washing Quotes', 'Explain how wall and roof areas are measured and what the price covers, so the customer understands the quote.', 'Customers often expect a flat price for a whole house and are unclear on why roof and wall areas must be measured. This course covers explaining the measurement method, presenting roof and wall areas as separate line items, and noting areas that need a separate quote, such as steep or fragile surfaces. Chemical and warranty terms vary; state them in writing.', 'intermediate', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'cyan', false, 20, array['Explaining wall and roof area measurement', 'Presenting roof and wall areas as line items', 'Noting areas that need separate quotes', 'Handling the ''curb-side price'' question', 'Writing proposals that state method and scope']::text[], 'Explaining Whole-House and Roof Soft Washing Quotes', 'Explain how wall and roof areas are measured and what the price covers, so the customer understands the quote.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:soft-washing-estimating')::uuid, 'soft-washing-estimating', 'soft-washing', 'estimating', 'Soft Washing Estimates: Wall Area, Gables, Openings and Roof Planes', 'Measure wall perimeter and height, add gables, subtract large openings and price roof area plane by plane.', 'Soft washing estimates start with wall area from the building perimeter and height, then add gables and subtract large openings. Roof area is estimated plane by plane, and pitch and complexity change the price. This course covers building an area takeoff, adjusting for gables and openings, and pricing roof planes and trim separately from the walls.', 'intermediate', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'navy', false, 30, array['Wall area from perimeter and height', 'Adding gables and subtracting large openings', 'Roof area plane by plane', 'Pricing for pitch and roof complexity', 'Separating estimate from method decisions']::text[], null, 'Measure wall perimeter and height, add gables, subtract large openings and price roof area plane by plane.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:soft-washing-project-management')::uuid, 'soft-washing-project-management', 'soft-washing', 'project_management', 'Scheduling Soft Washing Around Weather, Dry Time and Plant Protection', 'Plan exterior cleaning days around wind, rain and plant protection needs so jobs finish on schedule.', 'Soft washing depends on calm weather, dry time for surfaces, and protection for plants and nearby property. This course covers scheduling around wind and rain, planning plant pre-wetting and protection, and setting dry-time expectations with the customer. Local rules on chemical application timing vary; confirm them before scheduling.', 'intermediate', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'green', false, 40, array['Weather windows and wind limits', 'Plant pre-wetting and protection plans', 'Routing jobs to limit travel', 'Dry-time expectations for customers', 'Follow-up visits for stubborn stains']::text[], null, 'Plan exterior cleaning days around wind, rain and plant protection needs so jobs finish on schedule.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:soft-washing-accounting')::uuid, 'soft-washing-accounting', 'soft-washing', 'accounting', 'Soft Washing Job Costing: Chemicals, Equipment and Time by Area', 'Track chemical use, equipment and labor time per job so the price per area reflects actual cost.', 'Soft washing margins depend on chemical use, equipment wear, and labor time that varies with building height and access. This course covers tracking chemical use by job, recording time by area and story, and reviewing whether your area pricing covers actual costs. Tax treatment of equipment and chemicals varies by state; confirm details with your accountant.', 'intermediate', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'amber', false, 50, array['Tracking chemical use by job', 'Recording labor time by story and area', 'Equipment wear and maintenance costs', 'Reviewing price per area against actuals', 'Deposits and payment terms for recurring work']::text[], null, 'Track chemical use, equipment and labor time per job so the price per area reflects actual cost.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:soft-washing-hr')::uuid, 'soft-washing-hr', 'soft-washing', 'hr', 'Training Soft Washing Technicians for Method and Documentation', 'Train technicians to follow the mix, method and documentation standards your business has set for each surface.', 'Soft washing quality depends on consistent mixing, correct method for each surface, and documentation of what was applied. This course covers hiring technicians, training on mixing and application by surface type, and keeping job records that show method and chemical use. Wage, classification, and chemical training rules vary by state; confirm them with your accountant and licensing board.', 'beginner', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'rose', false, 60, array['Hiring technicians for exterior cleaning', 'Mixing standards and label compliance', 'Application method by surface type', 'Job records for method and chemicals', 'Keeping technicians through the season']::text[], null, 'Train technicians to follow the mix, method and documentation standards your business has set for each surface.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:soft-washing-growth')::uuid, 'soft-washing-growth', 'soft-washing', 'growth', 'Recurring Exterior Cleaning Plans for Homes and Property Managers', 'Build annual soft washing plans for homes, HOAs and property managers who want roofs and walls cleaned on a schedule.', 'Exterior cleaning needs return on a schedule, which makes annual soft washing plans a steady source of recurring work. This course covers designing annual plans by building type, reminder schedules, and property manager and HOA relationships. Solicitation, advertising, and chemical claim rules vary by locality; confirm requirements before offering plans.', 'intermediate', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'cyan', false, 70, array['Annual plans by building type', 'Reminder schedules for exterior cleaning', 'HOA and property manager relationships', 'Referrals from roofers and window companies', 'Tracking recurring accounts by route']::text[], null, 'Build annual soft washing plans for homes, HOAs and property managers who want roofs and walls cleaned on a schedule.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:soft-washing-safety')::uuid, 'soft-washing-safety', 'soft-washing', 'safety', 'Soft Washing Safety: Chemical Handling, Roof Access and Runoff Control', 'Handle cleaning chemicals with PPE, manage ladder and roof access safely and control runoff near plants and water.', 'Soft washing uses chemicals applied at height on ladders and roofs, and runoff can reach plants, pets, and waterways. This course covers chemical handling and PPE, ladder and roof access safety, and runoff control and plant protection. Chemical application, worker protection, and runoff rules vary by state and locality; confirm the requirements that apply to your work.', 'advanced', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'slate', false, 80, array['Chemical handling and PPE', 'Ladder and roof access safety', 'Runoff control near plants and water', 'Keeping pets and people clear during application', 'Spill response and storage basics']::text[], null, 'Handle cleaning chemicals with PPE, manage ladder and roof access safely and control runoff near plants and water.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:cleaning-getting-started')::uuid, 'cleaning-getting-started', 'cleaning', 'getting_started', 'Cleaning Business Setup: Licensing, Bonding and Insurance', 'Business basics for a residential, commercial or post-construction cleaning company.', 'Starting a cleaning company means choosing your market, registering the business, and carrying the right insurance and bonding for working inside customers'' homes and buildings. This course covers entity setup, general liability and janitorial bonds, workers'' compensation basics and setting a service area. Requirements vary by state and city; confirm them with your licensing office and insurance agent.', 'beginner', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'slate', false, 10, array['Choosing residential, commercial or post-construction work', 'Entity setup and tax registration basics', 'Liability insurance and janitorial bonds', 'Workers'' compensation basics', 'Setting a service area and minimum job']::text[], 'Cleaning Business Setup: Licensing, Bonding and Insurance', 'Business basics for a residential, commercial or post-construction cleaning company.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:cleaning-sales')::uuid, 'cleaning-sales', 'cleaning', 'sales', 'Selling Cleaning Services Beyond the Lowest Price', 'Show customers exactly what is included so they compare value, not just price.', 'Cleaning quotes are easy to compare on price alone. This course covers walking the space with the customer, presenting the scope room by room, offering add-ons as separate choices, and explaining how a first deep clean differs from recurring visits.', 'intermediate', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'cyan', false, 20, array['Walking the space and confirming expectations', 'Presenting scope room by room', 'Offering add-ons as separate choices', 'Explaining first deep clean versus recurring', 'Following up on quotes that went quiet']::text[], 'Selling Cleaning Services Beyond the Lowest Price', 'Show customers exactly what is included so they compare value, not just price.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:cleaning-estimating')::uuid, 'cleaning-estimating', 'cleaning', 'estimating', 'Cleaning Estimates by Square Foot, Room and Hour', 'Choose the right pricing method for each job and keep supplies, travel and add-ons visible.', 'Square-foot pricing suits post-construction and commercial space, per-room pricing suits homes, and hourly suits small or unpredictable jobs. This course covers measuring space, estimating crew hours from production rates you track, pricing post-construction phases, and adding supplies, travel and a minimum charge.', 'intermediate', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'navy', false, 30, array['Measuring cleanable area', 'Tracking your own production rates', 'Pricing rough, final and touch-up cleans', 'Pricing add-ons and supplies', 'Setting a minimum service charge']::text[], 'Cleaning Estimates by Square Foot, Room and Hour', 'Choose the right pricing method for each job and keep supplies, travel and add-ons visible.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:cleaning-project-management')::uuid, 'cleaning-project-management', 'cleaning', 'project_management', 'Scheduling Cleaning Crews and Post-Construction Phases', 'Plan crews and visits so cleans land on time, including around other trades on construction sites.', 'Post-construction cleaning happens in phases that depend on other trades finishing, while recurring service depends on dependable routes. This course covers coordinating with the general contractor, scheduling rough, final and touch-up cleans, building recurring routes and using checklists for consistent quality.', 'intermediate', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'green', false, 40, array['Coordinating with the general contractor', 'Scheduling rough, final and touch-up cleans', 'Building efficient recurring routes', 'Quality checklists and walkthroughs', 'Handling reschedules and access issues']::text[], 'Scheduling Cleaning Crews and Post-Construction Phases', 'Plan crews and visits so cleans land on time, including around other trades on construction sites.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:cleaning-accounting')::uuid, 'cleaning-accounting', 'cleaning', 'accounting', 'Cleaning Business Financials: Job Costing and Recurring Billing', 'Track labor, supplies and travel per job and bill recurring customers reliably.', 'Labor is the largest cost in cleaning, so margins depend on knowing real crew hours. This course covers costing each job, tracking supplies and travel, billing recurring customers on a schedule, and reading profit and loss by service type.', 'intermediate', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'amber', false, 50, array['Job costing crew hours', 'Tracking supplies and travel costs', 'Recurring billing and autopay', 'Profit by service type', 'Setting aside taxes and overhead']::text[], null, 'Track labor, supplies and travel per job and bill recurring customers reliably.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:cleaning-hr')::uuid, 'cleaning-hr', 'cleaning', 'hr', 'Hiring, Training and Keeping Cleaning Crews', 'Recruit dependable cleaners, train to a standard and reduce turnover.', 'Turnover is one of the biggest challenges in cleaning. This course covers recruiting, background checks where permitted, training to written checklists, scheduling fairly and recognizing good work. Employment and background check rules vary by state; follow the laws where you operate.', 'beginner', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'rose', false, 60, array['Recruiting dependable cleaners', 'Background checks where permitted', 'Training to written checklists', 'Fair scheduling and pay', 'Reducing turnover']::text[], 'Hiring, Training and Keeping Cleaning Crews', 'Recruit dependable cleaners, train to a standard and reduce turnover.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:cleaning-growth')::uuid, 'cleaning-growth', 'cleaning', 'growth', 'Building Recurring Cleaning Revenue', 'Turn one-time cleans into weekly, every-two-weeks and monthly service.', 'Recurring customers make cleaning revenue predictable. This course covers offering recurring plans after a first clean, pricing frequency fairly, partnering with builders and property managers for post-construction and turnover work, and asking for reviews and referrals.', 'intermediate', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'cyan', false, 70, array['Offering recurring plans after the first clean', 'Pricing by frequency', 'Builder and property manager partnerships', 'Reviews and referrals', 'Seasonal and move-season promotions']::text[], 'Building Recurring Cleaning Revenue', 'Turn one-time cleans into weekly, every-two-weeks and monthly service.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:cleaning-safety')::uuid, 'cleaning-safety', 'cleaning', 'safety', 'Cleaning Chemical Safety and Hazard Communication', 'Use cleaning chemicals safely, keep safety data sheets and protect crews and customers.', 'Cleaning crews handle chemicals daily. This course covers OSHA hazard communication, safety data sheets, never mixing incompatible products, protective equipment, and construction dust and silica awareness on post-construction jobs. Follow product labels and the rules where you work.', 'beginner', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'slate', false, 80, array['Hazard communication basics', 'Safety data sheets and labeling', 'Avoiding dangerous chemical mixes', 'Protective equipment', 'Construction dust and silica awareness']::text[], 'Cleaning Chemical Safety and Hazard Communication', 'Use cleaning chemicals safely, keep safety data sheets and protect crews and customers.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:excavation-getting-started')::uuid, 'excavation-getting-started', 'excavation', 'getting_started', 'Starting an Excavation Business: Licensing, Insurance and Equipment', 'Business basics for an excavation company, including licensing, equipment insurance and utility locate responsibilities.', 'Excavation work involves heavy equipment, buried utilities, and public roads, which create serious liability. This course covers business setup, licensing and bonding for excavation work, liability and equipment coverage, and responsibilities for utility locates before digging. Licensing, bonding, and locate rules vary by state and locality; confirm them with your licensing board and the locate service in your area.', 'beginner', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'slate', false, 10, array['Entity setup and tax registration basics', 'Licensing and bonding for excavation work', 'Equipment and liability coverage', 'Utility locate responsibilities before digging', 'Choosing your service area and equipment mix']::text[], null, 'Business basics for an excavation company, including licensing, equipment insurance and utility locate responsibilities.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:excavation-sales')::uuid, 'excavation-sales', 'excavation', 'sales', 'Presenting Excavation Bids with Hauling and Fill Itemized', 'Itemize equipment time, trucking, fill and mobilization so customers see what the price covers.', 'Customers often compare excavation bids by hourly equipment rate and do not see the trucks, fill, and mobilization behind the number. This course covers presenting bids with hauling and fill as separate lines, explaining why unknown soil conditions change the price, and writing change-order terms for rock or unexpected utilities. Permit and disposal requirements vary by locality.', 'intermediate', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'cyan', false, 20, array['Itemizing equipment time and trucking', 'Explaining fill and import quantities', 'Mobilization and site access pricing', 'Writing change-order terms for rock and utilities', 'Handling the ''hourly rate'' comparison']::text[], 'Presenting Excavation Bids with Hauling and Fill Itemized', 'Itemize equipment time, trucking, fill and mobilization so customers see what the price covers.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:excavation-estimating')::uuid, 'excavation-estimating', 'excavation', 'estimating', 'Excavation Estimates: Equipment Hours, Hauling, Fill and Grading', 'Estimate dig and grade work by volume and equipment hours, then add hauling, fill, mobilization and disposal.', 'Excavation estimates depend on cut and fill volumes, equipment hours, and the number of truck loads to haul material. Mobilization, access, and disposal fees are the costs most often left out. This course covers volume takeoffs, truck and load counts, equipment-hour estimating, and pricing for mobilization and fill imports.', 'intermediate', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'navy', false, 30, array['Cut and fill volume takeoffs', 'Truck counts and load calculations', 'Equipment hours for dig and grade', 'Mobilization and site access pricing', 'Disposal and fill import pricing']::text[], null, 'Estimate dig and grade work by volume and equipment hours, then add hauling, fill, mobilization and disposal.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:excavation-project-management')::uuid, 'excavation-project-management', 'excavation', 'project_management', 'Sequencing Excavation with Utility Locates, Inspections and Trucks', 'Plan locates, dig sequence, inspections and truck flow so the site moves without rework or waiting.', 'Excavation starts with utility locates and ends with grading and compaction, and the sequence determines whether trucks wait on the site. This course covers scheduling locates, planning dig and haul sequence, coordinating inspections for footings and drains, and managing truck flow on tight sites. Locate, inspection, and compaction rules vary by locality; confirm them before scheduling.', 'intermediate', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'green', false, 40, array['Utility locate timing before digging', 'Dig and haul sequence on tight sites', 'Inspections for footings and drains', 'Truck flow and staging', 'Compaction and final grade checks']::text[], null, 'Plan locates, dig sequence, inspections and truck flow so the site moves without rework or waiting.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:excavation-accounting')::uuid, 'excavation-accounting', 'excavation', 'accounting', 'Excavation Job Costing: Equipment Hours, Trucking and Fill', 'Track equipment hours, truck loads and fill by job so you can see where trucking and fill ate the margin.', 'Excavation margins depend on equipment hours, truck loads, and fill that costs more than estimated. This course covers tracking equipment hours by machine and job, recording loads and fill imports, and billing change orders for unexpected conditions. Equipment depreciation and fuel tax treatment vary by state; confirm details with your accountant.', 'intermediate', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'amber', false, 50, array['Tracking equipment hours by machine', 'Recording truck loads and fill imports', 'Fuel costs and fuel surcharges', 'Billing change orders for rock and water', 'Deposits and progress billing for excavation']::text[], 'Excavation Job Costing: Equipment Hours, Trucking and Fill', 'Track equipment hours, truck loads and fill by job so you can see where trucking and fill ate the margin.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:excavation-hr')::uuid, 'excavation-hr', 'excavation', 'hr', 'Hiring Equipment Operators and Laborers for Excavation Crews', 'Recruit operators and laborers, define roles for dig, haul and grade, and train them on signals and site awareness.', 'Excavation crews depend on skilled operators and laborers who can communicate with each other around heavy equipment. This course covers hiring operators and laborers, defining roles for dig, haul, and grade work, and training on hand signals and site awareness. Operator certification and wage rules vary by state; confirm them with your licensing board and accountant.', 'beginner', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'rose', false, 60, array['Hiring equipment operators and laborers', 'Roles for dig, haul and grade', 'Hand signals and communication on site', 'Operator certification and training paths', 'Keeping operators through the slow season']::text[], 'Hiring Equipment Operators and Laborers for Excavation Crews', 'Recruit operators and laborers, define roles for dig, haul and grade, and train them on signals and site awareness.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:excavation-growth')::uuid, 'excavation-growth', 'excavation', 'growth', 'Repeat Excavation Work from Builders, Developers and Municipalities', 'Build repeat work from builders, developers and public agencies that need dependable dig and grade crews.', 'Excavation work repeats with builders who start multiple lots, developers who need site prep, and public agencies for road and drainage projects. This course covers building a record with builders and developers, bidding public work where you qualify, and offering drainage and grading services as repeat work. Public bidding and qualification rules vary by agency and locality.', 'intermediate', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'cyan', false, 70, array['Building a record with builders', 'Site prep work for developers', 'Qualifying for public and municipal bids', 'Drainage and grading as repeat service', 'Tracking repeat clients by project type']::text[], null, 'Build repeat work from builders, developers and public agencies that need dependable dig and grade crews.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:excavation-safety')::uuid, 'excavation-safety', 'excavation', 'safety', 'Trench, Excavation and Underground Utility Safety', 'Protect workers in trenches, avoid buried utilities and manage equipment and spotter safety on every dig.', 'Excavation exposes workers to trench collapse, buried utilities, and equipment movement around people. This course covers trench protection and access, utility locates and hand digging near lines, and spotter and equipment safety on busy sites. Trenching, excavation, and utility-strike rules vary by state and locality; confirm the requirements that apply to your jobs.', 'advanced', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'slate', false, 80, array['Trench protection and safe access', 'Locating and hand digging near utilities', 'Spotter and equipment movement safety', 'Water and gas line emergency response', 'Inspecting spoil piles and edges daily']::text[], 'Trench, Excavation and Underground Utility Safety', 'Protect workers in trenches, avoid buried utilities and manage equipment and spotter safety on every dig.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:foundations-getting-started')::uuid, 'foundations-getting-started', 'foundations', 'getting_started', 'Starting a Foundation Business: Licensing, Insurance and Engineering', 'Business basics for a foundation company, including licensing, insurance and how you work with engineers on structural repairs.', 'Foundation work is structural, so licensing, insurance, and engineering involvement are central from the start. This course covers business setup, licensing or registration for foundation work, liability and equipment coverage, and working with engineers on structural repair plans. Requirements vary by state and locality; confirm them with your licensing board and the engineers you work with.', 'beginner', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'slate', false, 10, array['Entity setup and tax registration basics', 'Licensing or registration for foundation work', 'Liability and equipment coverage', 'Working with engineers on structural repairs', 'Choosing new construction, repair or both']::text[], null, 'Business basics for a foundation company, including licensing, insurance and how you work with engineers on structural repairs.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:foundations-sales')::uuid, 'foundations-sales', 'foundations', 'sales', 'Explaining Foundation Repair Options and Causes to Homeowners', 'Explain the cause of a crack or leak, the repair options and what each one leaves unresolved.', 'Homeowners often want the cheapest patch for a crack or leak, and the cause may need a larger repair. This course covers site inspections and photos, explaining drainage and soil causes in plain terms, and presenting repair options with what each one addresses. Engineering reports and warranty terms vary; state them in writing and refer structural questions to the engineer.', 'intermediate', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'cyan', false, 20, array['Inspecting cracks, leaks and drainage', 'Explaining causes in plain terms', 'Presenting patch versus structural repair', 'Working with engineers and inspectors', 'Writing proposals that state what is excluded']::text[], null, 'Explain the cause of a crack or leak, the repair options and what each one leaves unresolved.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:foundations-estimating')::uuid, 'foundations-estimating', 'foundations', 'estimating', 'Foundation Estimates: Footings, Walls, Rebar and Drainage', 'Price footings, walls, reinforcement, waterproofing and drainage by phase with concrete volume shown clearly.', 'Foundation estimates are built by phase: excavation and footings, walls, reinforcement, waterproofing, and drainage. Concrete volume, rebar schedules, and access for pumps and equipment all change the price. This course covers footing and wall takeoffs, rebar quantities from the plan, and pricing for waterproofing membranes and drain systems.', 'intermediate', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'navy', false, 30, array['Footing and wall volume takeoffs', 'Rebar quantities from the plan', 'Waterproofing membrane and sealant pricing', 'Perimeter drain and sump pricing', 'Access and pump pricing for tight lots']::text[], 'Foundation Estimates: Footings, Walls, Rebar and Drainage', 'Price footings, walls, reinforcement, waterproofing and drainage by phase with concrete volume shown clearly.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:foundations-project-management')::uuid, 'foundations-project-management', 'foundations', 'project_management', 'Sequencing Footings, Walls, Inspections and Backfill', 'Plan footing inspections, wall pours, cure time, waterproofing and backfill so each phase passes before the next starts.', 'Foundation work moves through footings, inspections, walls, cure time, and backfill, and backfilling too early can crack walls. This course covers scheduling footing and rebar inspections before the pour, planning wall pours and cure time, and sequencing waterproofing and drainage before backfill. Inspection and backfill rules vary by locality; confirm them with the building department and engineer.', 'intermediate', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'green', false, 40, array['Footing and rebar inspections before the pour', 'Wall pour scheduling and cure time', 'Waterproofing and drainage before backfill', 'Backfill timing and compaction', 'Coordinating framers after foundation sign-off']::text[], 'Sequencing Footings, Walls, Inspections and Backfill', 'Plan footing inspections, wall pours, cure time, waterproofing and backfill so each phase passes before the next starts.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:foundations-accounting')::uuid, 'foundations-accounting', 'foundations', 'accounting', 'Foundation Job Costing: Concrete Volume, Rebar and Repair Overruns', 'Track concrete volume, rebar and repair labor per phase so you can compare each foundation job to its estimate.', 'Foundation margins depend on concrete volume, rebar quantities, and repairs that uncover more damage than the initial inspection showed. This course covers tracking concrete and rebar by phase, recording repair labor and materials, and billing change orders for hidden damage. Tax treatment of materials and subcontracts varies by state; confirm details with your accountant.', 'intermediate', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'amber', false, 50, array['Tracking concrete volume by phase', 'Rebar quantities against the schedule', 'Recording repair labor and materials', 'Billing hidden damage as change orders', 'Progress billing tied to inspections']::text[], null, 'Track concrete volume, rebar and repair labor per phase so you can compare each foundation job to its estimate.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:foundations-hr')::uuid, 'foundations-hr', 'foundations', 'hr', 'Training Foundation Crews for Rebar, Forming and Drainage', 'Build crews skilled in rebar tying, form layout and drainage installation, with clear inspection habits.', 'Foundation crews need skill in rebar tying, form layout, and drainage installation, and inspection-ready work depends on careful habits. This course covers hiring and training for rebar and forming, drainage installation standards, and self-checks before inspections. Wage and classification rules vary by state; confirm them with your accountant.', 'beginner', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'rose', false, 60, array['Hiring laborers for rebar and forming', 'Rebar tying and cover standards', 'Drainage installation and slope checks', 'Self-inspection before the building inspector', 'Keeping crews through slow seasons']::text[], 'Training Foundation Crews for Rebar, Forming and Drainage', 'Build crews skilled in rebar tying, form layout and drainage installation, with clear inspection habits.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:foundations-growth')::uuid, 'foundations-growth', 'foundations', 'growth', 'Repeat Foundation Work from Waterproofing and Repair Clients', 'Build repeat work from waterproofing follow-up, monitoring visits and builders who need reliable foundation subs.', 'Foundation and waterproofing work often leads to follow-up visits, and builders need dependable subs for each new home. This course covers follow-up after repairs, monitoring and warranty visits, and relationships with builders and real estate inspectors. Warranty terms, marketing, and solicitation rules vary by locality.', 'intermediate', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'cyan', false, 70, array['Follow-up visits after waterproofing', 'Monitoring and warranty inspections', 'Relationships with builders', 'Referrals from home inspectors', 'Tracking repeat clients by repair type']::text[], 'Repeat Foundation Work from Waterproofing and Repair Clients', 'Build repeat work from waterproofing follow-up, monitoring visits and builders who need reliable foundation subs.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:foundations-safety')::uuid, 'foundations-safety', 'foundations', 'safety', 'Foundation Safety: Excavation Walls, Concrete Handling and Rebar', 'Protect crews in deep excavations, handle wet concrete and manage rebar and form hazards.', 'Foundation work involves deep excavations, wet concrete, and exposed rebar and forms that create trip and impalement hazards. This course covers excavation protection and access, concrete handling and skin protection, and rebar and form hazard controls. Excavation, concrete, and fall protection rules vary by state and locality; confirm the requirements that apply to your jobs.', 'advanced', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'slate', false, 80, array['Excavation protection and safe access', 'Wet concrete skin and eye protection', 'Rebar cap and form hazard control', 'Crane and pump line safety', 'Ground stability near excavations']::text[], null, 'Protect crews in deep excavations, handle wet concrete and manage rebar and form hazards.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:masonry-getting-started')::uuid, 'masonry-getting-started', 'masonry', 'getting_started', 'Starting a Masonry Business: Licensing, Insurance and Structural Work', 'Business basics for a masonry company, including licensing, liability insurance and structural limits on retaining walls.', 'Masonry work is heavy and structural, and retaining walls and chimneys carry significant liability if they fail. This course covers business setup, licensing or registration for masonry, liability and workers'' comp coverage, and engineering and permit requirements for walls and chimneys. Licensing and structural permit rules vary by state and locality; confirm them with your licensing board and building department.', 'beginner', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'slate', false, 10, array['Entity setup and tax registration basics', 'Licensing or registration for masonry', 'Liability coverage for structural walls', 'Engineering and permits for retaining walls', 'Choosing veneer, repair, hardscape or all three']::text[], null, 'Business basics for a masonry company, including licensing, liability insurance and structural limits on retaining walls.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:masonry-sales')::uuid, 'masonry-sales', 'masonry', 'sales', 'Selling Tuckpointing, Repair and New Veneer with Clear Scope', 'Explain the joint work, mortar type and wall condition so customers understand what repair or veneer includes.', 'Customers often ask for the cheapest tuckpointing and expect the mortar to match old joints without testing. This course covers inspecting joints and wall condition, explaining mortar type and why matching matters, and presenting veneer and repair options with clear scope. Material and warranty terms vary by supplier; state them in writing.', 'intermediate', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'cyan', false, 20, array['Inspecting joints and wall condition', 'Explaining mortar type and matching', 'Presenting veneer versus repair options', 'Handling the cheapest-mortar request', 'Writing proposals with clear scope and exclusions']::text[], 'Selling Tuckpointing, Repair and New Veneer with Clear Scope', 'Explain the joint work, mortar type and wall condition so customers understand what repair or veneer includes.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:masonry-estimating')::uuid, 'masonry-estimating', 'masonry', 'estimating', 'Masonry Estimates: Units, Mortar, Reinforcement and Scaffolding', 'Count brick or block by wall area, add mortar, reinforcement, ties, scaffolding and waste in one estimate.', 'Masonry estimates start with wall area and unit counts, then add mortar, reinforcement, ties, flashing, and scaffolding. Openings, corners, and cut units change waste more than many customers expect. This course covers unit takeoffs by wall, mortar and reinforcement quantities, and pricing for scaffolding and cold-weather protection.', 'intermediate', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'navy', false, 30, array['Unit takeoffs by wall and opening', 'Mortar and reinforcement quantities', 'Ties, flashing and weeps', 'Scaffolding and access pricing', 'Cold-weather protection allowances']::text[], null, 'Count brick or block by wall area, add mortar, reinforcement, ties, scaffolding and waste in one estimate.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:masonry-project-management')::uuid, 'masonry-project-management', 'masonry', 'project_management', 'Scheduling Masonry Around Temperature, Cure and Scaffold Setup', 'Plan masonry work around temperature limits, mortar cure, scaffold setup and the trades that follow.', 'Masonry is sensitive to temperature, wind, and rain, and mortar must cure before loads are placed. This course covers scheduling around temperature and weather, planning scaffold setup, and coordinating with framing, roofing, and window trades. Cold-weather masonry requirements vary by specification and locality; confirm them before scheduling winter work.', 'intermediate', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'green', false, 40, array['Temperature and weather scheduling limits', 'Scaffold setup and move sequence', 'Mortar cure before loading', 'Coordinating with framing and roofing trades', 'Protecting finished masonry from weather']::text[], null, 'Plan masonry work around temperature limits, mortar cure, scaffold setup and the trades that follow.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:masonry-accounting')::uuid, 'masonry-accounting', 'masonry', 'accounting', 'Masonry Job Costing: Units, Mortar, Scaffolding and Crew Hours', 'Track units, mortar, scaffolding rental and crew hours by job so each wall is compared to its bid.', 'Masonry margins depend on unit waste, mortar use, scaffolding costs, and labor hours that vary with wall complexity. This course covers tracking unit and mortar use against the takeoff, recording scaffolding rental and crew hours, and billing change orders for hidden conditions. Tax treatment of materials and subcontracts varies by state; confirm details with your accountant.', 'intermediate', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'amber', false, 50, array['Tracking units and waste by wall', 'Mortar use against the takeoff', 'Scaffolding rental and move costs', 'Crew hours by wall complexity', 'Deposits and progress billing for masonry']::text[], null, 'Track units, mortar, scaffolding rental and crew hours by job so each wall is compared to its bid.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:masonry-hr')::uuid, 'masonry-hr', 'masonry', 'hr', 'Training Masons and Helpers for Level Courses and Clean Joints', 'Build masons and helpers who lay level courses, strike consistent joints and mix mortar to specification.', 'Masonry quality depends on level courses, consistent joints, and mortar mixed to specification, and those skills take years to build. This course covers hiring masons and helpers, training on mortar mixing and joint striking, and quality checks for plumb and level walls. Wage, apprenticeship, and classification rules vary by state; confirm them with your accountant.', 'beginner', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'rose', false, 60, array['Hiring masons and helpers', 'Mortar mixing to specification', 'Striking joints consistently', 'Plumb and level checks on each course', 'Apprenticeship paths for new masons']::text[], null, 'Build masons and helpers who lay level courses, strike consistent joints and mix mortar to specification.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:masonry-growth')::uuid, 'masonry-growth', 'masonry', 'growth', 'Repeat Masonry Work: Tuckpointing Cycles and Property Maintenance', 'Build repeat work from tuckpointing follow-up, chimney inspections and property managers with ongoing repair needs.', 'Masonry needs periodic tuckpointing and chimney repair, which creates repeat work for homeowners and property managers. This course covers inspection-based follow-up, offering maintenance on chimneys and walls, and relationships with property managers and builders. Marketing and solicitation rules vary by locality.', 'intermediate', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'cyan', false, 70, array['Inspection-based follow-up for tuckpointing', 'Chimney inspection and repair offers', 'Property manager maintenance programs', 'Builder relationships for veneer and hardscape', 'Referrals from finished projects']::text[], null, 'Build repeat work from tuckpointing follow-up, chimney inspections and property managers with ongoing repair needs.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:masonry-safety')::uuid, 'masonry-safety', 'masonry', 'safety', 'Masonry Safety: Scaffold Access, Heavy Units and Silica Dust', 'Work safely on scaffolds, lift heavy units with mechanical aids and control silica dust from cutting and grinding.', 'Masonry crews work on scaffolds, lift heavy units and pallets, and cut or grind masonry that releases silica dust. This course covers scaffold setup and inspection, mechanical lifts and team lifts for units, and dust control and respiratory protection during cutting. Scaffolding, silica, and lifting rules vary by state and locality; confirm the requirements that apply to your work.', 'advanced', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'slate', false, 80, array['Scaffold setup, inspection and access', 'Mechanical lifts and team lifts for units', 'Silica dust control during cutting', 'Respiratory protection for grinding work', 'Wall stability during partial construction']::text[], 'Masonry Safety: Scaffold Access, Heavy Units and Silica Dust', 'Work safely on scaffolds, lift heavy units with mechanical aids and control silica dust from cutting and grinding.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:asphalt-paving-getting-started')::uuid, 'asphalt-paving-getting-started', 'asphalt-paving', 'getting_started', 'Starting an Asphalt Business: Licensing, Bonding and Insurance', 'Business basics for an asphalt and paving company, including licensing, bonding and liability coverage for active sites.', 'Paving businesses often bid on commercial and public lots and drives, which can require bonds and specific insurance. This course covers business setup, licensing or registration for paving work, bonding and liability coverage for active sites, and public bid qualification. Licensing, bonding, and public bid rules vary by state and locality; confirm them with your licensing board and the agencies you plan to bid.', 'beginner', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'slate', false, 10, array['Entity setup and tax registration basics', 'Licensing and bonding for paving work', 'Liability coverage for active sites', 'Qualifying for public and commercial bids', 'Choosing residential, commercial or both']::text[], null, 'Business basics for an asphalt and paving company, including licensing, bonding and liability coverage for active sites.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:asphalt-paving-sales')::uuid, 'asphalt-paving-sales', 'asphalt-paving', 'sales', 'Selling Paving Jobs on Base Preparation, Not Just Surface', 'Explain base repair, thickness and drainage so the property owner understands what drives pavement life.', 'Property owners often compare paving bids by surface price and miss that base repair and thickness decide how long pavement lasts. This course covers site inspections for cracks and drainage, presenting base prep and thickness options, and explaining sealcoat and striping as separate services. Warranty and material terms vary by supplier; state them in writing.', 'intermediate', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'cyan', false, 20, array['Inspecting cracks, ponding and drainage', 'Presenting base prep and thickness options', 'Explaining sealcoat as a separate service', 'Handling the lowest-price comparison', 'Writing proposals with base and surface lines']::text[], 'Selling Paving Jobs on Base Preparation, Not Just Surface', 'Explain base repair, thickness and drainage so the property owner understands what drives pavement life.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:asphalt-paving-estimating')::uuid, 'asphalt-paving-estimating', 'asphalt-paving', 'estimating', 'Paving Estimates: Base Prep, Asphalt Tonnage, Sealcoat and Striping', 'Calculate base aggregate, asphalt tonnage by thickness, sealcoat area and striping footage for each paving scope.', 'Paving estimates depend on area, thickness, and base aggregate depth, which together set asphalt tonnage. Sealcoat coverage, striping footage, and cutting or patching for failed areas are priced separately. This course covers tonnage takeoffs by thickness, base aggregate calculations, and pricing for sealcoat, striping, and patch work.', 'intermediate', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'navy', false, 30, array['Area and thickness tonnage calculations', 'Base aggregate depth and quantities', 'Sealcoat coverage and passes', 'Striping footage and layout', 'Patch and cut-out pricing']::text[], null, 'Calculate base aggregate, asphalt tonnage by thickness, sealcoat area and striping footage for each paving scope.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:asphalt-paving-project-management')::uuid, 'asphalt-paving-project-management', 'asphalt-paving', 'project_management', 'Scheduling Paving Around Temperature, Traffic and Site Access', 'Plan paving days around temperature, delivery windows, traffic control and the owner''s need to use the lot.', 'Asphalt must be placed within temperature limits, and deliveries run on a tight window once the mix leaves the plant. This course covers scheduling around temperature and weather, coordinating hot-mix deliveries, and planning traffic control and phased closures for the property. Traffic control and temperature requirements vary by locality and specification; confirm them before scheduling.', 'intermediate', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'green', false, 40, array['Temperature limits for placement', 'Hot-mix delivery window coordination', 'Phased closures and traffic control', 'Sealcoat cure time before traffic', 'Striping timing after sealcoat']::text[], null, 'Plan paving days around temperature, delivery windows, traffic control and the owner''s need to use the lot.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:asphalt-paving-accounting')::uuid, 'asphalt-paving-accounting', 'asphalt-paving', 'accounting', 'Paving Job Costing: Tonnage Overruns, Fuel and Equipment Hours', 'Track tonnage, fuel, equipment hours and crew hours by job so you can tell whether a paving job made its margin.', 'Paving margins shift with tonnage overruns, fuel prices, and equipment hours that run long on tight sites. This course covers tracking tonnage delivered against the takeoff, recording equipment and fuel costs, and billing change orders for base repair found during prep. Tax treatment of materials and equipment varies by state; confirm details with your accountant.', 'intermediate', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'amber', false, 50, array['Tonnage delivered against the takeoff', 'Equipment hours and fuel tracking', 'Recording base repair as change orders', 'Striping and sealcoat cost tracking', 'Progress billing for paving phases']::text[], null, 'Track tonnage, fuel, equipment hours and crew hours by job so you can tell whether a paving job made its margin.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:asphalt-paving-hr')::uuid, 'asphalt-paving-hr', 'asphalt-paving', 'hr', 'Hiring and Training Paving Crews for Raking, Rolling and Flagging', 'Build crews that rake, roll and place asphalt evenly, and run flagging and traffic control on active sites.', 'Paving crews need people who rake and roll evenly, work quickly with hot mix, and handle traffic control. This course covers hiring laborers and equipment operators, training on raking and rolling, and flagging and traffic control roles. Wage, classification, and certification rules vary by state; confirm them with your accountant and licensing board.', 'beginner', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'rose', false, 60, array['Hiring laborers and equipment operators', 'Raking and rolling techniques', 'Flagging and traffic control roles', 'Hot-mix handling and crew pacing', 'Keeping a paving crew through slow seasons']::text[], null, 'Build crews that rake, roll and place asphalt evenly, and run flagging and traffic control on active sites.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:asphalt-paving-growth')::uuid, 'asphalt-paving-growth', 'asphalt-paving', 'growth', 'Repeat Paving Work: Sealcoat Cycles, Striping and Patching', 'Build repeat work from sealcoat and striping cycles, patching calls and property managers with multiple lots.', 'Pavement needs sealcoating, striping, and patching on a cycle, which creates repeat work for property managers and homeowners. This course covers maintenance schedules for sealcoat and striping, patch and crack-sealing calls, and relationships with property managers with multiple lots. Marketing, bidding, and solicitation rules vary by locality.', 'intermediate', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'cyan', false, 70, array['Sealcoat and striping maintenance cycles', 'Crack sealing and patch service calls', 'Property manager accounts with multiple lots', 'Follow-up after new paving', 'Referrals from contractors and property managers']::text[], 'Repeat Paving Work: Sealcoat Cycles, Striping and Patching', 'Build repeat work from sealcoat and striping cycles, patching calls and property managers with multiple lots.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:asphalt-paving-safety')::uuid, 'asphalt-paving-safety', 'asphalt-paving', 'safety', 'Paving Safety: Hot Mix, Equipment Traffic and Sealcoat Fumes', 'Protect crews from hot mix burns, manage equipment near workers and control sealcoat fumes and skin exposure.', 'Paving work involves hot mix that causes burns, rollers and trucks moving near workers, and sealcoat products that release fumes. This course covers hot-mix burn prevention, equipment spotter and separation practices, and ventilation and skin protection around sealcoat. Traffic control, equipment, and product handling rules vary by state and locality; confirm the requirements that apply to your work.', 'advanced', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'slate', false, 80, array['Hot-mix burn prevention and PPE', 'Spotter and equipment separation on site', 'Traffic control and flagging safety', 'Sealcoat fume and skin exposure control', 'Heat illness prevention on hot pavement']::text[], 'Paving Safety: Hot Mix, Equipment Traffic and Sealcoat Fumes', 'Protect crews from hot mix burns, manage equipment near workers and control sealcoat fumes and skin exposure.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:demolition-getting-started')::uuid, 'demolition-getting-started', 'demolition', 'getting_started', 'Starting a Demolition Business: Licensing, Permits and Insurance', 'Business basics for a demolition company, including licensing, permits, liability coverage and utility disconnect rules.', 'Demolition involves structural removal, utility disconnects, and debris hauling, and mistakes can injure people and damage neighboring property. This course covers business setup, licensing and permits, liability and equipment coverage, and responsibilities for utility disconnects. Licensing, permit, and disconnect rules vary by state and locality; confirm them with your licensing board and building department.', 'beginner', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'slate', false, 10, array['Entity setup and tax registration basics', 'Licensing and permits for demolition', 'Liability and equipment coverage', 'Utility disconnect responsibilities', 'Choosing interior, exterior or full teardown work']::text[], null, 'Business basics for a demolition company, including licensing, permits, liability coverage and utility disconnect rules.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:demolition-sales')::uuid, 'demolition-sales', 'demolition', 'sales', 'Presenting Demolition Scope, Disposal and Add-Ons Clearly', 'Write the demolition scope, disposal and protection items into the proposal so the price is clear before work begins.', 'Demolition prices change with what is found inside walls, and customers often push back on dump fees and protection costs. This course covers scoping demolition with a walkthrough, presenting disposal and protection as line items, and writing change-order terms for hidden materials. Disposal and hazardous material rules vary by locality; state them in writing.', 'intermediate', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'cyan', false, 20, array['Walkthroughs that find hidden conditions', 'Presenting disposal and dump fees as lines', 'Protection of adjacent rooms and finishes', 'Writing change-order terms for hidden materials', 'Handling the ''why is dump fee so high'' question']::text[], 'Presenting Demolition Scope, Disposal and Add-Ons Clearly', 'Write the demolition scope, disposal and protection items into the proposal so the price is clear before work begins.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:demolition-estimating')::uuid, 'demolition-estimating', 'demolition', 'estimating', 'Demolition Estimates: Labor, Equipment, Dumpsters and Haul-Off', 'Estimate demolition by area and debris volume, with dumpsters, haul-off, equipment and protection priced separately.', 'Demolition estimates start with area and debris volume, then add labor, equipment, dumpster sizes, haul-off trips, and protection. Hazardous material testing, if required, can change the schedule and cost before work begins. This course covers debris volume estimating, dumpster and haul-off pricing, equipment time, and allowances for protection.', 'intermediate', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'navy', false, 30, array['Debris volume by area and room', 'Dumpster sizes and swap-out pricing', 'Haul-off trips and disposal fees', 'Equipment time for heavy removal', 'Protection and dust barrier allowances']::text[], null, 'Estimate demolition by area and debris volume, with dumpsters, haul-off, equipment and protection priced separately.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:demolition-project-management')::uuid, 'demolition-project-management', 'demolition', 'project_management', 'Sequencing Demolition Around Utility Disconnects and Protection', 'Plan disconnects, protection, room-by-room removal and debris flow so the site stays safe and on schedule.', 'Demolition sequence depends on utility disconnects, protection of adjacent areas, and a plan for moving debris out of the building. This course covers scheduling disconnects and inspections before removal, planning room-by-room tear-out, and coordinating dumpster placement and haul-off. Utility and disconnect requirements vary by locality; confirm them before the first day.', 'intermediate', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'green', false, 40, array['Utility disconnect scheduling before removal', 'Room-by-room removal sequence', 'Dumpster placement and haul-off timing', 'Protecting adjacent spaces during tear-out', 'Handover to the next trade']::text[], null, 'Plan disconnects, protection, room-by-room removal and debris flow so the site stays safe and on schedule.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:demolition-accounting')::uuid, 'demolition-accounting', 'demolition', 'accounting', 'Demolition Job Costing: Dump Fees, Equipment and Change Orders', 'Track dump fees, equipment hours and labor per job so you can see what hidden materials cost in time and money.', 'Demolition margins are lost on dump fees, equipment hours, and hidden materials that stop work until they are handled. This course covers tracking dump fees and haul-off by job, recording equipment and labor hours, and billing change orders for unexpected materials. Tax treatment of equipment and disposal costs varies by state; confirm details with your accountant.', 'intermediate', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'amber', false, 50, array['Tracking dump fees and haul-off by job', 'Recording equipment and labor hours', 'Billing change orders for hidden materials', 'Deposits and progress billing for demo', 'Reviewing margin after each demolition']::text[], null, 'Track dump fees, equipment hours and labor per job so you can see what hidden materials cost in time and money.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:demolition-hr')::uuid, 'demolition-hr', 'demolition', 'hr', 'Hiring and Training Demolition Crews for Careful Tear-Out', 'Build crews that remove material carefully, keep the site organized and communicate around equipment.', 'Demolition crews need people who work carefully, keep debris moving, and communicate about hazards. This course covers hiring laborers and operators, training on careful tear-out and salvage, and defining roles for debris handling and equipment spotting. Wage, classification, and overtime rules vary by state; confirm them with your accountant.', 'beginner', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'rose', false, 60, array['Hiring laborers and equipment operators', 'Careful tear-out and salvage practices', 'Debris handling and site organization', 'Spotter roles around equipment', 'Keeping demolition crews through slow periods']::text[], 'Hiring and Training Demolition Crews for Careful Tear-Out', 'Build crews that remove material carefully, keep the site organized and communicate around equipment.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:demolition-growth')::uuid, 'demolition-growth', 'demolition', 'growth', 'Repeat Demolition Work from Remodelers, Builders and Property Managers', 'Earn repeat demolition work from remodelers and builders, plus clean-out jobs for property managers.', 'Demolition work repeats with remodelers and builders who need tear-out before new construction, and property managers who need clean-outs between tenants. This course covers building relationships with remodelers and builders, offering turnover clean-outs, and following up after large jobs. Marketing, bidding, and solicitation rules vary by locality.', 'intermediate', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'cyan', false, 70, array['Relationships with remodelers and builders', 'Turnover clean-outs for property managers', 'Follow-up after large tear-outs', 'Salvage and reuse as a service', 'Tracking repeat clients by job type']::text[], null, 'Earn repeat demolition work from remodelers and builders, plus clean-out jobs for property managers.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:demolition-safety')::uuid, 'demolition-safety', 'demolition', 'safety', 'Demolition Safety: Hazardous Materials, Collapse and Utilities', 'Check for hazardous materials before demolition, manage structural collapse risk and protect crews from utility hazards.', 'Demolition exposes workers to hazardous materials in older buildings, structural collapse, and live utilities hidden in walls. This course covers hazardous material checks, structural assessment before removing load-bearing elements, and utility lock-out before cutting. Hazardous material, structural, and utility rules vary by state and locality; confirm them for each job.', 'advanced', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'slate', false, 80, array['Hazardous material checks before disturbing', 'Structural assessment before removing elements', 'Utility lock-out before cutting', 'Falling debris and overhead hazards', 'Equipment and spotter safety on site']::text[], null, 'Check for hazardous materials before demolition, manage structural collapse risk and protect crews from utility hazards.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:basements-getting-started')::uuid, 'basements-getting-started', 'basements', 'getting_started', 'Basement Finishing Business: Permits, Licensing and Insurance', 'Business basics for a basement finishing company, including licensing, insurance and permit-required scope.', 'Basement finishing involves framing, electrical, and sometimes egress and mechanical changes that often require permits. This course covers business setup, licensing scope for the trades you perform, insurance for work in occupied homes, and which basement changes typically need permits. Permit and egress rules vary by state and locality; confirm them with your building department before bidding.', 'beginner', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'slate', false, 10, array['Entity setup and tax registration basics', 'Licensing scope for basement trades', 'Insurance for occupied-home finishing', 'Permits for framing, electrical and egress', 'Choosing which trades to self-perform']::text[], null, 'Business basics for a basement finishing company, including licensing, insurance and permit-required scope.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:basements-sales')::uuid, 'basements-sales', 'basements', 'sales', 'Scoping Basement Finishes Around Moisture and Egress', 'Walk the basement with the homeowner, identify moisture and egress needs and agree on scope before pricing.', 'Homeowners often price a basement by its floor area and are surprised by moisture control, egress windows, or electrical upgrades. This course covers walkthroughs that check for moisture, identifying egress and ceiling-height requirements, and presenting phased finish options with the required work listed first. Local code requirements vary; confirm them before the proposal goes out.', 'intermediate', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'cyan', false, 20, array['Walkthroughs that check for moisture', 'Identifying egress and ceiling-height needs', 'Presenting phased finish options', 'Listing required work before finishes', 'Handling the ''just finish the room'' request']::text[], 'Scoping Basement Finishes Around Moisture and Egress', 'Walk the basement with the homeowner, identify moisture and egress needs and agree on scope before pricing.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:basements-estimating')::uuid, 'basements-estimating', 'basements', 'estimating', 'Basement Estimates by Phase: Framing, Electrical, Finishes', 'Estimate a basement by phase, with framing, insulation, electrical, drywall, flooring and bath work in separate sections.', 'Basement estimates are built by phase: framing and soffits, insulation and vapor control, electrical rough-in, drywall, flooring, and any bath or egress work. Moisture remediation and ceiling-height limits can change the scope before framing starts. This course covers takeoffs by phase, allowances for finishes, and contingency language for hidden moisture.', 'intermediate', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'navy', false, 30, array['Framing and soffit takeoffs by phase', 'Insulation and vapor control quantities', 'Electrical rough-in and fixture allowances', 'Drywall, flooring and trim pricing', 'Moisture remediation contingency language']::text[], 'Basement Estimates by Phase: Framing, Electrical, Finishes', 'Estimate a basement by phase, with framing, insulation, electrical, drywall, flooring and bath work in separate sections.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:basements-project-management')::uuid, 'basements-project-management', 'basements', 'project_management', 'Sequencing a Basement Finish Through Inspections and Close-Up', 'Plan framing, rough-ins, inspections and drywall so the basement is inspected before walls close.', 'Basement work follows a strict order: framing, rough-in, inspection, insulation, and then drywall, with flooring and finishes last. This course covers scheduling framing and rough-in inspections, planning insulation and vapor control before close-up, and coordinating drywall, flooring, and trim trades. Inspection requirements vary by locality; confirm them before closing walls.', 'intermediate', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'green', false, 40, array['Framing and rough-in inspection timing', 'Insulation and vapor control before close-up', 'Drywall and flooring sequence', 'Coordinating bath rough-in and fixtures', 'Final inspection and homeowner walkthrough']::text[], null, 'Plan framing, rough-ins, inspections and drywall so the basement is inspected before walls close.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:basements-accounting')::uuid, 'basements-accounting', 'basements', 'accounting', 'Basement Job Costing: Phases, Moisture Work and Change Orders', 'Track costs by phase and record moisture remediation and change orders so the owner sees what drove the total.', 'Basement margins shift with moisture remediation, hidden conditions, and finish selections made after framing starts. This course covers cost codes by phase, tracking moisture and remediation work separately, and documenting change orders before work begins. Tax treatment of materials and subcontracts varies by state; confirm details with your accountant.', 'intermediate', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'amber', false, 50, array['Cost codes by phase', 'Tracking moisture remediation separately', 'Documenting change orders before work', 'Subcontract tracking for electrical and bath', 'Progress billing tied to inspections']::text[], null, 'Track costs by phase and record moisture remediation and change orders so the owner sees what drove the total.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:basements-hr')::uuid, 'basements-hr', 'basements', 'hr', 'Building a Basement Finish Crew with Framing and Trade Skills', 'Hire framers, drywall finishers and helpers who can move through a basement efficiently and protect the finished work.', 'Basement finishing relies on framers, drywall finishers, and helpers who work in low-light, tight spaces. This course covers hiring for multi-skill basement crews, defining roles across framing and finish, and training on protection standards for occupied homes. Wage and classification rules vary by state; confirm them with your accountant.', 'beginner', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'rose', false, 60, array['Hiring framers and drywall finishers', 'Roles across framing and finish', 'Working in low-light, low-height spaces', 'Protection standards for occupied homes', 'Retaining crews between basement jobs']::text[], null, 'Hire framers, drywall finishers and helpers who can move through a basement efficiently and protect the finished work.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:basements-growth')::uuid, 'basements-growth', 'basements', 'growth', 'Repeat Basement Work from Homeowners and Builders', 'Earn repeat work from homeowners who finish more space, builders who need basement subs and referrals from finished clients.', 'Basement finishing repeats with homeowners who expand into bathrooms or bedrooms, builders who need reliable basement subs, and referrals from satisfied clients. This course covers final walkthroughs, post-job check-ins, and relationships with builders and waterproofing companies. Marketing and solicitation rules vary by locality.', 'intermediate', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'cyan', false, 70, array['Final walkthrough and care instructions', 'Post-job check-ins for the next phase', 'Relationships with builders', 'Referrals from waterproofing companies', 'Asking for referrals and reviews']::text[], 'Repeat Basement Work from Homeowners and Builders', 'Earn repeat work from homeowners who finish more space, builders who need basement subs and referrals from finished clients.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:basements-safety')::uuid, 'basements-safety', 'basements', 'safety', 'Basement Safety: Low Light, Moisture, Electrical and Confined Access', 'Manage low-light and tight-access hazards, electrical risk in wet spaces and trip hazards in unfinished basements.', 'Basement work happens in low light, tight spaces, and damp conditions where electrical hazards and trip risks are higher. This course covers lighting and access planning, electrical safety around moisture, and ladder and stair safety during framing. Electrical, egress, and confined-space rules vary by state and locality; confirm the requirements that apply to your jobs.', 'advanced', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'slate', false, 80, array['Lighting and access planning', 'Electrical safety around moisture', 'Ladder and stair safety during framing', 'Trip hazards in unfinished basements', 'Mold, dust and air quality precautions']::text[], null, 'Manage low-light and tight-access hazards, electrical risk in wet spaces and trip hazards in unfinished basements.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:additions-getting-started')::uuid, 'additions-getting-started', 'additions', 'getting_started', 'Starting an Addition Business: Permits, Licensing and Insurance', 'Business basics for a home addition company, including licensing, insurance and the permit path for structural work.', 'Additions are structural projects that tie into existing homes, so permits, engineering, and inspections are central. This course covers business setup, licensing scope for structural and trade work, insurance for occupied-home construction, and the permit path for foundations and roof tie-ins. Permit and licensing rules vary by state and locality; confirm them with your building department.', 'beginner', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'slate', false, 10, array['Entity setup and tax registration basics', 'Licensing scope for structural work', 'Insurance for occupied-home construction', 'Permit path for foundation and framing', 'Working with architects and engineers']::text[], null, 'Business basics for a home addition company, including licensing, insurance and the permit path for structural work.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:additions-sales')::uuid, 'additions-sales', 'additions', 'sales', 'Presenting Addition Designs with Phased Pricing', 'Present the addition as foundation, shell, mechanical and finish phases so the homeowner sees what each one costs.', 'Homeowners often fall for an addition design and then react to the total once the foundation, roof tie-in, and mechanical work are added. This course covers presenting designs in phases, explaining why structural and mechanical work come first, and offering finish alternates that let the homeowner set the budget. Design and product warranties vary; state them in writing.', 'intermediate', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'cyan', false, 20, array['Presenting designs as phases', 'Explaining foundation and roof tie-in needs', 'Mechanical and HVAC upgrades explained', 'Offering finish alternates', 'Writing proposals with a clear total']::text[], 'Presenting Addition Designs with Phased Pricing', 'Present the addition as foundation, shell, mechanical and finish phases so the homeowner sees what each one costs.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:additions-estimating')::uuid, 'additions-estimating', 'additions', 'estimating', 'Phased Addition Estimates: Foundation, Shell, Mechanical and Finishes', 'Estimate an addition by phase, with foundation, framing, roofing, windows, mechanical and finish work in separate sections.', 'Addition estimates build phase by phase, with foundation, shell, roof, windows, mechanical, and finishes each carrying its own quantities and allowances. Tie-ins to the existing house and mechanical extensions often add scope the design does not show. This course covers phase takeoffs, tie-in allowances, and contingency language for existing conditions.', 'intermediate', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'navy', false, 30, array['Phase takeoffs from design and plans', 'Tie-in allowances to the existing house', 'Mechanical extension pricing', 'Window and door allowances', 'Contingency language for existing conditions']::text[], null, 'Estimate an addition by phase, with foundation, framing, roofing, windows, mechanical and finish work in separate sections.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:additions-project-management')::uuid, 'additions-project-management', 'additions', 'project_management', 'Sequencing an Addition from Foundation Through Final Inspection', 'Plan foundation, framing, roof dry-in, rough-ins and inspections so the addition is weathertight and approved.', 'An addition is built in a strict order, from foundation through dry-in, rough-ins, inspections, and finishes, and weather exposure starts once the roof opens. This course covers sequencing foundations and framing, planning roof dry-in before rough-ins, and scheduling inspections at each phase. Inspection and tie-in requirements vary by locality; confirm them with the building department before starting.', 'advanced', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'green', false, 40, array['Foundation and framing sequence', 'Roof dry-in before rough-ins', 'Inspection holds at each phase', 'Tie-in work on the existing house', 'Final inspection and homeowner handoff']::text[], null, 'Plan foundation, framing, roof dry-in, rough-ins and inspections so the addition is weathertight and approved.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:additions-accounting')::uuid, 'additions-accounting', 'additions', 'accounting', 'Addition Job Costing: Phase Costs, Tie-Ins and Change Orders', 'Track costs by phase and document tie-in and design changes so each addition is compared to its estimate.', 'Addition margins shift with tie-in surprises, design changes, and phases that run long. This course covers cost codes by phase, tracking tie-in and existing-house work separately, and documenting change orders before work begins. Tax treatment of materials, subcontracts, and deposits varies by state; confirm details with your accountant.', 'intermediate', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'amber', false, 50, array['Cost codes by phase', 'Tracking tie-in work separately', 'Documenting design changes as change orders', 'Subcontract and engineering cost tracking', 'Progress billing tied to inspections']::text[], 'Addition Job Costing: Phase Costs, Tie-Ins and Change Orders', 'Track costs by phase and document tie-in and design changes so each addition is compared to its estimate.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:additions-hr')::uuid, 'additions-hr', 'additions', 'hr', 'Building an Addition Crew with Structural and Finish Skills', 'Hire framers, roofers and finish carpenters, then train crews for tie-in work and protection of the existing home.', 'Addition work needs framers, roofers, and finish carpenters who can handle tie-ins to an existing house. This course covers hiring for structural and finish skills, defining crew roles across phases, and training on protecting the existing home during tie-in work. Wage and classification rules vary by state; confirm them with your accountant.', 'beginner', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'rose', false, 60, array['Hiring framers and finish carpenters', 'Roles across foundation, shell and finish', 'Tie-in work and existing-house protection', 'Coordinating subs across multiple phases', 'Retaining crew through a long project']::text[], 'Building an Addition Crew with Structural and Finish Skills', 'Hire framers, roofers and finish carpenters, then train crews for tie-in work and protection of the existing home.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:additions-growth')::uuid, 'additions-growth', 'additions', 'growth', 'Repeat Addition Work from Homeowners and Designers', 'Earn repeat work from homeowners who expand again, designers who specify additions and neighbors who see a finished project.', 'Additions often lead to more work, as homeowners expand again, designers specify projects, and neighbors ask about their own homes. This course covers relationships with designers and architects, follow-up after completion, and portfolio photos with permission. Marketing and solicitation rules vary by locality.', 'intermediate', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'cyan', false, 70, array['Relationships with architects and designers', 'Follow-up after the final inspection', 'Portfolio photos with client permission', 'Neighborhood follow-up after a visible project', 'Referrals from finished homeowners']::text[], 'Repeat Addition Work from Homeowners and Designers', 'Earn repeat work from homeowners who expand again, designers who specify additions and neighbors who see a finished project.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:additions-safety')::uuid, 'additions-safety', 'additions', 'safety', 'Addition Safety: Excavation, Roof Openings and Tie-In Hazards', 'Manage excavation and roof-opening hazards, protect occupants during tie-ins and control dust in an occupied home.', 'Additions involve excavation next to occupied homes, open roof areas, and tie-in cuts that can expose live systems. This course covers excavation protection near the house, fall protection at open roof areas, and lock-out and protection before cutting into existing systems. Excavation, fall protection, and utility rules vary by state and locality; confirm the requirements that apply to your jobs.', 'advanced', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'slate', false, 80, array['Excavation protection near the house', 'Fall protection at open roof areas', 'Lock-out before cutting into existing systems', 'Dust and occupant protection during tie-ins', 'Crane and material hoist safety']::text[], null, 'Manage excavation and roof-opening hazards, protect occupants during tie-ins and control dust in an occupied home.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:garages-getting-started')::uuid, 'garages-getting-started', 'garages', 'getting_started', 'Starting a Garage Construction Business: Permits and Insurance', 'Business basics for a garage construction company, including licensing, insurance and setback and permit rules.', 'Garages are structures that often need permits, setback checks, and inspections for slab, framing, and electrical work. This course covers business setup, licensing scope for structural and trade work, insurance for garage construction, and setback and permit rules for detached and attached structures. Permit and zoning rules vary by state and locality; confirm them with your building department before bidding.', 'beginner', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'slate', false, 10, array['Entity setup and tax registration basics', 'Licensing scope for garage trades', 'Insurance for garage construction', 'Setbacks, zoning and permits', 'Choosing detached, attached or conversion work']::text[], null, 'Business basics for a garage construction company, including licensing, insurance and setback and permit rules.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:garages-sales')::uuid, 'garages-sales', 'garages', 'sales', 'Selling Garage Builds and Conversions with Clear Specs', 'Specify slab thickness, door size, electrical service and roof pitch so the garage the customer sees is the one priced.', 'Garage customers often pick a door and a size without knowing the slab, footing, and electrical needs behind them. This course covers specifying slab thickness, door size, roof pitch, and electrical service in the proposal, and presenting conversion options for attached garages. Door and product warranties vary by manufacturer; state terms in writing.', 'intermediate', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'cyan', false, 20, array['Specifying slab thickness and reinforcement', 'Door size and opening options', 'Roof pitch and matching the house', 'Electrical service and outlet planning', 'Presenting garage conversion options']::text[], 'Selling Garage Builds and Conversions with Clear Specs', 'Specify slab thickness, door size, electrical service and roof pitch so the garage the customer sees is the one priced.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:garages-estimating')::uuid, 'garages-estimating', 'garages', 'estimating', 'Garage Estimates: Slab, Framing, Roofing, Siding, Doors and Electrical', 'Price the garage by system: slab, framing, roof, siding, doors and electrical, each with its own takeoff.', 'Garage estimates are built by system, with slab area and thickness, wall and roof framing, roofing and siding areas, doors, and electrical. Slab thickness, excavation for footings, and electrical service upgrades are common surprises. This course covers takeoffs by system, door and opener allowances, and pricing for electrical and excavation.', 'intermediate', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'navy', false, 30, array['Slab area, thickness and reinforcement', 'Wall and roof framing takeoffs', 'Roofing and siding area takeoffs', 'Door and opener allowances', 'Electrical and excavation pricing']::text[], null, 'Price the garage by system: slab, framing, roof, siding, doors and electrical, each with its own takeoff.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:garages-project-management')::uuid, 'garages-project-management', 'garages', 'project_management', 'Sequencing Garage Slab, Framing, Roof and Doors', 'Plan slab curing, framing, roof dry-in, door install and electrical rough-in so the garage is weathertight and inspected.', 'Garage work moves from slab to framing, roof dry-in, siding, door install, and electrical, and the slab must cure before framing starts. This course covers scheduling slab pours and cure time, sequencing framing and roof dry-in, and coordinating door and electrical installs. Inspection and slab requirements vary by locality; confirm them early.', 'intermediate', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'green', false, 40, array['Slab pour and cure timing', 'Framing and roof dry-in sequence', 'Siding and trim after roof', 'Garage door install and opener timing', 'Electrical rough-in and final inspection']::text[], 'Sequencing Garage Slab, Framing, Roof and Doors', 'Plan slab curing, framing, roof dry-in, door install and electrical rough-in so the garage is weathertight and inspected.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:garages-accounting')::uuid, 'garages-accounting', 'garages', 'accounting', 'Garage Job Costing: Slab Volume, Doors and Electrical Changes', 'Track slab volume, framing, doors and electrical by phase so you can see what changed from the original bid.', 'Garage margins shift with slab volume, door choices made after framing starts, and electrical changes. This course covers cost codes by system, tracking slab and framing against the takeoff, and documenting door and electrical change orders. Tax treatment of materials and subcontracts varies by state; confirm details with your accountant.', 'intermediate', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'amber', false, 50, array['Cost codes by system', 'Tracking slab volume against takeoff', 'Door and opener change orders', 'Electrical change order tracking', 'Progress billing tied to inspections']::text[], null, 'Track slab volume, framing, doors and electrical by phase so you can see what changed from the original bid.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:garages-hr')::uuid, 'garages-hr', 'garages', 'hr', 'Training Garage Crews for Framing, Roofing and Door Installs', 'Build crews that frame square, set doors plumb and work safely on roofs and slabs.', 'Garage crews frame square walls, install doors that must operate smoothly, and work on roofs and slabs. This course covers hiring framers and roofers, training on square framing and door installs, and quality checks before handoff. Wage and classification rules vary by state; confirm them with your accountant.', 'beginner', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'rose', false, 60, array['Hiring framers and roofers', 'Framing square and plumb', 'Garage door install and adjustment', 'Quality checks before handoff', 'Keeping crews through the season']::text[], 'Training Garage Crews for Framing, Roofing and Door Installs', 'Build crews that frame square, set doors plumb and work safely on roofs and slabs.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:garages-growth')::uuid, 'garages-growth', 'garages', 'growth', 'Repeat Garage Work: Door Service, Openers and Neighbor Referrals', 'Build repeat work from door service and opener replacements, plus neighbor and builder referrals.', 'Garage doors and openers need service and replacement over time, and finished garages lead to referrals in the same neighborhood. This course covers door service and opener replacement programs, neighborhood follow-up, and relationships with builders who need garage packages. Marketing and solicitation rules vary by locality.', 'intermediate', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'cyan', false, 70, array['Door service and opener replacement', 'Neighborhood follow-up after a garage build', 'Relationships with builders', 'Referrals from finished homeowners', 'Tracking repeat clients by service type']::text[], null, 'Build repeat work from door service and opener replacements, plus neighbor and builder referrals.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:garages-safety')::uuid, 'garages-safety', 'garages', 'safety', 'Garage Construction Safety: Door Springs, Roof Work and Slab Pours', 'Handle garage door springs safely, manage roof and framing fall exposure and stay safe during slab pours.', 'Garage work involves torsion springs under tension, fall exposure on roofs and framing, and wet concrete during slab pours. This course covers spring handling and door installation safety, fall protection on roofs and framed walls, and concrete pour safety. Garage door, fall protection, and concrete rules vary by state and locality; confirm the requirements that apply to your jobs.', 'advanced', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'slate', false, 80, array['Garage door spring handling and tension', 'Fall protection on roofs and framed walls', 'Wet concrete safety during slab pours', 'Temporary bracing of wall sections', 'Ladder and lift safety at roofline']::text[], null, 'Handle garage door springs safely, manage roof and framing fall exposure and stay safe during slab pours.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:pole-barns-getting-started')::uuid, 'pole-barns-getting-started', 'pole-barns', 'getting_started', 'Starting a Pole Barn Business: Permits, Licensing and Insurance', 'Business basics for a post-frame and metal building company, including licensing, insurance and building permits.', 'Post-frame and metal buildings are structures that often need engineered designs, permits, and inspections for footings and framing. This course covers business setup, licensing scope for structural and trade work, insurance for erection work, and working with engineers on wind and snow load documentation. Licensing and permit rules vary by state and locality; confirm them with your building department and engineers.', 'beginner', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'slate', false, 10, array['Entity setup and tax registration basics', 'Licensing scope for post-frame work', 'Insurance for erection and lift work', 'Permits and engineered drawings', 'Choosing agricultural, residential or commercial work']::text[], null, 'Business basics for a post-frame and metal building company, including licensing, insurance and building permits.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:pole-barns-sales')::uuid, 'pole-barns-sales', 'pole-barns', 'sales', 'Presenting Kit and Installed Pole Barn Quotes Side by Side', 'Show the kit price and the installed scope in separate columns so customers compare the same building.', 'Customers often compare a kit price against an installed bid and miss footings, concrete, insulation, and erection labor. This course covers presenting kit and installed options side by side, explaining what the kit leaves out, and writing door, trim, and insulation options into the proposal. Warranty and engineering terms vary by supplier; state them in writing.', 'intermediate', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'cyan', false, 20, array['Presenting kit and installed options side by side', 'Explaining what a kit leaves out', 'Door, trim and insulation options', 'Handling the ''kit price'' comparison', 'Writing proposals with engineering and permit lines']::text[], 'Presenting Kit and Installed Pole Barn Quotes Side by Side', 'Show the kit price and the installed scope in separate columns so customers compare the same building.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:pole-barns-estimating')::uuid, 'pole-barns-estimating', 'pole-barns', 'estimating', 'Pole Barn Estimates: Posts, Trusses, Purlins, Panels and Doors', 'Price posts, trusses, purlins, metal panels, trim, doors and footings by system, with erection labor shown separately.', 'Pole barn estimates build from post count and depth, trusses and purlins, metal panel area, trim, and doors, then add footings, concrete, and erection labor. Wind and snow loads from the engineered design affect post size and spacing. This course covers takeoffs by system, footing and concrete quantities, and pricing for doors, trim, and erection.', 'intermediate', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'navy', false, 30, array['Post count, depth and footing takeoffs', 'Truss and purlin quantities from design', 'Metal panel area and waste', 'Door, trim and accessory pricing', 'Erection labor and crane or lift pricing']::text[], null, 'Price posts, trusses, purlins, metal panels, trim, doors and footings by system, with erection labor shown separately.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:pole-barns-project-management')::uuid, 'pole-barns-project-management', 'pole-barns', 'project_management', 'Sequencing Post-Frame Erection Around Footings, Weather and Lifts', 'Plan footings, post setting, truss erection, panel install and door hang around weather and lift access.', 'Post-frame erection starts with footings and post setting, then trusses, purlins, and panels, and high-wind or wet days stop the crew. This course covers scheduling footings and concrete cure before erection, planning truss and lift days, and sequencing panel and door installs. Inspection and engineering requirements vary by locality; confirm them before erection.', 'intermediate', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'green', false, 40, array['Footing layout and concrete cure timing', 'Post setting and bracing sequence', 'Truss and purlin erection days', 'Panel install and weather planning', 'Door hang and final inspection']::text[], null, 'Plan footings, post setting, truss erection, panel install and door hang around weather and lift access.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:pole-barns-accounting')::uuid, 'pole-barns-accounting', 'pole-barns', 'accounting', 'Pole Barn Job Costing: Materials, Lift Rental and Erection Hours', 'Track materials, lift rental and erection hours per building so you can compare each job to its bid.', 'Pole barn margins depend on material deliveries, lift rental days, and erection hours that run long on large spans. This course covers tracking materials and deliveries against the takeoff, recording lift rental and crew hours, and billing change orders for site conditions and design revisions. Tax treatment of materials and rentals varies by state; confirm details with your accountant.', 'intermediate', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'amber', false, 50, array['Tracking materials and deliveries by job', 'Lift rental costs and days', 'Erection hours by span and bay', 'Billing site and design change orders', 'Deposits and progress billing for buildings']::text[], null, 'Track materials, lift rental and erection hours per building so you can compare each job to its bid.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:pole-barns-hr')::uuid, 'pole-barns-hr', 'pole-barns', 'hr', 'Training Post-Frame Erection Crews for Trusses, Panels and Lifts', 'Build erection crews who set posts plumb, handle trusses safely and install panels square and straight.', 'Post-frame erection depends on plumb posts, truss handling, and square panel installs, and crews need to work at height. This course covers hiring erection crew members, training on post setting and truss handling, and quality checks for square and plumb framing. Wage, classification, and overtime rules vary by state; confirm them with your accountant.', 'beginner', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'rose', false, 60, array['Hiring erection crew members', 'Post setting plumb and in line', 'Truss handling and bracing', 'Panel install square and straight', 'Keeping erection crews through the season']::text[], null, 'Build erection crews who set posts plumb, handle trusses safely and install panels square and straight.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:pole-barns-growth')::uuid, 'pole-barns-growth', 'pole-barns', 'growth', 'Repeat Pole Barn Work from Farms, Shops and Repeat Builders', 'Build repeat work from farm and shop owners who expand, plus builders and dealers who refer projects.', 'Pole barn customers often return for additional buildings, storage, and doors, and dealers and builders refer work. This course covers relationships with farms and shops, follow-up after erection, and referral programs with dealers and suppliers. Marketing and solicitation rules vary by locality; confirm terms before offering referral incentives.', 'intermediate', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'cyan', false, 70, array['Follow-up with farm and shop owners', 'Expansion projects for past customers', 'Relationships with dealers and suppliers', 'Door and accessory add-on service', 'Referrals from finished buildings']::text[], 'Repeat Pole Barn Work from Farms, Shops and Repeat Builders', 'Build repeat work from farm and shop owners who expand, plus builders and dealers who refer projects.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:pole-barns-safety')::uuid, 'pole-barns-safety', 'pole-barns', 'safety', 'Pole Barn Safety: Erection at Height, Overhead Power and Wind', 'Manage erection fall exposure, overhead power line clearance and wind risks during truss and panel work.', 'Pole barn erection puts crews at height on trusses and panels, often near overhead power and in changing wind. This course covers fall protection during erection, overhead power line clearance for lifts and metal panels, and wind limits for truss and panel work. Fall protection, lift, and power line rules vary by state and locality; confirm the requirements that apply to your jobs.', 'advanced', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'slate', false, 80, array['Fall protection during erection', 'Overhead power line clearance for lifts', 'Wind limits for truss and panel work', 'Temporary bracing until purlins are set', 'Lift operation and rigging safety']::text[], null, 'Manage erection fall exposure, overhead power line clearance and wind risks during truss and panel work.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:commercial-remodeling-getting-started')::uuid, 'commercial-remodeling-getting-started', 'commercial-remodeling', 'getting_started', 'Commercial Remodeling Business: Bonding and Licensing', 'Business basics for a commercial remodeling company, including licensing, bonding, insurance and prequalification.', 'Commercial remodeling often requires bonds, higher insurance limits, and prequalification before owners will award work. This course covers business setup, licensing and registration for commercial work, bonding and insurance requirements, and building a prequalification package. Bonding, insurance, and licensing rules vary by state and locality; confirm them with your licensing board, surety, and insurance agent.', 'beginner', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'slate', false, 10, array['Entity setup and tax registration basics', 'Licensing and registration for commercial work', 'Bonding and surety relationships', 'Insurance limits commercial owners require', 'Building a prequalification package']::text[], 'Commercial Remodeling Business: Bonding and Licensing', 'Business basics for a commercial remodeling company, including licensing, bonding, insurance and prequalification.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:commercial-remodeling-sales')::uuid, 'commercial-remodeling-sales', 'commercial-remodeling', 'sales', 'Bidding Tenant Improvements and Presenting General Conditions', 'Present the scope by division and explain general conditions and fees so the owner can check the total line by line.', 'Commercial owners often compare bids by total and question general conditions and fees they do not understand. This course covers organizing bids by division, explaining general conditions such as supervision and temporary facilities, and presenting fees and allowances in a clear form. Bid form requirements vary by owner; follow the instructions in each invitation.', 'intermediate', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'cyan', false, 20, array['Organizing bids by division', 'Explaining general conditions to owners', 'Presenting fees and allowances clearly', 'Following owner bid form requirements', 'Handling clarification questions after bid']::text[], null, 'Present the scope by division and explain general conditions and fees so the owner can check the total line by line.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:commercial-remodeling-estimating')::uuid, 'commercial-remodeling-estimating', 'commercial-remodeling', 'estimating', 'Commercial Estimates: Divisions, Subcontractors and General Conditions', 'Build a commercial estimate by division with self-performed scope, sub bids, general conditions and fees shown separately.', 'Commercial estimates combine self-performed work, subcontractor bids, general conditions, and fees across many divisions. Missing subcontractor scope or undercounted general conditions can erase the margin on a large bid. This course covers division takeoffs, sub bid leveling, general conditions budgeting, and fee and contingency setup.', 'advanced', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'navy', false, 30, array['Division takeoffs and scope lists', 'Leveling subcontractor bids', 'Budgeting general conditions by duration', 'Setting fees and contingency', 'Allowances and unit prices for owners']::text[], null, 'Build a commercial estimate by division with self-performed scope, sub bids, general conditions and fees shown separately.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:commercial-remodeling-project-management')::uuid, 'commercial-remodeling-project-management', 'commercial-remodeling', 'project_management', 'Scheduling Tenant Work Around Owner Hours, Inspections and Deliveries', 'Plan tenant improvement work around owner and building hours, inspection holds and long-lead equipment deliveries.', 'Commercial work often has to happen after hours or on weekends to avoid disrupting tenants, and inspections and deliveries have their own timing. This course covers building a schedule around owner and building hours, planning inspection holds, and tracking long-lead equipment and fixtures. Owner schedule and inspection rules vary by project and locality; confirm them in the contract.', 'advanced', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'green', false, 40, array['Scheduling around owner and building hours', 'Inspection holds and sequence', 'Long-lead equipment and fixture tracking', 'Subcontractor coordination on a shared schedule', 'Schedule updates and owner reporting']::text[], null, 'Plan tenant improvement work around owner and building hours, inspection holds and long-lead equipment deliveries.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:commercial-remodeling-accounting')::uuid, 'commercial-remodeling-accounting', 'commercial-remodeling', 'accounting', 'Commercial Job Costing: Sub Billing, Retainage and Change Orders', 'Track subcontractor billing, retainage and change orders so the project financials match the contract.', 'Commercial projects involve progress billing, subcontractor pay applications, and retainage that ties up cash until closeout. This course covers tracking sub pay applications against the contract, managing retainage on both sides, and documenting change orders promptly. Retainage and payment rules vary by state and contract; confirm terms with your accountant and attorney.', 'advanced', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'amber', false, 50, array['Tracking sub pay applications', 'Retainage on owner and sub contracts', 'Documenting change orders promptly', 'Cash flow planning for long projects', 'Closeout financials and lien waiver tracking']::text[], null, 'Track subcontractor billing, retainage and change orders so the project financials match the contract.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:commercial-remodeling-hr')::uuid, 'commercial-remodeling-hr', 'commercial-remodeling', 'hr', 'Building Supervision and Trade Crews for Commercial Projects', 'Hire superintendents, foremen and trade crews who can manage tenant schedules, documentation and quality standards.', 'Commercial projects need superintendents and foremen who manage schedules, documentation, and quality across many trades. This course covers hiring and developing superintendents and foremen, defining roles for self-performed work and sub oversight, and setting documentation standards. Supervisor, wage, and classification rules vary by state; confirm them with your accountant and employment counsel.', 'intermediate', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'rose', false, 60, array['Hiring superintendents and foremen', 'Defining self-performed and sub oversight roles', 'Documentation standards for daily logs', 'Training crews on owner and building rules', 'Retaining supervisors through the pipeline']::text[], 'Building Supervision and Trade Crews for Commercial Projects', 'Hire superintendents, foremen and trade crews who can manage tenant schedules, documentation and quality standards.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:commercial-remodeling-growth')::uuid, 'commercial-remodeling-growth', 'commercial-remodeling', 'growth', 'Repeat Commercial Work from Owners, Property Managers and Tenants', 'Build repeat commercial work from owners and property managers, plus tenant buildouts that lead to the next space.', 'Commercial remodeling repeats with property managers who run multiple buildings and tenants who take on additional spaces. This course covers building relationships with owners and property managers, following up after closeout, and pursuing bids for repeat tenant work. Bid, marketing, and qualification rules vary by owner and locality.', 'intermediate', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'cyan', false, 70, array['Relationships with property managers', 'Follow-up after closeout and warranty', 'Pursuing repeat tenant buildouts', 'Prequalification updates for repeat owners', 'Tracking owner and tenant pipeline']::text[], null, 'Build repeat commercial work from owners and property managers, plus tenant buildouts that lead to the next space.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:commercial-remodeling-safety')::uuid, 'commercial-remodeling-safety', 'commercial-remodeling', 'safety', 'Commercial Site Safety: Occupied Buildings and Public Access', 'Protect tenants and the public during commercial work, coordinate safety with multiple subs and manage site access.', 'Commercial remodels happen in occupied buildings where tenants, visitors, and staff share hallways and exits with crews. This course covers protecting the public during work, coordinating safety among many subs, and controlling site access and egress. Building, egress, and site safety rules vary by state and locality; confirm the requirements that apply to each project.', 'advanced', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'slate', false, 80, array['Protecting tenants and public during work', 'Coordinating safety among many subs', 'Site access and egress control', 'Fire protection and hot work permits', 'Documenting safety and incident reporting']::text[], 'Commercial Site Safety: Occupied Buildings and Public Access', 'Protect tenants and the public during commercial work, coordinate safety with multiple subs and manage site access.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:general-contracting-getting-started')::uuid, 'general-contracting-getting-started', 'general-contracting', 'getting_started', 'Setting Up a GC Business: Licensing, Bonding and Insurance', 'Business basics for a general contracting company, including licensing, bonding, liability coverage and sub requirements.', 'General contractors are responsible for the whole project, including the subs they hire, and owners often require licensing, bonds, and proof of insurance. This course covers business setup, licensing and registration, bonding and liability coverage, and the insurance certificates subs and owners request. Licensing and bonding rules vary by state and locality; confirm them with your licensing board.', 'beginner', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'slate', false, 10, array['Entity setup and tax registration basics', 'Licensing and registration for GC work', 'Bonding and liability coverage', 'Insurance certificates for subs and owners', 'Choosing residential, commercial or both']::text[], 'Setting Up a GC Business: Licensing, Bonding and Insurance', 'Business basics for a general contracting company, including licensing, bonding, liability coverage and sub requirements.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:general-contracting-sales')::uuid, 'general-contracting-sales', 'general-contracting', 'sales', 'Presenting GC Proposals with the Right Level of Detail', 'Choose how much scope detail to show, from summary to line by line, and explain fees and allowances clearly.', 'Owners vary in how much detail they want, and a proposal that is too thin or too thick can lose the job. This course covers choosing the right level of detail, presenting sub quotes and allowances, and explaining fees such as overhead and profit in plain terms. Contract and fee terms vary by project and state; state them in writing.', 'intermediate', 'public', 'published', 'mixed', 'cyan', false, 20, array['Choosing summary or line-item detail', 'Presenting sub quotes and allowances', 'Explaining overhead and profit', 'Handling the ''why does a GC cost more'' question', 'Writing proposals with clear exclusions']::text[], 'Presenting GC Proposals with the Right Level of Detail', 'Choose how much scope detail to show, from summary to line by line, and explain fees and allowances clearly.', now()),
  (md5('academy:course:general-contracting-estimating')::uuid, 'general-contracting-estimating', 'general-contracting', 'estimating', 'GC Estimates: Your Labor, Sub Quotes, Allowances and Fees', 'Build a general contracting estimate from your own labor, leveled sub quotes, allowances and fees, each shown separately.', 'General contracting estimates combine your self-performed labor, subcontractor quotes, allowances, and fees, and gaps between quotes are a common source of loss. This course covers leveling sub quotes against the same scope, setting allowances for owner selections, and building overhead and profit into the price. Pricing decisions are yours; verify subcontractor scope before you bid.', 'advanced', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'navy', false, 30, array['Leveling sub quotes to the same scope', 'Self-performed labor takeoffs', 'Setting allowances for owner selections', 'Overhead, profit and contingency', 'Identifying scope gaps between trades']::text[], 'GC Estimates: Your Labor, Sub Quotes, Allowances and Fees', 'Build a general contracting estimate from your own labor, leveled sub quotes, allowances and fees, each shown separately.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:general-contracting-project-management')::uuid, 'general-contracting-project-management', 'general-contracting', 'project_management', 'Managing Subcontractors, Schedules and Owner Communication', 'Coordinate subs on a shared schedule, track their start dates and keep the owner informed of progress and changes.', 'A general contractor''s margin depends on sub coordination, and a late sub can delay every trade behind it. This course covers building a master schedule, sub start-date commitments, weekly coordination meetings, and owner updates that show progress and changes. Contract schedule and notice requirements vary by state and project; confirm them in the agreement.', 'advanced', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'green', false, 40, array['Building a master schedule with subs', 'Sub start-date commitments and buffers', 'Weekly coordination meeting agenda', 'Owner progress reports and change notices', 'Managing delays and schedule recovery']::text[], 'Managing Subcontractors, Schedules and Owner Communication', 'Coordinate subs on a shared schedule, track their start dates and keep the owner informed of progress and changes.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:general-contracting-accounting')::uuid, 'general-contracting-accounting', 'general-contracting', 'accounting', 'GC Job Costing: Sub Payments, Draws and Change Orders', 'Track sub payments, owner draws and change orders so the project''s cash position and margin stay clear.', 'General contractors carry cash risk when they pay subs before owners pay them, and unrecorded change orders erode margin. This course covers tracking sub contracts and pay applications, managing owner draw schedules, and documenting change orders as they occur. Lien waiver, payment, and retainage rules vary by state; confirm details with your accountant and attorney.', 'advanced', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'amber', false, 50, array['Tracking sub contracts and pay applications', 'Owner draw schedules and cash position', 'Documenting change orders as they occur', 'Lien waiver collection and tracking', 'Closeout financials and margin review']::text[], 'GC Job Costing: Sub Payments, Draws and Change Orders', 'Track sub payments, owner draws and change orders so the project''s cash position and margin stay clear.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:general-contracting-hr')::uuid, 'general-contracting-hr', 'general-contracting', 'hr', 'Building a Core Team of Supervisors and Carpenters', 'Hire a superintendent or lead carpenter and a core crew you can rely on, then manage the sub roster around them.', 'General contractors rely on a core team of supervisors and carpenters, with subs filling in as needed. This course covers hiring a superintendent or lead carpenter, building a core crew, and managing a sub roster with clear performance expectations. Wage, classification, and independent contractor rules vary by state; confirm them with your accountant and employment counsel.', 'intermediate', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'rose', false, 60, array['Hiring a superintendent or lead carpenter', 'Core crew roles and responsibilities', 'Managing a sub roster and performance', 'Independent contractor versus employee rules', 'Keeping the core team through slow periods']::text[], 'Building a Core Team of Supervisors and Carpenters', 'Hire a superintendent or lead carpenter and a core crew you can rely on, then manage the sub roster around them.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:general-contracting-growth')::uuid, 'general-contracting-growth', 'general-contracting', 'growth', 'Repeat Work from Owners, Designers and Repeat Subs', 'Earn repeat work from owners and designers, and build a reliable sub roster that wants to work with you again.', 'General contracting repeats with owners who renovate again, designers who specify builders, and subs who want steady work. This course covers follow-up after closeout, building designer and developer relationships, and paying subs on time to keep reliable crews on your roster. Marketing, bidding, and contract rules vary by locality.', 'intermediate', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'cyan', false, 70, array['Follow-up after closeout and warranty', 'Relationships with designers and developers', 'Keeping a reliable sub roster', 'Referrals from past owners', 'Tracking repeat clients and their projects']::text[], 'Repeat Work from Owners, Designers and Repeat Subs', 'Earn repeat work from owners and designers, and build a reliable sub roster that wants to work with you again.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:general-contracting-safety')::uuid, 'general-contracting-safety', 'general-contracting', 'safety', 'GC Site Safety: Coordinating Subs, Job Hazards and Documentation', 'Coordinate safety among subs, manage shared site hazards and document safety training and inspections.', 'A general contractor is responsible for jobsite conditions that affect every trade, from fall protection to shared access and housekeeping. This course covers site-wide safety planning, coordinating subs on hazards and access, and documenting training and inspections. Safety responsibilities, contract obligations, and inspection rules vary by state and locality; confirm the requirements that apply to your projects.', 'advanced', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'slate', false, 80, array['Site-wide safety planning with subs', 'Shared access and housekeeping rules', 'Fall protection and edge coordination', 'Documenting training and inspections', 'Incident reporting and follow-up']::text[], null, 'Coordinate safety among subs, manage shared site hazards and document safety training and inspections.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:handyman-getting-started')::uuid, 'handyman-getting-started', 'handyman', 'getting_started', 'Starting a Handyman Business: Licensing, Insurance and Scope Limits', 'Business basics for a handyman business, including licensing limits, liability insurance and which trades you avoid.', 'Handyman work spans many trades, and some tasks such as electrical or plumbing changes require licensed trades. This course covers business setup, licensing limits on what a handyman can perform, liability insurance for in-home work, and setting a clear list of tasks you do and do not take. Licensing and scope rules vary by state and locality; confirm them with your licensing board.', 'beginner', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'slate', false, 10, array['Entity setup and tax registration basics', 'Licensing limits on trade work', 'Liability insurance for in-home work', 'Defining the tasks you do and decline', 'Setting a service area and trip radius']::text[], null, 'Business basics for a handyman business, including licensing limits, liability insurance and which trades you avoid.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:handyman-sales')::uuid, 'handyman-sales', 'handyman', 'sales', 'Quoting Small Jobs Clearly Over the Phone and On Site', 'Give quick task prices, state minimums and trip charges, and know when a job needs an on-site look first.', 'Homeowners often want a price over the phone for several small repairs and expect one low number. This course covers quoting by task with minimums and trip charges, writing short estimates that list each task, and knowing when a job needs an on-site look before a firm price. Warranty terms and service agreements should be stated in writing.', 'beginner', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'cyan', false, 20, array['Quoting by task with minimums', 'Trip charges and service area fees', 'Phone quotes versus on-site estimates', 'Writing short estimates that list tasks', 'Handling a long to-do list from one call']::text[], 'Quoting Small Jobs Clearly Over the Phone and On Site', 'Give quick task prices, state minimums and trip charges, and know when a job needs an on-site look first.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:handyman-estimating')::uuid, 'handyman-estimating', 'handyman', 'estimating', 'Handyman Pricing: Hourly, Per-Task, Materials and Trip Charges', 'Set hourly and per-task rates, add materials with markup and include trip charges so small jobs still pay.', 'Handyman pricing blends hourly labor, per-task rates, materials, and trip charges, and small jobs can lose money without minimums. This course covers setting hourly and task rates, adding materials and markup clearly, and building trip charges and minimum job fees. Pricing decisions are yours; check local rules on any advertised rates.', 'intermediate', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'navy', false, 30, array['Setting hourly and per-task rates', 'Materials, markup and receipts', 'Trip charges and minimum job fees', 'Quoting multi-task visits', 'Reviewing pricing against actual time']::text[], null, 'Set hourly and per-task rates, add materials with markup and include trip charges so small jobs still pay.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:handyman-project-management')::uuid, 'handyman-project-management', 'handyman', 'project_management', 'Routing and Scheduling a Week of Small Repair Calls', 'Group calls by neighborhood, plan parts runs and keep the day full without overbooking one-person work.', 'Handyman days depend on how calls are grouped, how parts runs fit in, and how many tasks one person can finish safely. This course covers routing calls by neighborhood, planning supply runs, and setting realistic time windows so the day stays on track. Customer notice and access rules vary by locality and building type.', 'beginner', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'green', false, 40, array['Grouping calls by neighborhood', 'Parts runs and supply planning', 'Realistic time windows per task', 'Confirming access and key arrangements', 'Handling reschedules and no-shows']::text[], 'Routing and Scheduling a Week of Small Repair Calls', 'Group calls by neighborhood, plan parts runs and keep the day full without overbooking one-person work.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:handyman-accounting')::uuid, 'handyman-accounting', 'handyman', 'accounting', 'Handyman Job Costing: Materials, Time and Callbacks', 'Track materials, labor time and callbacks per job so you can see which services earn their time.', 'Handyman margins erode with unbilled materials, time spent on small tasks that add up, and callbacks that go unpaid. This course covers tracking materials and time by task, recording callbacks, and reviewing which services earn their time. Tax treatment of supplies and vehicle costs varies by state; confirm details with your accountant.', 'intermediate', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'amber', false, 50, array['Tracking materials and receipts by job', 'Recording time by task type', 'Vehicle and tool cost allocation', 'Callback policy and unpaid return visits', 'Reviewing which services earn their time']::text[], 'Handyman Job Costing: Materials, Time and Callbacks', 'Track materials, labor time and callbacks per job so you can see which services earn their time.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:handyman-hr')::uuid, 'handyman-hr', 'handyman', 'hr', 'Adding Helpers to a Handyman Business', 'Decide when to add a helper, train them for common repairs and set expectations for work quality and customer care.', 'Handyman businesses grow when the owner can hand off routine tasks to a trained helper. This course covers deciding when to hire a helper, training on common repairs and customer etiquette, and setting quality and conduct expectations. Wage, classification, and vehicle and driving rules vary by state; confirm them with your accountant.', 'beginner', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'rose', false, 60, array['Deciding when to add a helper', 'Training on common repairs', 'Customer etiquette in homes', 'Classification of helpers and contractors', 'Quality and conduct expectations']::text[], 'Adding Helpers to a Handyman Business', 'Decide when to add a helper, train them for common repairs and set expectations for work quality and customer care.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:handyman-growth')::uuid, 'handyman-growth', 'handyman', 'growth', 'Repeat Handyman Work from Homeowners and Property Managers', 'Turn one-time fixes into recurring service with property managers, home-sale punch lists and seasonal maintenance visits.', 'Handyman customers often return for the next repair, and property managers and real estate agents need steady work. This course covers building property manager accounts, offering seasonal maintenance visits, and marketing punch-list services for home sales. Marketing, advertising, and solicitation rules vary by locality; confirm them before promoting services.', 'intermediate', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'cyan', false, 70, array['Property manager accounts and priority service', 'Seasonal maintenance visit offers', 'Punch-list service for home sales', 'Referrals from real estate agents', 'Reminders and rebooking for past clients']::text[], 'Repeat Handyman Work from Homeowners and Property Managers', 'Turn one-time fixes into recurring service with property managers, home-sale punch lists and seasonal maintenance visits.', null),
  (md5('academy:course:handyman-safety')::uuid, 'handyman-safety', 'handyman', 'safety', 'Handyman Safety: Ladders, Power Tools and Working in Occupied Homes', 'Use ladders and power tools safely, avoid hazards in occupied homes and know when to stop and refer work.', 'Handyman work involves ladders, power tools, and tasks in homes with children, pets, and occupants who may be affected. This course covers ladder setup and three-point contact, power tool guards and cord safety, and recognizing when a task belongs to a licensed trade. Ladder, tool, and trade licensing rules vary by state and locality; confirm the requirements that apply to your work.', 'advanced', 'public', 'upcoming', 'original', 'slate', false, 80, array['Ladder setup and three-point contact', 'Power tool guards and cord safety', 'Recognizing tasks for licensed trades', 'Protecting occupants and pets during work', 'Lifting and moving heavy items safely']::text[], null, 'Use ladders and power tools safely, avoid hazards in occupied homes and know when to stop and refer work.', null)
